  {"a":"gwen","b":"aatrox","win":["Gwen","Skill","Aatrox","Aatrox","Gwen","Skill","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Both of you are limp here — Aatrox's first Q sweetspot is slow and easy to sidestep, and your Snip Snip! cone is short with a wind-up, so it is a pure last-hit fight with no kill threat either way."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Aatrox's R (World Ender) gives him bonus AD, healing and move speed, turning his Q1-Q2-Q3 sweetspot chain into his hardest all-in; eat the third knockup under R and you likely die, so save W to break it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Aatrox's Eclipse/Profane Hydra spike lands before your Nashor's-into-Riftmaker comes fully online, and his R-healing plus Hydra drain out-sustains your Q poke in the extended trades he forces."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Riftmaker omnivamp/true damage plus A Thousand Cuts %-max-HP magic chews through the bruiser HP he stacks faster than his R-window heal can refund it — this is where you flip the lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold Hallowed Mist for his all-in, then drop it as his third sweetspot Q or his R commits so the follow-up swing whiffs and you keep snipping untargetable from inside the fog","Survive his Eclipse/Profane Hydra spike, farm at the cone tip, and reach Nashor's into Riftmaker, where %-max-HP Q out-grinds his drain","Spend E's dash and on-champ cooldown refund to break his W chain-pull and disengage the trade, not to chase him into his sword zone"],"foe":["Chain Q1-Q2-Q3 sweetspots into a Deathbringer Stance auto reset — that empowered swing heals him and stat-checks you","Catch you with W (Infernal Chains) to drag you back into his minions and dropped-sword zone for a trade you can't walk out of","Hit 6 and pop R into a committed all-in where his bonus AD, move speed and active healing out-sustain your trade damage"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are a coin flip — Aatrox is just as weak early as you are, with a slow, dodgeable first Q sweetspot and no real burst until he chains all three casts. Last-hit at the cone tip and never walk up for a Q he can punish: the sweetspot knockup feeds his Deathbringer Stance auto reset, which heals him. Respect his W (Infernal Chains, 20s at rank 1): if the ring lands and you stay inside it he yanks you back toward his sword zone, so step out of the circle before it detonates. Neither of you wins a clean all-in yet, so trade Q tips, dodge his sweetspots, and farm.","mid":"This is his window. From level 3 his Q1-Q2-Q3 sweetspot chain plus a W pull out-stats you before your kit and items come online, and at 6 his R adds AD, healing and move speed that out-drain your trade damage in any extended fight. Your one out is Hallowed Mist — bait the all-in, then drop the fog the instant his third Q or his R commits so the follow-up swings whiff and you snip from untargetable. Never duel him in the open while his W and R are up; let his R timer burn, farm with E resets, and concede a plate over feeding a chained combo.","late":"At two-plus items you take the lane back. Aatrox is a drain-bruiser who stacks HP, and that is exactly what A Thousand Cuts and percent-max-HP Snip Snip! were built to punish — the bigger his bar, the harder your magic Q lands and the more your abilities heal you. With Nashor's into Riftmaker online and Mist for the all-in, you out-grind him because his R-window healing and Hydra drain can't keep pace with %-max-HP plus your true-damage center snip and Riftmaker conversion. Anti-heal (Morellonomicon) seals it: cut his sustain and the extended trade he wanted becomes the trade you win.","whys":["You are both miserable at level 1 — his first sweetspot Q is slow and dodgeable and your cone Q has a wind-up, so it is a skill last-hit fight with no kill pressure either way.","Still even at 2 — neither of you has a committed combo online, so contest the wave, step out of his W ring before it pulls, and don't force a trade.","From 3 his Q1-Q2-Q3 sweetspot chain plus a W pull out-stats you, and you have no Hallowed Mist yet to nullify the engage.","Levels 4-5 are his window — Umbral Dash heals him mid-combo on a 9s rank-1 cooldown, so his chained knockups out-trade you even with Mist up.","World Ender's 120s rank-1 cooldown buys him AD, healing and move speed, so his all-in out-sustains your poke unless Mist lands on the commit.","His Eclipse/Profane Hydra spike lands before your Nashor's-into-Riftmaker — buy Executioner's Calling early so his drain stops out-grinding you.","At two-plus items your %-max-HP Q plus Thousand Cuts shred the bruiser HP he stacks faster than his R-window heal can refund, and Morellonomicon anti-heal cuts his sustain for good."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"akali","win":["Skill","Akali","Akali","Skill","Skill","Akali","Akali"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Stack Snip Snip! on the wave and tag her with the true-damage center snip if she creeps up to last-hit — neither of you wants the level 1-2 fight, so farm even, track her energy bar, and watch how she contests the first waves."},{"when":"Lvl 4-6","text":"Her best window: she pokes with Q shuriken from outside your cone, then commits E-mark into Q-AA the instant your Hallowed Mist is on cooldown — hold Mist for the all-in instead of bleeding it on poke, and farm at max snip range."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's flips it — %-HP Snip plus Skip 'n Slash resets let you win the extended duel; she can W into Twilight Shroud to drop targeting, so stand on top of her in melee and keep auto-snipping through the cloud."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Akali scales hard — past two items her R two-cast dash plus item burst can delete you between Mist windows, so close the lane at your spike rather than gambling on the very late 1v1."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait out her Twilight Shroud, then stand inside it in melee with Mist down so her invis means nothing while your autos and %-HP Snip grind her squishy frame","Hit your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike and force the extended duel — A Thousand Cuts healing plus %-HP Q out-sustains her once she has dumped her E-Q burst","Hold Hallowed Mist for her all-in, not her poke, and keep Skip 'n Slash up to dash out of her R execute window"],"foe":["Poke with Q shuriken from range, then E-mark in for the Q-AA burst the moment your Mist or E is on cooldown","Use Twilight Shroud to break your targeting, sidestep your cone, and reset poke from inside the invis cloud","Avoid the extended brawl — burst with R's two casts, dash out, and scale to her two-item assassin spike"]},"early":"Neither of you wants the level 1-2 fight here — she has energy and a Q shuriken poke pattern but no shroud yet, and you are a clunky cone with Mist on a 22s cooldown, so stack Snip Snip! on the wave and tag her with the true-damage center snip if she creeps into melee to last-hit. With Q+E at three you can poke-and-reset, but her Q out-ranges your cone, so never chase a snip she can sidestep. Her burst opens on an Assassin's Mark auto reset — that wind-up is your cue to step back, not the E cast. Track her energy and do not fall behind.","mid":"This is her window, not yours. She pokes with Q shuriken from outside your cone, then E-marks in for the Q-AA burst the instant your Hallowed Mist is on cooldown — hold Mist for her all-in instead of bleeding it on trades, and farm at max snip range. At 6 you have the full kit, but Shuriken Flip is 16s at rank 1 against your 22s Mist, so she gets more entries than you get answers; commit only when Twilight Shroud is down and Skip 'n Slash is up to dash out of her reset. Bank CS, dodge the empowered Q, survive to your item.","late":"Once Riftmaker (or Nashor's into Riftmaker) completes, the lane flips to you — %-HP Snip plus Hallowed Mist wins the extended duel, and standing on top of her in melee means Twilight Shroud only breaks targeting while you keep auto-snipping and healing off the damage through the cloud. Skip 'n Slash refunds part of its cooldown on every champion hit, so you can chase her dashes. Force every fight on her 20s shroud. But Akali scales too: past two items her item burst and R execute window can blow you up between Mist drops, so close it out at your spike rather than gambling on the very late 1v1.","whys":["Neither of you has a fight button yet — stack snips on the wave, land the true-damage center, and watch how Akali contests the first waves with her energy bar.","She can poke with Q shuriken but has no shroud yet and your Mist is a 22s cooldown at rank 1 — it stays even, so trade only when her energy is dry.","Your Q+E pattern comes online, but her Q out-ranges your cone and she can sidestep the snip — contest CS, do not chase a poke she dodges.","Her window: she pokes with Q, then E-marks in for Q-AA burst the moment your Hallowed Mist is down — hold Mist for the all-in and farm safe.","At 6 her R two-cast dash can execute you before Mist matters — all-in only when Twilight Shroud is down and Skip 'n Slash is up to dash out.","Riftmaker online — %-HP Snip plus Mist win the extended duel; stand on her in melee so the Shroud only briefly breaks your targeting while you keep snipping.","At two items you shred her squishy frame and out-sustain with A Thousand Cuts healing — force the brawl on her 20s shroud before her own scaling reclaims the very late game."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"akshan","win":["Akshan","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Akshan","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Akshan's thinnest window — Heroic Swing is 18s at rank 1, so once he spends it he cannot kite far: step up with a Q snip into an E on-hit and reset out before his Avengerang poke adds up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"R Comeuppance plus passive camouflage off a wall lets him line up the execute the instant your W mist drops or you step to CS — his hardest punish window, not yours."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike lets you tank an extended trade, but his Avengerang chip and Heroic Swing still reset the gap before your %-HP Snip Snip lands."},{"when":"Late","text":"At 2+ items your true-damage Q center-snip and passive on-hit healing out-grind his squishy frame in any fight he can't swing out of — force a sidelane 1v1 with no wall to grapple off."}],"wants":{"you":["Punish the 18s window right after he spends Heroic Swing — Q snip into E on-hit, then back before Avengerang chip stacks","Drop W mist on top of him so he can't poke you out, then close for a %-HP Snip Snip all-in","Scale to 2+ items and force narrow sidelane fights with no wall for him to Heroic Swing to safety"],"foe":["Kite with Heroic Swing and chip you down with Avengerang poke before you ever reach mist range","Hold R Comeuppance plus brush camouflage to execute you the instant your W drops or you over-extend","Roam off his swing mobility and revive a dead ally to snowball the map while you're stuck farming"]},"early":"Akshan is one of the few ranged tops with an actually weak early — Heroic Swing is an 18s cooldown at rank 1, so the moment he spends it he cannot kite far and that is your cleanest window. Step up with a Q snip and E in for a quick on-hit before he can chip you with Avengerang, then back out — your passive %-HP autos chunk even his low HP bar fast. The rest of the time he grapples over a wall whenever you commit, his Avengerang out-ranges everything you have, and Hallowed Mist only shields you from enemies outside it — which is a kiter's whole plan, so the mist buys almost nothing. Last-hit safe and accept you are behind until two items.","mid":"This is his window, not yours — that's the honest read. Your W Hallowed Mist gives armor/MR and untargetability, but Akshan never has to walk into it: he sits at Avengerang range and chips you while your mist sits empty. At 6, R Comeuppance plus passive camouflage off a brush or wall means the second your mist drops or you step to CS, he can channel the execute. There's nothing to bait here because he never all-ins — so just deny the easy poke: hug your mist's edge for the resist when the boomerang comes, hold E to dash out of a Swing engage rather than chasing it, and ping your jungler every time he leaves to go revive a teammate.","late":"Late is where you reclaim it. Akshan is a squishy ranged skirmisher, and once you have 2+ items your true-damage center Snip Snip and the on-hit healing off your passive grind him out of any fight he can't kite. Your win condition is a narrow sidelane 1v1 with no wall to Heroic Swing off and no ally nearby to revive — drop W to deny his R Comeuppance line, E-dash onto him, and Snip Snip deletes a target with no HP to hide behind. In a teamfight, catch him after he's burned his Swing charge. He out-ranges you all game, so the whole match is surviving to the point where one clean gap-close ends him.","whys":["Both of you are soft at level 1, and Akshan has no Swing mobility yet either, so it's a true coin-flip on who lands the first auto and trade.","He starts grappling your Q-E poke over walls with Heroic Swing, and your E cooldown refund means nothing if you cannot touch him to trigger it.","Avengerang's 850 range beats your 450 cone, and Hallowed Mist is dead value against a kiter who never walks into it — free chip every wave.","Levels 4-5 are your worst stretch — a melee with no mist yet against a ranged kiter who now swings freely and out-trades every step-up.","At 6 his R Comeuppance plus camo execute beats your all-in — he punishes the instant your W drops, where most melee would be forced into a mist duel.","His first-item Avengerang chip and Swing mobility still let him poke and escape before your Riftmaker %-HP Snip can close the gap.","At 2+ items your true-damage center Snip Snip and passive healing out-grind his squishy frame in any sidelane 1v1 he can't swing out of — force the fight where there's no wall to grapple off."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"ambessa","win":["Skill","Gwen","Skill","Gwen","Ambessa","Ambessa","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Snip Snip! cone chips her, but her Cunning Sweep edge deals max-HP damage and converts into Sundering Slam on hit, and her Drakehound's Step lets her dash an empowered auto onto you mid-combo — trade only when Skip 'n Slash is up to dash out before the slam lands."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her threat window: Public Execution dashes behind you and suppresses into a stun, and her Lacerate slow keeps you pinned for the follow-up — if your W isn't already down she catches you in the open, so hold Hallowed Mist for the instant she ults."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Ambessa's Eclipse plus her level-9 Q max lets Cunning-Sweep-into-Sundering-Slam chunk you before your AP comes online — bait her Drakehound's Step dash into your mist and don't duel her while Skip 'n Slash is on cooldown."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your second AP item flips it: Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP magic plus its true-damage center snip cut through her armor, and Skip 'n Slash's attack speed and on-hit range kite her dash chains — extended fights are yours."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold Hallowed Mist and drop it the instant she commits a dash or Public Execution so her empowered auto and Sundering Slam whiff on an untargetable you","Farm safe and stack AP behind your mist until Snip Snip!'s true damage and Skip 'n Slash kiting come fully online","Reach 2+ items where your %-max-HP and true damage reclaim the duel against her armor while your passive healing eats her burst"],"foe":["Brace Repudiation to ground your Skip 'n Slash, then land Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam while your Mist is down","Catch you in the open at 6 with Public Execution's suppress-and-stun before you can reposition into mist","Snowball her Eclipse plus Q-max burst window before your second AP item and Snip Snip!'s true damage take over"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are a knife-fight neither of you owns — her combo is not fully online and you are a clunky cone with no W armour and no Skip 'n Slash refund to lean on. Her plan is Cunning Sweep's edge into a Drakehound's Step empowered auto, which converts her next cast into Sundering Slam, so have Hallowed Mist ready to snap untargetable and eat the slam on air. The trap is Repudiation: while she braces it she grounds you, and a grounded Skip 'n Slash cannot leave. Dash before the brace, chip with the cone tip, and last-hit.","mid":"This is her window and you have to respect it. At levels 4-5 you are a melee with no untargetability if W is down, and her Cunning-Sweep-into-empowered-auto out-trades you while she farms toward 6. At 6 Public Execution blinks behind you and suppresses into a stun, and Lacerate's slow keeps you pinned — if your mist is already spent she catches you clean. So hold Hallowed Mist for the exact moment she commits the ult, and never dash in after Repudiation is braced: it grounds Skip 'n Slash and strands you inside the slam. Through her Eclipse and level-9 Q-max spike, bait Sundering Slam into the mist, slow her with Needlework, and refuse the extended trade until your AP comes online.","late":"The late game is yours and the win rate knows it. Past your second AP item, Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP magic plus its true-damage centre snip cut straight through whatever armour she stacks, your ability healing off her health bar eats her burst, and Skip 'n Slash's attack speed and on-hit range kite her dash chains instead of getting pinned by Lacerate. Public Execution heals her on a 100s cooldown at rank 3, so carry Grievous Wounds and that refund disappears. Her largely physical kit running into your health-and-MR scaling loses the long fight, so survive her 6-and-Eclipse spikes, scale safe behind the mist, and drag every fight long. Do not coinflip an even trade at 6 when waiting two items makes the duel a freebie.","whys":["I'm a weak level-1 with one clunky cone and no mist armor, but Ambessa is energy-gated with her combo not online yet, so nobody owns the opening — just deny her Cunning Sweep last-hits and set up my spike.","Her Cunning Sweep edge into a Drakehound's Step empowered auto can trade, but Hallowed Mist snaps you untargetable mid-commit, so the exchange stays even on who reads the cooldown.","My Snip Snip!-into-Skip-'n-Slash poke-and-reset is online, but she can still pin me with Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam if my W is down — it's a skill matchup on whether I catch her commit on a dropped mist.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window: Repudiation grounds Skip 'n Slash every 18s, so her empowered auto out-trades you and you cannot leave.","Public Execution dashes behind me and suppresses into a stun while Lacerate's slow holds me still, so if my mist is on cooldown she gets a guaranteed lockdown — her cleanest kill window.","Eclipse and Q max let her Cunning-Sweep-Sundering-Slam chunk me before I scale — her hardest favor window, so she'll force the all-in here and I should bait the mist instead.","Past two AP items my Snip Snip! %-max-HP and true damage shred her armor and Skip 'n Slash kites her dashes — her physical-heavy kit loses the extended duel, so I reclaim it."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"aurora","win":["Aurora","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Aurora","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Roughly even at the start — Aurora has no W blink reset rhythm going and Gwen has no Snip Snip! trades that matter, so both just soak XP and last-hit while you wait for your spacing tools."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Aurora's worst window for you: you are a melee without enough Hallowed Mist uptime, and she chips you with Twofold Hex plus a Weirding slow on every walk-up to farm."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Aurora's spike — Between Worlds repositions you off your wave and Across the Veil keeps her out of Hallowed Mist and invisible, so she bursts before Needlework volleys and your ability-healing ever grind."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Gwen's only reclaim window — Riftmaker plus %-max-HP Snip Snip! and a bought anti-heal item let her delete Aurora the instant the W blink is down and she's pinned inside the mist."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive to your 2+ item spike with even CS — Riftmaker and %-max-HP Snip Snip! are the only things that flip this lane against her range","Bait Across the Veil first, then E in and drop Hallowed Mist so her Twofold Hex and Weirding slow whiff while you sit untargetable","Save your Skip 'n Slash for AFTER she blinks with W, not before — chasing into the blink just feeds her a free root-and-burst"],"foe":["Chip you with Twofold Hex and a Weirding slow every time you step up to last-hit, healing it all back with Spirit Abjuration","Hold the W blink to dodge the instant Gwen's Skip 'n Slash dash commits, leaving her stranded outside her own mist","Drop Between Worlds at 6 to knock you off your wave and out of mist range, then land the Weirding slow and burst you down"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are roughly even because neither of you wants to commit — you have no Hallowed Mist value yet and Aurora cannot all-in before her blink is online, so both of you soak XP and last-hit. The problem starts around 3: she pokes with Twofold Hex from 900 range that your 450 cone cannot reach, Spirit Abjuration heals the chip straight back off you, and Skip 'n Slash is your only way in — which is exactly what Across the Veil punishes, blinking and turning her invisible as you land. Never dash to chase the poke. Farm, buy Grievous Wounds early, and respect that she out-ranges you until your items land.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your single worst window: you are melee without enough Hallowed Mist uptime, so every walk-up to a minion is a free Twofold Hex and Weirding slow for Aurora. At 6 it gets worse before it gets better — Between Worlds knocks you off your wave and Across the Veil keeps her outside the mist and invisible on landing, so Needlework volleys and your ability-healing never get to grind. Only commit once she has spent Across the Veil: Skip 'n Slash in, drop Hallowed Mist as she casts so her Q and the Weirding slow whiff, then Needlework to slow the disengage. Otherwise take the safe CS.","late":"This is the only stretch you genuinely own. Once Riftmaker and your second item land, Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP magic plus the true-damage center snip and your ability-healing turn any caught fight into a kill — and Grievous Wounds against Spirit Abjuration means that if you ever pin her inside the mist, she dies before Between Worlds can reset the fight. But Aurora spends the whole game blinking away from exactly that, so do not expect to corner her in the side lane. Group, force fights where Hallowed Mist swallows her Twofold Hex and Weirding slow, and use Skip 'n Slash's refund to stay glued once Across the Veil is down.","whys":["Neither commits at level 1 — you have no mist value and Aurora has no blink-reset all-in, so you trade last-hits and soak XP even.","Twofold Hex out-ranges your 450 cone and Spirit Abjuration heals her off the poke — buy Grievous Wounds, you cannot out-chip her.","She pokes from 900 range and holds Across the Veil for the instant your Skip 'n Slash lands, going invisible — every trade attempt costs you more.","You are melee without enough Hallowed Mist uptime — Aurora chips you with Twofold Hex and a Weirding slow on every walk-up and you cannot answer.","Between Worlds knocks you off your wave and Across the Veil keeps her out of mist and invisible, bursting before Needlework and healing grind.","Aurora's first-item burst plus blink mobility still beats Gwen's pre-Riftmaker self — she pokes, dodges the dash, and Gwen can't pin her.","Riftmaker online: %-max-HP Snip Snip!, the true-damage snip, ability-healing and Grievous Wounds delete Aurora the moment Across the Veil is down inside the mist."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"camille","win":["Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Camille's window — a 16s Hookshot stun into her Precision Protocol true-damage cast out-stats you before Hallowed Mist exists, so never hold E range with her Q charged."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework flips the lane: drop W as her E stun lands so she's committed inside the fog while you sit untargetable on its edge, then R-slow and snip her down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker online — A Thousand Cuts, %-max-HP Snip Snip! and Grievous Wounds win every extended duel her Tactical Sweep heal cannot keep pace with."},{"when":"Late","text":"Her R arena traps her inside the mist with you, so Hallowed Mist hides nothing there — bait the wall-dash re-engage and her Q reset first."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit 6 and drop Hallowed Mist as her E hookshot stun lands so she's stuck committed while you sit untargetable on the fog's edge","Reach your first AP item and Grievous Wounds, where %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus healing out-grind her Tactical Sweep in long fights","Keep Skip 'n Slash up and its cooldown refunded on-hit so you can re-mist every time she dashes off a wall to reset"],"foe":["Land the wall-dash E stun into a second-cast Q true-damage proc at level 2-3 to win the trade before your W exists","Use the R arena for a 1v1 where Hallowed Mist cannot hide you, since she is trapped inside it with you","Stall the lane to two-plus items where her true-damage duelist kit and reset-Q tempo scale up"]},"early":"Level 1 you are both soft, but Camille owns the lane the second she hits 2 — Hookshot is a 16s stun at rank 1 (long off a wall) into a Precision Protocol true-damage second cast, and that out-stats you before Hallowed Mist exists. Do not sit in E range with her Q charged; last-hit at the tip of Snip Snip! and eat a little poke rather than feed a wall-dash trade. Tactical Sweep heals her on the slowed half, so a short Q-and-back just feeds her sustain — farm to 6, do not brawl on her terms.","mid":"Six is the flip. When Camille E's in, drop Hallowed Mist on top of yourself as her stun lands — she is committed inside the fog while you are untargetable to her from its edge, then Needlework slows her and Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP cone plus the true-damage centre snip grind her down. Her burst opens on a Precision Protocol auto reset, so the wind-up is your cue, not the cast. Levels 4-5 before your W are still a coinflip if she hookshots you onto a wall, so do not over-extend until you have the mist button.","late":"This is yours if you close it — at your first AP item %-max-HP Snip Snip! shreds and A Thousand Cuts sustain out-grinds her cone heal, so you win the straight duel. The one thing that flips it is The Hextech Ultimatum: Hallowed Mist only hides you from enemies outside it, and her arena locks her inside it with you, so the mist is simply off in there. Keep Skip 'n Slash up, never get caught dashing off terrain, bait her Hookshot into the fog and let the Q reset whiff before you commit.","whys":["You are both weak at level 1 — she cannot wall-stun without E ranked and you have no Mist, so just deny her last-hits and set the lane up.","At 2 her 16s Hookshot stun into a Precision Protocol true-damage cast out-stats you and you have no Hallowed Mist to escape — respect the all-in.","With E plus Q she dashes in, stuns and procs true damage before you can mist it away — farm at Snip Snip!'s tip and do not trade.","Pre-W you are a melee with no untargetability and she can hook you onto a wall, but neither of you spikes here — play for 6.","Needlework online: drop W as her E stun lands so she is committed in the fog, R-slow her, and out-sustain through A Thousand Cuts healing.","Riftmaker plus %-max-HP Snip Snip! and Grievous Wounds beat her Tactical Sweep heal in every extended fight — force the all-in now.","Even at items your %-HP Q shreds and your sustain beats her cone heal — you win the duel, but the mist is off inside her ult arena."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"cassiopeia","win":["Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Cassiopeia owns the early lane — her Q (Noxious Blast) poison plus Twin Fang chip you down before you have Hallowed Mist to hide in or E's on-hit range to touch her."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her R (Petrifying Gaze) face-stun is the spike that beats you: if you're facing her when it lands she stuns and full-combos you before you can drop Hallowed Mist or E away."},{"when":"Lvl 6 (yours)","text":"Needlework plus your full Q-W-E lets you mist her R, slow her, and E-dash onto her squishy bar — Miasma grounds that dash for 24s, so spend E only after the grounding ends."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's plus Grievous Wounds online: %-max-HP Snip Snip! and Hallowed Mist beat the healing Twin Fang refunds her — force the all-in before her 2-item kite arrives."}],"wants":{"you":["Wait out Miasma's 24s grounding, then E-dash in under Hallowed Mist so her poke whiffs and your Snip Snip! center-snip true damage lands","Hit Riftmaker/Nashor's with Grievous Wounds and all-in her — %-max-HP shred plus A Thousand Cuts beats the healing Twin Fang gives her back","Punish when her Twin Fang is the only spell up — she has no dash or blink to peel your Skip 'n Slash, so she can't escape once you're on top of her"],"foe":["Stack Q (Noxious Blast) poison and Twin Fang on you from range while you have no Hallowed Mist to break line of sight or E range to reach her","Land Petrifying Gaze frontally to stun you out of W and full-combo before you can mist the damage or dash in","Survive to 2+ items and kite you with her bootless passive move speed and Miasma grounding, out-DPSing your melee range from outside mist"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are hers, not yours. Cassiopeia's Q (Noxious Blast) poison and Twin Fang chip you down before you have Hallowed Mist to hide in or Skip 'n Slash's on-hit range to touch her, and her W (Miasma) grounds your dash for 24s at rank 1 if you force it raw. Do not walk up to last-hit into her poison cloud — soak the minimum, eat the chip, and stay above half HP so her R never has a kill setup. Twin Fang refires every 0.75s on a poisoned target and heals her as it goes, so every tick she lands both speeds up and repays her next one.","mid":"Level 6 is the swing, and the order matters: HER 6 (Petrifying Gaze, the face-stun) beats you if you are caught facing her flat-footed, but YOUR 6 flips the lane. Drop Hallowed Mist the instant her R or Miasma commits — the stun and grounding still land, but you keep snipping untargetably from inside the fog, and once the grounding ends you E-dash on top of her and chain Needlework's slow so she cannot kite. Her R is 120s at rank 1: bait it once and the next two minutes are yours. She has no dash or blink, so in Snip Snip! range her poison cannot out-trade A Thousand Cuts plus your healing.","late":"This is where you take over — but close it before she hits her own 2-item scaling. Your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike turns Snip Snip! into %-max-HP shred her squishy bar cannot survive, and Hallowed Mist nullifies her only defensive layer since she has no escape. All-in on cooldown: wait out Miasma's 24s grounding, E in, mist to eat the R, Q through her, and let A Thousand Cuts plus Grievous Wounds beat the healing Twin Fang refunds her. The danger is dragging it to her 2+ item window, where her passive move speed and Miasma grounding let her kite you from outside mist. Win it at first item.","whys":["You're both weak level 1 — she has no real Twin Fang chain yet and you have no Hallowed Mist, so it's a wash decided by who wins the last-hit poke; just deny her free Q (Noxious Blast) harass on the wave.","Her Q poison plus a Twin Fang that heals her out-chip you while you have no W untargetability and no E range to answer — eat the poke and farm, do not enter the cloud.","She still out-stats you here: Miasma grounds any raw Skip 'n Slash for 24s at rank 1, and her poison keeps Twin Fang's bonus damage online faster than you trade back.","Once you hit your full kit you out-trade a no-mobility mage — drop Hallowed Mist on her engage so the poison whiffs, then E-dash in after the grounding ends.","Petrifying Gaze is a hard answer at 6: a frontal hit stuns you out of W and full-combos before you can mist the damage — but it is 120s, so bait it and commit.","Needlework plus your full Q-W-E lets you mist her R, slow her with R, and grind her squishy bar down — your real flip point this lane.","Your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike plus %-max-HP Snip Snip! and Hallowed Mist untargetability win every extended duel — all-in before her 2-item kite scaling arrives."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"chogath","win":["Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Q+E online — Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP magic cone plus its true-damage center snip ignore his armor, and Skip 'n Slash refunds most of its cooldown when it lands so you dash in, snip, and dash out before he can Rupture you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His one threat window: Feast (R, 80s at rank 1) is flat true damage that kills you outright if it beats your current HP, so never fight him near half — Mist's armour and MR do not touch true damage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's is your peak — %-max-HP A Thousand Cuts autos and Q grind his stacked health while Hallowed Mist's untargetability blanks his single-target auto follow-up and tower dives on you."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Cho out-scales most bruisers and a 6+ stack Feast still executes you, but his armor does nothing to your magic-and-true package — open every all-in with him healthy, snip him down, and finish before his R comes back up."}],"wants":{"you":["Open every trade with Snip Snip! — the %-max-HP cone and true center snip melt his stacked, armor-heavy HP bar that bruiser AD can't touch","Use Skip 'n Slash to dash in, refund it off the hit, and weave autos so A Thousand Cuts chunks more of his health the bigger he stacks","Drop Hallowed Mist for the armor/MR and to go untargetable to his autos and single-target follow-up while you keep snipping him inside the fog"],"foe":["Land Rupture (Q) knockup to lock you in place, then chain Feral Scream (W) silence to deny both your E dash and your W cloud","Stack Feast HP and chip you with Vorpal Spikes from inside his wave, zoning a short-range melee off CS with his long Q range","Hit a Feast (R) execute threshold so his flat true-damage nuke kills you outright regardless of your Mist armor or passive healing"]},"early":"Cho'Gath is a bully target — his giant HP bar is exactly what Snip Snip! eats, since the cone deals %-max-HP magic and the centre snip is true damage, both ignoring the armour he stacks. Level 1 is a wash, so farm and sidestep Rupture (Q, 6s); that delayed knockup is his only real punish. From 2-3 poke with Q and refund Skip 'n Slash off the hit to dash back out, but respect Vorpal Spikes chipping and slowing you from inside his own wave, and bait Feral Scream (W, 11s) before you commit — that silence takes both your dash and your mist.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are even because he can shove with Rupture and zone you off CS with his longer range while you are still a short-range melee, so respect his Q and farm for your item spike. The big trap is level 6: Feast (R, 80s at rank 1) is flat true damage that kills you outright if it exceeds your current HP, so even though you out-trade him all lane, fighting him under half gets you deleted — and Hallowed Mist's armour and MR do nothing against true damage. Keep snipping his health, drop Mist for untargetability against his autos, and only all-in when his R is down or you are healthy.","late":"This is your house — the fatter he stacks Feast the harder your A Thousand Cuts autos and %-HP Snip hit, and your passive heals more the bigger his HP bar gets, so his scaling literally feeds you. Hallowed Mist gives armour and MR and dodges his single-target auto follow-up while you grind him down, and his stacked armour is worthless against your magic-and-true package. One rule never changes: a fully stacked Cho's Feast is flat true damage that ignores your sustain, so never duel him low — open every fight healthy, snip him to nothing, and finish inside his 80s R window.","whys":["Level 1 is even — he has no Rupture-into-Feral-Scream combo set up yet and you have no Mist, so you both just last-hit and trade jabs.","At 2 your Q comes online and its %-max-HP magic plus true centre snip already out-trade a Cho who can only poke with Rupture into your armour-ignoring damage.","With Q+E you dash in, snip his armour-stacked HP for percent damage, and refund Skip 'n Slash to dash out before his slow body can Rupture you.","Levels 4-5 even out — he shoves and zones with Rupture's range and Vorpal Spikes chip while you are still a short-range melee with no item spike yet.","At 6 Feast is flat true damage on an 80s cooldown that kills through Mist's resistances and your healing, so this window is his — do not fight him low.","Your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike plus Hallowed Mist win the extended duel, snipping his health while his autos cannot target you inside the fog.","Late, his Feast stacks just feed your %-HP autos and passive healing — you shred him harder the bigger he builds, as long as you open healthy and his R is down."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"darius","win":["Darius","Darius","Skill","Darius","Skill","Darius","Darius"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Darius owns the opener — Apprehend drags you in on a 26s cooldown, Decimate's outer blade chunks and heals him while Hemorrhage ticks, and you have no mist or E dash yet to escape his brutal melee range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hallowed Mist plus Needlework finally let you mist his all-in and out-grind a long fight, but Noxian Guillotine executes with true damage if you let your HP dip into its threshold."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike turns Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP magic into real DPS, evening the brawl as long as you bait Apprehend before committing."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Two items in, your magic %-max-HP Q ignores his armour, his stacked HP feeds A Thousand Cuts, and Grievous Wounds stops Decimate refunding him — you out-trade every extended duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait or sidestep Apprehend for a 26s window, then mist so his Decimate and Crippling Strike follow-up land while you are untargetable","Survive levels 1-5 farming with the outer snips of Snip Snip! and reach your level 6 plus first-item spike","Fight long inside mist: let %-max-HP Q plus your ability healing grind his big HP bar down faster than his bleed grinds yours"],"foe":["Land Apprehend to drag you out of mist, then Crippling Strike into a Decimate all-in","Stack Hemorrhage to five for Noxian Might and snowball levels 1-9 before your scaling matters","Finish you with Noxian Guillotine's true-damage execute while you are low, beating your sustain"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are his. Darius out-stats you flat — Apprehend yanks you in, the outer blade of Decimate carves a chunk while it heals him off you, and Hemorrhage bleeds keep ticking while your cone Q is still clunky and you have no mist or E dash to escape. Do not trade through this; last-hit with the outer snips of Snip Snip!. Apprehend is 26s at rank 1, so the moment he misses it you have twenty seconds to farm freely — that window is the whole early game.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay soft for you, but at 6 it evens out. With Hallowed Mist plus Needlework you can finally answer his commit — bait the Apprehend pull, drop your mist as you land so his Decimate and Crippling Strike follow-up land while you are untargetable, and slow him with R while you snip. Crippling Strike is an auto reset, so the wind-up is your mist cue, not the cast. The longer the fight runs the more your healing and %-max-HP Q swing it. The trap is Noxian Guillotine: caught low, its true damage ignores your sustain, so only commit healthy.","late":"This flips to you. Two items in, every point of HP Darius stacks is more fuel for A Thousand Cuts and Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP magic — his armour does nothing against it, and his big bar means more healing for you on every ability hit. Buy Grievous Wounds so Decimate stops refunding him, fight inside Hallowed Mist so his all-in stalls, and respect only the 120s Guillotine when you are low. Close the lane on his 26s Apprehend cooldowns and you own every extended brawl.","whys":["Darius out-stats you at level 1 — Apprehend, Decimate's outer-blade chunk and self-heal, and Hemorrhage bleeds beat a clunky cone Q with no mist or E dash to escape.","He still owns level 2 — his pull into Decimate all-in outdamages your single new tool, so farm and dodge Apprehend instead of trading.","Even with Q plus E online, his bleed stacks and pull win every melee trade before your spikes — step up only in the 26s after Apprehend whiffs.","Levels 4-5 are a coinflip — you are pre-6 with no untargetability, but you can deny trades around his Apprehend cooldown and bank farm with the outer snips.","At 6 you can mist his all-in and out-grind a long fight, but Noxian Guillotine true-damages through your healing — even, and HP-dependent.","Your Riftmaker spike evens the brawl as %-max-HP Snip starts to bite, but Guillotine still punishes any mistimed engage — fight only after baiting the pull.","Two items on, your magic %-max-HP Q ignores his armour, his stacked HP feeds A Thousand Cuts, and Grievous Wounds cuts Decimate's heal — you win every long duel."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"drmundo","win":["Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Mundo's Q cleaver throws percent-current-HP poke that his passive regenerates back, and you have no mist, no E dash, and a slow six-snip cone Q — sidestep the cleaver, farm with the tips of Snip Snip!, and accept some chip rather than forcing a fight."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus full Q-W-E comes online: drop Hallowed Mist so his autos and E-empowered swing can't touch you, then snip his oversized HP bar — the center line of Snip Snip! deals true damage his armor and bonus HP can't reduce while your abilities heal you off the trade."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's is your takeover — Snip Snip!'s percent-max-HP magic and A Thousand Cuts on-hit ignore the armour he builds, and the more HP he stacks the harder you cut, so out-DPS his Q self-heal here."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Maximum Dosage is a huge instant heal plus regen, MS and AD on a flat 120s at every rank — but percent-max-HP magic, true-damage centre snips and Grievous Wounds out-shred his heal-per-second, so bait it, then commit inside Hallowed Mist and grind him down."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 6 and your first item, then duel Mundo from inside Hallowed Mist and shred his huge HP bar with percent-max-HP and the true-damage center line of Snip Snip!","Buy Grievous Wounds early so his grey-health regen, Q self-heal, stored Heart Zapper damage and Maximum Dosage cannot out-sustain your DPS","Use Hallowed Mist to blank his autos and E-empowered swing, and Skip 'n Slash to reposition and refund the dash by hitting him, then reset and re-snip"],"foe":["Land Q cleaver percent-HP pokes at levels 1-3 while you're a mist-less melee with no dash and a slow cone Q","Stack HP and soak your burst in Heart Zapper to heal it back, until Maximum Dosage and grey-health regen out-heal you","Use the move speed and slow-immunity from a landed Q cleaver to walk you down or kite away from your all-in"]},"early":"Level 1 belongs to Mundo and you have to respect it — you have no mist, no E dash, just a slow six-snip cone Q, while his Q cleaver throws percent-current-HP poke that his passive grey-health regen heals back. Do not walk into cleaver range; sidestep it, farm with the tips of Snip Snip!, and accept some chip. His step-up opens on a Blunt Force Trauma auto reset, so the wind-up is your cue to back off, not the cast. By 2-3 you can poke and hold E for safety, but this is still a farm phase. Every point of HP he stacks is future fuel for your percent-max-HP autos and Q.","mid":"This is the turning point but it is a skill phase, not a free win — at 6, Needlework plus full Q-W-E lets you actually duel him. Drop Hallowed Mist on yourself so his autos and the Blunt Force Trauma reset cannot target you, then snip his oversized bar: the centre line of Snip Snip! lands TRUE damage his armour and bonus HP cannot reduce, and your damage heals you back. Never dump a trade into an active Heart Zapper — it stores what you deal and gives it back as health, so snip after it expires. Skip 'n Slash repositions and refunds off hitting him; his Q cleaver is a skillshot the mist will not dodge, so keep moving.","late":"This is your kingdom and the rare lane where late game gets BETTER for you. Mundo does not out-scale you — he stacks the exact stat you punish: HP. Your percent-max-HP magic and the true-damage centre line of Snip Snip! ignore all the armour and bonus health he buys, so the fatter he gets the harder you cut. Maximum Dosage is a huge instant heal plus regen on a flat 120s at every rank, so keep Grievous Wounds up, bait it once, and the next two minutes are a Mundo who cannot reset a fight. Do not disengage off his R — commit, snip, and out-DPS the regen inside the mist.","whys":["Mundo's Q cleaver percent-HP poke and passive self-heal own the level-1 lane while you have no mist, no dash, and only a slow cone Q — sidestep and farm.","You can poke with Q at level 2 but you're still a soft melee against his cleaver poke and grey-health regen — even, lean toward farming.","Q lets you trade and you can hold E for safety, but his early bulk and Q self-heal soak it and he can walk you down off a landed cleaver — skill matchup.","You're a mist-less, pre-spike melee in your worst window and his percent-HP poke keeps pace, but he can't kill you either — genuinely even.","Needlework and full Q-W-E let you blank his autos in Hallowed Mist and snip true damage, yet his sustain means it's a window not a guaranteed kill — even.","Riftmaker online: Snip Snip!'s percent-max-HP magic ignores his armor and hits harder the more HP he stacks, out-DPSing his Q self-heal — your spike beats his.","The more tank items and HP he buys the harder your percent-max-HP and true damage cut, and Grievous Wounds answers a 120s Maximum Dosage — you shred this drain-tank inside the mist."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"fiora","win":["Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Fiora owns the early lane: her Q-dash spaces your cone Snip Snip! and her passive vitals chunk you with %-max-HP true damage while your only Q-poke is a slow, telegraphed cone you can't safely step up to land."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework (R) is your flip — bait her Q-Q all-in, drop Hallowed Mist so she lands standing OUTSIDE the fog where she can't target you, then slow with R and grind her with your %-HP autos and snips."},{"when":"Her W (Riposte)","text":"Riposte is the whole lane: 24s at rank 1, and if she parries the cast that matters — your E dash-in or your R — she stuns you and free-trades, so never throw Skip 'n Slash or R into an up Riposte."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your real spike: post-Riftmaker, %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus A Thousand Cuts autos, healing and Grievous Wounds out-grind her once a single parry cannot undo a full duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive lanes 1-5 farming with the Q cone's true-damage center snip until your level-6 R and Hallowed Mist let you fight","Buy Grievous Wounds — Duelist's Dance and Grand Challenge heal her off vitals, and without it she refunds your whole grind","Bait or eat her 24s Riposte on a throwaway Skip 'n Slash before committing your real R plus Snip Snip! burst and healing"],"foe":["Land Riposte (W) on your E dash-in or your R cast to stun you and win the trade for free","Q-dash onto your vitals to proc her passive %-max-HP true damage before you reach Hallowed Mist range","Use her stronger early stats and Q spacing to snowball a lead before your Riftmaker %-HP spike arrives"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to Fiora and you have to respect it — your Hallowed Mist isn't enough to fight in yet and Snip Snip! is a slow cone you can't step up to land, while her Q-dash plus passive vitals shred you with %-max-HP true damage before you reach a trade you win. Don't walk into her Q range to throw the cone; farm safely with the true-damage center snip when she's last-hitting and the on-hit chip from your autos. Her early stats simply beat yours, so bank CS and HP, not pride.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still her window — you are a short-range melee and she out-trades you every time Riposte is up. The flip is level 6: now you can drop Hallowed Mist as she commits her Q-Q all-in so she ends up standing outside the fog and literally cannot target you, while you slow with Needlework and grind her down with %-HP autos. The non-negotiable rule is Riposte, 24s at rank 1 — if her W is up, give nothing, because she parries your Skip 'n Slash or R, stuns you, and free-trades. Bait it on a throwaway E, then run your real combo inside those 24 seconds.","late":"This is where you take the lane back. Once Riftmaker and your second item land, %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus A Thousand Cuts autos and your healing out-grind her in any extended duel — one Riposte cannot undo a full fight the way it undid your early commits. Carry Grievous Wounds: Duelist's Dance heals her on every vital and Grand Challenge heals off the ones it marks, and without anti-heal she simply refunds the grind. Force long trades inside Hallowed Mist where she is stuck outside it and cannot target you, and never give her a clean Lunge-vital reset.","whys":["Fiora's Q-dash and passive vitals out-stat your slow level-1 cone — your Hallowed Mist can't carry a fight yet, so just last-hit and concede the level.","She gets Riposte and Q spacing online while you're a soft short-range melee — don't contest, she wins the level-2 trade outright.","Her Q-dash chains onto your vitals for %-max-HP true damage before you can land the cone, and you can't outrun it at this range.","Levels 4-5 are your worst window — pre-spike and stuck in melee range, so she out-trades you around a 24s Riposte all day.","Even at 6 she edges it: if she parries your R or Skip 'n Slash with Riposte she stuns you and wins, so your mist-and-slow only evens the fights she misreads — bait the W first.","Pre-Riftmaker your damage can't out-grind a Fiora who plays around her parry — she still out-trades your engage windows on cooldown.","Now %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus A Thousand Cuts autos, your healing and Grievous Wounds beat her in extended duels — one parry cannot out-value sustained magic damage."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"galio","win":["Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once you have Q+E you can Skip 'n Slash in, Snip Snip!, and dash back out — but Winds of War chunks you every time you walk up to last-hit on an 11s cooldown, so only commit in the gaps."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hero's Entrance is a global all-in tool on 180s at rank 1 — he flies a roaming ally onto you and knocks you up on landing, so do not overstay on a pushed wave while it is up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's is your real spike — your %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus its true-damage center snip finally bite into his stacked MR, and you can start winning extended duels from inside Hallowed Mist."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"With two items you out-scale him: %-HP magic and the true-damage snip shred his tank body faster than his Q poke and W damage-reduction shield can sustain, so this is your kill window."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive the level 1-5 Winds of War poke war, then bait his Shield of Durand charge and drop Hallowed Mist as the taunt releases so the follow-up hits nothing","Reach Riftmaker and use percent-max-HP Snip Snip! with its true-damage center snip to cut through the magic resist he stacks","Stall to 2+ items where your %-HP shred and passive sustain out-grind his tank body, then duel him inside Mist where his single-target damage can't reach"],"foe":["Spam Q (Winds of War) tornado to poke you down before you ever reach Mist range","Charge Shield of Durand to soak your snips and release the taunt, or open with a Justice Punch knockup to lock you for the trade","Use global R (Hero's Entrance) to roam to a sidelane or knock you up out of your all-in"]},"early":"Galio owns these levels and you have to accept it. Winds of War out-ranges everything you have on an 11s cooldown and chunks you every time you step up to farm, and you have no Mist yet to hide in. Do not trade through the tornado; last-hit at max range and take the chip. His step-up opens on a Colossal Smash auto reset, and the ability that actually locks you down is Shield of Durand — he charges it, then releases a taunt — while Justice Punch is a dash knockup, not a taunt. Your passive keeps you topped between minions, so just do not fall so far behind that you miss your item spike.","mid":"Still his window, but it is damage control now. Winds of War poke plus Shield of Durand, which cuts the damage he takes while he charges and then releases a taunt, lets him soak your snips and win any short trade before items — especially if Justice Punch knocks you up first. At 6, Hero's Entrance is the real threat: it is 180s at rank 1, so when it is gone you have a long free window, but when it is up he flies a roamer in and knocks you up out of your own all-in. Your one good play is reactive — bait the W charge, drop Hallowed Mist the instant the taunt releases so you are untargetable while it ticks, and snip him from inside the fog.","late":"This is where the lane flips to you. Once you have two items, Snip Snip!'s percent-max-HP magic plus its true-damage centre snip cut straight through all the magic resist Galio stacks — the tankier he builds, the harder you hit, and his poke and W damage reduction cannot out-sustain your passive healing in an extended brawl. Bait the Shield of Durand taunt and the Justice Punch knockup, drop Mist when he commits, and grind him down inside the fog where his single-target poke cannot reach you. Respect his global R in fights elsewhere — he matters more to his team than to this 1v1 now.","whys":["You are both soft at level 1, but his Q tornado pokes from a range you cannot answer — last-hit safe and learn his Winds of War cadence.","Winds of War out-ranges your kit on an 11s cooldown and you have no Mist — he chunks you every time you walk up to farm.","You get Q+E to Skip 'n Slash in and snip-refund, but his Q poke into a Justice Punch knockup still out-trades you before items.","Your worst window — no untargetability against his tornado, and a Shield of Durand taunt locks you for a free trade.","Hero's Entrance drops a roamer on you and knocks you up out of your own all-in — you cannot safely commit at 6 while it is up.","His stacked magic resist eats your pre-Riftmaker damage; he soaks your snips with W and wins the extended trade.","Two items on, your %-max-HP and true-damage Snip Snip! shred his tank body faster than he can sustain — this lane is finally yours."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"gangplank","win":["Gangplank","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gangplank","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Gangplank has no Powder Keg yet and his Parrrley last-hit is mana-hungry and slow, so step up with Skip 'n Slash into Snip Snip! for a free %-max-HP trade before any poke pattern exists."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"His Powder Keg comes online: a placed keg detonated by Parrrley chunks you from outside your range, and Remove Scurvy cleanses your Needlework slow — his hardest early window, so stop facetanking kegs for CS."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Cannon Barrage plus keg zoning lets him fight and deny cannon waves from range you can't reach in melee — bait the keg into Hallowed Mist rather than forcing the all-in on his terms."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Nashor's/Riftmaker is your peak: %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus Hallowed Mist untargetability wins every duel he tries to keg-poke, before his crit and global pressure scale away."}],"wants":{"you":["Drop Hallowed Mist on top of his Powder Keg detonation so the keg blast and Parrrley land harmlessly outside the cloud while you keep snipping him","Hold Skip 'n Slash to dash the gap the instant he commits a keg, then refund it on the champ hit and chunk him with %-max-HP Snip Snip! before he kites","Hit your Nashor's/Riftmaker spike and all-in around 6+ while you out-duel him, before crit barrels and Cannon Barrage start swinging fights off your wave"],"foe":["Place a Powder Keg and detonate it with Parrrley to poke you out before you ever reach autorange, denying you the trade","Use a 22s Remove Scurvy to cleanse your Needlework slow and heal the chip off, then walk out of your melee threat and keep farming","Stall the lane to two-plus items where crit barrels, Cannon Barrage and Cutlass/Shojin pressure out-scale your single-target snowball"]},"early":"Gangplank has nothing at level 1 — no Powder Keg, and a mana-hungry, slow Parrrley last-hit — so step up with Skip 'n Slash into Snip Snip! for a free %-max-HP trade before his poke pattern exists. The lane flips at 3 when the keg comes online: a barrel placed and popped by Parrrley chunks you from outside your range, and Remove Scurvy, 22s at rank 1, cleanses any Needlework slow you land and heals him besides. Stop facetanking kegs to last-hit — walk wide of the barrel, soak the cannon with the tip of Snip Snip!, and do not chase a poke you cannot catch.","mid":"From 4-5 you're a melee soaking keg poke until your kit is fully online, so farm patiently and trade only when Snip Snip! is up. At 6 he gets the better fight at range — Cannon Barrage, keg zoning, and cannon-wave denial you can't contest in melee — so don't force it on his terms. Your answer is the dash and the fog: hold Skip 'n Slash to close, and the SECOND he commits a keg, drop Hallowed Mist on the detonation so the blast and Parrrley whiff outside the cloud while you stay untargetable and snip him down. Bait the keg, mist it, dash in, then Snip-into-R for the chunk.","late":"Your Nashor's/Riftmaker spike is where you take over — %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus Hallowed Mist untargetability wins every extended duel he sets up with kegs, and with Grievous Wounds his 22s Remove Scurvy stops undoing the chip and healing him back once you are in his face. He is a global scaler, so close the lane before crit barrels and a 160s Cannon Barrage start swinging fights across the map — and note that Barrage deals true damage, so no amount of resistances answers it. In fights, dash onto him and stand in your mist on his keg detonations; never let him kite you in the open.","whys":["Pre-keg Gangplank has no Powder Keg and a slow, mana-hungry Parrrley last-hit, so your Skip 'n Slash into Snip Snip! lands a free %-max-HP trade he can't answer.","He gains the keg but you gain Snip Snip! and the dash too — it's a genuine coinflip on whether his Parrrley-popped keg poke or your Skip 'n Slash trade wins the exchange.","His Powder Keg chain detonated by Parrrley is fully online — he pokes from outside autorange and a 22s Remove Scurvy cleanses your slow and heals him before you reach him.","You out-trade a one-item Gangplank by baiting his keg into Hallowed Mist so the blast whiffs outside the cloud while your %-max-HP Snip Snip! keeps hitting.","Cannon Barrage plus keg zoning lets him fight and deny cannon waves from range you can't contest in melee — respect the kegs and don't force the all-in here.","Your Nashor's/Riftmaker spike with %-max-HP Snip Snip! and untargetable mist wins every duel his kegs try to set up, so all-in once you hit it.","With Grievous Wounds you shred him faster than Remove Scurvy can heal once you are in melee, so close the lane before crit barrels and Cannon Barrage scale."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"gnar","win":["Skill","Gnar","Gnar","Skill","Skill","Gnar","Gnar"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Mini-Gnar's boomerang and Hop kite your Snip Snip! cone before you have W mist or your E dash, so he chips you down and repositions on every approach."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"When Rage fills, mega-Gnar's Wallop line-stun — a flat 7s, far faster than your Mist — pins you the instant you step out, and GNAR! into a wall is longer, setting up a gank."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker online: bait the transform, drop W as Wallop lands so the stun-into-burst whiffs, then snip his stacked mega HP and heal off it."},{"when":"Late","text":"Past two items your max-HP Snip Snip and untargetable mist outlast his shrinking mega windows — he is not a true hyperscaler, so this window stays yours."}],"wants":{"you":["Walk fights into Hallowed Mist so mega-Gnar's Wallop stun and boomerang whiff while you keep snipping his max HP","Survive to Riftmaker and use Skip 'n Slash to dash-and-reset onto him, closing the gap mini-Gnar's Hop keeps opening","Bait the mega transform and drop W before Wallop is in flight, then R-slow and grind him out in the extended brawl your sustain wins"],"foe":["Stay in mini form and kite your melee with boomerang poke and Hops, never letting you reach Hallowed Mist range","Land mega-Gnar's Wallop or GNAR! the instant you leave W to chain his burst combo or a jungle gank","Poke you down with boomerang chip so his transform burst or jungler closes the lane before you hit two items"]},"early":"Gnar owns the first three levels and you cannot fight it honestly. Mini-Gnar's Boomerang Throw (Q) and Hop (E) let him poke and reposition while your only tool is a slow six-snip cone you can barely land on a target that keeps hopping away, and you have no W mist or E dash yet. Do not walk up to throw a Q he kites out of. Soak XP at max range, eat the chip, and watch his Rage bar rather than his health bar — catching his boomerang refunds its cooldown, so trading into the return path only funds his next poke. Track the Rage, not the HP.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your first breath: you finally have a real kit and can use Skip 'n Slash to dash in, snip, and refund the dash off hitting him, so a whiffed Hop is a 22-second window at rank 1 to actually reach him. But level 6 swings back: the moment his Rage fills, mega-Gnar's Wallop line-stun can pin you the instant you leave your mist, and GNAR! can throw you into a wall for longer — either chains into his beefier autos. Wallop is a flat 7s, three times faster than your Mist, so you cannot outlast it; drop Hallowed Mist as the transform animation starts, before the stun is in flight, and never commit while he is one boomerang from mega.","late":"This is where the matchup flips to you, and it is the only reason the lane is TRICKY and not HARD. Once Riftmaker and a second item are online, your Snip Snip! shreds the max HP and resists mega-Gnar stacks, your kit heals off the damage you deal to his fat bar, and Hallowed Mist makes his transform burst miss while you keep snipping from untargetable. He is not a true hyperscaler like Kayle or Vayne, so he does not reclaim this window — his mega window just gets smaller and harder to land relative to your two-item brawl. Survive to two items, then walk every fight into your mist and grind him out.","whys":["Mini-Gnar's boomerang poke and Hop out-range and out-kite your slow Snip Snip! cone, and you have neither W mist nor E dash yet to answer.","He keeps kiting with boomerang and Hops while your early kit can't pin down a champion who repositions on cooldown, and catching his boomerang only refunds it for more poke.","Even as your Q and E come online, mini-Gnar's range and lowered-cooldown boomerang own the trade before you can reach mist.","Skip 'n Slash finally lets you contest and a whiffed 22s Hop is a real window, but you are a melee with no W up yet against a ranged kiter — coinflip.","Mega-Gnar's Wallop line-stun pins you the instant you step out of mist and chains into his burst or a gank, and GNAR! into a wall is even longer.","His transform burst still beats your first item if he catches you outside W, so respect the Rage bar over your Riftmaker timing.","Two items in, your max-HP Snip Snip and untargetable mist shred his stacked mega HP faster than his shrinking transform window can burst you, and you heal off every snip."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"gragas","win":["Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once you have Q+E, Skip 'n Slash in, land the center-snip true damage, and dash back out before his Body Slam E comes off cooldown to stun you — your first clean trade window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Gragas spikes hardest here: a 100s Explosive Cask can knock you OUT of your Hallowed Mist, stripping the untargetability mid-fight, or flip the displacement to peel and roam — any fight he starts at 6 is his."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online — %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus A Thousand Cuts healing and Grievous Wounds out-grind his Drunken Rage reduction and Happy Hour sustain, evening the lane."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your magic %-HP shred out-duels a scaling AP brawler whose only escape is a telegraphed Body Slam — close the gap before he roams off the R and the straight 1v1 is yours."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his Body Slam E, then drop Hallowed Mist as it commits so you sit untargetable and his stun-follow-up whiffs","Reach Riftmaker and Grievous Wounds, then grind his HP bar with %-max-HP Snip Snip! and passive healing","Skip 'n Slash in for a center snip and dash out before his E and barrel poke come back up"],"foe":["Land Body Slam E to gap-close and stun, then Explosive Cask R to displace you out of your Hallowed Mist","Sustain trades with Happy Hour healing off every cast while Drunken Rage lets him tank your snips","Use R to peel you off, cancel your positioning, or knock you away and roam mid with the displacement"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are a careful AP brawl — neither of you wants to over-commit. Gragas pokes with the barrel and Happy Hour heals him on every cast, so do not walk up for a clunky cone Q he simply sustains back. By 2-3, once you have Q+E, you can Skip 'n Slash in, land the centre-snip true damage, and dash back out inside his 14s Body Slam cooldown. Respect that per-cast healing: it out-paces chip, so trade for tempo and farm rather than a kill you cannot close, and plan Grievous Wounds into your build.","mid":"Levels 4-6 belong to Gragas — Explosive Cask is the problem. He Body Slams onto you and ult-knockbacks to shove you clean OUT of your Hallowed Mist, stripping the untargetability, or flings you off a needle target. Do not drop W early and stand in it like a safe zone. Bait the 14s Body Slam, mist as it lands so the stun whiffs, then snip — and watch the swing wind-up, because Drunken Rage is an auto reset. His R is 100s against your 120s, so hold Needlework for after the knockback.","late":"Once Riftmaker comes online the lane flips even and the late game is yours. A scaling AP brawler like Gragas has a fat HP bar and no real escape past one telegraphed Body Slam — exactly what %-max-HP Snip Snip! and A Thousand Cuts healing want to grind on. His Drunken Rage reduction and Happy Hour sustain only delay it, and Grievous Wounds removes the delay. Drag him into Hallowed Mist for extended duels and out-sustain him. His one out is roaming off the R displacement, so keep him pinned: in a straight 1v1 at two items, you win.","whys":["Even AP brawl at level 1 — his barrel poke and Drunken Rage W sustain edge your clunky cone Q, but neither of you can commit, so just farm.","Gragas owns level 2 — his Body Slam E stun and W heal-and-reduction out-stat you before your kit comes together.","With Q+E you can Skip 'n Slash in, land the true-damage center snip, and dash out before his E resets — the trade evens out.","Gragas edges 4-5 — he out-pressures a pre-W Gwen with barrel poke and W sustain while you have no untargetability yet.","Gragas spikes hardest at 6 — his Explosive Cask R knocks you out of Hallowed Mist or flings you off your needle target, flipping any fight he starts.","Riftmaker and %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus Thousand Cuts healing let you grind through his Drunken Rage W damage reduction — the lane evens here.","You out-scale him 1v1 — %-HP shred, passive healing and Grievous Wounds beat a no-escape brawler the longer it goes."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"garen","win":["Gwen","Skill","Garen","Garen","Gwen","Skill","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Decisive Strike (Q) is a flat 8s auto reset that silences your Snip Snip! mid-cast while you have no Hallowed Mist to hide behind — his hardest window, and your E refund is dead against a foe who walks away on passive regen."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hallowed Mist plus Needlework online: drop the fog on his Q engage so his empowered strike and silence whiff, then chunk and slow him — but Demacian Justice (R) is missing-HP true damage that executes you the moment you dip low, so it stays genuinely even."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online: your %-max-HP Snip and on-hit grind out-trade his short Q-W combo, and E refunds let you reset in and out of mist to shove for plates."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"You shred him — %-max-HP magic Snip plus the center snip's true damage ignores his armor and Courage (W) only shaves burst, not your sustained on-hit DPS in mist."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm safely and only Snip (Q) inside the 8s Decisive Strike gap with his 22s Courage down, so he cannot cancel your cast or eat the trade","Reach Level 6 and your first item so Hallowed Mist plus %-HP Snip flip the duel and your heal-on-damage out-sustains his regen","Drop Hallowed Mist on his Q engage so his empowered strike and silence eat the fog, then slow him with Needlework and grind him in the cloud"],"foe":["Open with a Decisive Strike auto reset to silence your Snip cast and stick the crit while you are still mist-less","Pop Courage (W) as you Snip to cut your trade, then walk off and regen the chip with his passive","Hit Demacian Justice (R) the moment you drop below half HP — missing-HP true damage executes you through mist and armor"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are his, plainly. Decisive Strike (Q) is a flat 8s that silences your Snip Snip! mid-cast and comes out as an auto-attack reset, so the swing wind-up — not the cast — is your tell, and you have no Hallowed Mist yet to make any of it whiff. Last-hit at the tip of your cone Q, accept the chip, and never E-dash in to trade: there is no champion to hit for the cooldown refund early, his short Q-W combo out-stats you, and he walks away on passive regen. The upside is he cannot kill you outright if you never feed him a free silence window.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — a melee with no untargetability against a bruiser who out-stats you pre-mist and regens any chip you land. At 6 it finally evens out: drop Hallowed Mist as he flickers in for the Q so his empowered strike and silence eat the fog, slow him with Needlework, and let your heal-on-damage out-sustain his trade inside the cloud. But respect his ult — Demacian Justice is missing-HP true damage on 120s at rank 1, so the moment you dip low his execute deletes you regardless of mist or armour. Bait his 22s Courage (W) before you commit your real Snip.","late":"This is where you take the lane back. Your %-max-HP magic Snip plus the centre snip's true damage ignore his armour entirely, and Courage (W) only shaves burst — it does nothing against your sustained on-hit DPS once Riftmaker and an attack-speed item come online. Stand in your mist, use E's range and refund to stay glued to him, and grind his big HP bar down faster than he can spin, since A Thousand Cuts loves his health stacking. Just keep your HP topped: a careless trade still hands him a Demacian Justice execute, the one button that beats you all game.","whys":["His Decisive Strike (Q) silences your Snip cast and lands an empowered crit, and with no Hallowed Mist yet you have nothing to make it whiff — last-hit at Q range and never dash in.","He out-stats you and his passive regen heals your poke off, and with no champion to hit your E refund is dead — you're too soft to trade even at 2.","E (Skip 'n Slash) lets you poke-and-reset, but his 8s Q-silence into the empowered strike still wins the short trade and he regens the rest.","Your worst window — a pre-mist melee with no untargetability against a bruiser who out-stats you and regens any chip you land.","Hallowed Mist eats his Q engage and Needlework slows him, but his missing-HP true-damage R executes you right back — dead even.","Riftmaker/Nashor's online: %-max-HP Snip and on-hit grind out-trade his short Q-W combo and your E resets let you shove him off plates.","You shred him — %-max-HP magic plus the center snip's true damage ignores his armor and Courage only shaves burst, not your sustained DPS; just dodge his R execute."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"graves","win":["Graves","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Graves","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Your Snip Snip! cone hits as percent-max-HP magic with a true-damage center snip, so you can contest the first wave before Graves has Quickdraw up to dash away and kite."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Graves's window: Quickdraw gives him a dash plus True Grit armor, and his two-shell burst auto plus a Smoke Screen slow lets him zone you off the wave before you have any Hallowed Mist to hide in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it — drop W as he Quickdraws in, slow him with R, and his short-range pellets have to fight you inside a fog where he's locked out of targeting you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online: Skip 'n Slash's refund keeps your on-hit autos and %-HP Q rolling, out-DPSing his tanky-ADC build in any fight his 16s Quickdraw cannot disengage from."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 6 and bait his Quickdraw engage INTO Hallowed Mist so his short-range pellets fall outside the fog while you keep snipping","Hit your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike, then force extended fights where Skip 'n Slash's cooldown refund and %-HP Q grind him down","Stay clear of his 26s Smoke Screen so he cannot slow and zone you off the wave, and last-hit at the tip of your Q"],"foe":["Use Quickdraw's dash and his move speed to stay at pellet range, kite you out of Hallowed Mist, and burst you with the two-shell reload","Drop Smoke Screen on the wave to slow you and deny your vision, then zone you off CS while you have no untargetability","Spike his Eclipse/tank-ADC items and end trades early, before you reach Level 6 and your first AP item come online"]},"early":"Graves out-stats you levels 1-3 the moment he has Quickdraw — his two-shell burst auto and Smoke Screen slow chip you and zone you off the wave before you ever close to Snip Snip! range, and you have no Hallowed Mist to hide in yet. At Level 1 you can actually contest with your Q cone since his dash isn't up, but once he has Quickdraw to reposition, stop walking into pellet range to throw a Q he can just dash away from. Last-hit at the tip of your Q, eat the minimum poke, and respect that his burst is real before you have any untargetability.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are even but tense — he kites with Quickdraw and slows you with Smoke Screen, but your Q+E poke-and-reset trades back while his shells reload. Smoke Screen is 26s at rank 1, longer than your 22s Mist, so once he spends it you get a full mist cycle he cannot answer. At 6 the lane flips to you: drop Hallowed Mist as he Quickdraws in so his pellets cannot target you, slow him with Needlework, and make a short-range shotgun fight inside the fog. The fog stops his autos, not his skillshots — End of the Line and Collateral Damage still travel.","late":"Once your first AP item lands (Riftmaker or Nashor's into the Blackfire line) you own the extended fight — Skip 'n Slash's cooldown refund keeps your on-hit autos and %-HP Q rolling while his tanky-ADC build just feeds A Thousand Cuts more max-HP to shred and more healing to sustain on. He is a burst-and-disengage threat, so the danger is never the straight 1v1 — it is him Quickdrawing out of your mist and re-engaging on a 16s cooldown. Pin him in fog, slow with R, and do not chase a Graves who has already dashed; let him come back into your mist.","whys":["At Level 1 his Quickdraw dash isn't up, so your Snip Snip! cone with its true-damage center snip can contest the first wave before he can kite — take the early poke trade.","He gets Quickdraw and his two-shell burst auto first — he dashes out of Q range and bursts you while you have no Hallowed Mist to hide behind.","With Quickdraw plus Smoke Screen he owns the trade: he slows you, denies your vision, and dashes off, and you still have no untargetability to punish his commitment.","Even window — your Q+E poke-and-reset trades back while his shells reload, and a spent 26s Smoke Screen is your opening, but his slow-and-kite still answers it.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it — you mist his Quickdraw engage, slow him with R, and his short-range pellets have to fight inside fog where he can't target you.","Your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike beats his item timing — Skip 'n Slash's cooldown refund keeps your %-HP Q and on-hit autos grinding through his tanky-ADC build in any extended fight.","You out-scale his pellets the more he builds HP — A Thousand Cuts shreds his max-HP and heals you off it, so pin him in mist and the extended duel is yours."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"heimerdinger","win":["Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"His turret beam plus Hextech Micro-Rockets poke you off the wave before you have W's untargetability — his hardest zone window, so just soak XP."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework slow + Hallowed Mist: dash E onto him and drop the fog — turrets are stationary and cannot enter it, so the nest can never target you again."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online — %-max-HP Snip Snip! and on-hit E let you dive past the turrets and burst him inside one mist window."},{"when":"Late","text":"If you let it scale, his full turret nest plus rocket poke out-zones your engage from range — close the lane before the map opens up."}],"wants":{"you":["Sidestep the grenade and rockets to reach W range, then dash E onto him inside its flat 11s cooldown","Hit Level 6 and sit in Hallowed Mist so his turret beams and rockets can't target you while Needlework slows his kite","Spike Riftmaker/Nashor's and all-in through the turret nest with %-HP Snip Snip! and on-hit E"],"foe":["Wall you off the minions with turrets and chip you with Hextech Micro-Rockets and beam range","Land his lightning grenade to stun you before you dash and reset the turret zone before you reach mist","Stall lane and stack his turret nest so he out-ranges your all-in by mid-game"]},"early":"Heimerdinger owns the opening — his turrets wall you off the minions and Hextech Micro-Rockets plus the lightning grenade chip you down long before you have Hallowed Mist to hide in. With no W untargetability and no real all-in pre-6, you just eat poke if you walk up to last-hit under his beams. Soak XP at max range, grab the minions you can reach without diving the turret, and do NOT facecheck the grenade — it is a flat 11s, it stuns you before you can dash, and it resets the whole zone. This is a survival window, not a trade window.","mid":"By 4-5 you can contest if you bait the 11s grenade and dash E onto him while it is down — but he rebuilds the turret wall fast, so do not overstay. Level 6 is where it flips: Needlework gives you a slow to stick through his kite, and Hallowed Mist answers his whole zone. Turrets are stationary, so they can never enter your fog, which means they can never re-acquire you — drop W on top of him and snip while the nest shoots nothing. Force the all-in in the window right after his grenade; that is your real opening.","late":"Your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike is the moment to end it — %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus on-hit E lets you dive straight through the turret nest and burst him inside one mist window, and the cooldown refund on E keeps you on him. Let the game go long and his full nest plus rocket poke out-zones your engage from range, kiting you out of every fight before you close. This lane is even, but evenness rots in his favour the longer it runs — take the kill the moment your first item completes, then group and deny him a fortified nest on objectives.","whys":["No W yet and no all-in — his turret plus the lightning grenade poke you off the wave while you can only soak XP at max range.","His rockets and turret beam out-range everything you have at level 2; stepping up to last-hit just feeds him free poke.","With Q+E you can dash in inside the 11s grenade gap, but he rebuilds the turret wall fast — it is a coinflip trade window.","Lane-control window: trade around his 11s grenade and bank small leads, but neither of you can hard-commit yet.","Needlework slows his kite and his turrets cannot enter Hallowed Mist to target you — drop W on top of him and snip uncontested.","Riftmaker/Nashor's lets %-HP Snip and on-hit E dive past the nest and burst him inside one mist window, with E refunding for the chase.","Even on paper, but his full turret nest plus rocket poke out-zones your engage if the game runs long — you have to close it first."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"illaoi","win":["Illaoi","Illaoi","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Illaoi's biggest window — she out-stats you with raw base damage and a landed E (Test of Spirit) yanks your spirit out, spawning tentacles that chunk your soft, item-less HP. Do not stand for a Test of Spirit and do not trade into her tentacles."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework's slow plus your full Q-W-E kit lets you sit inside Hallowed Mist on top of her: the armor/MR and untargetability to her autos and E-grab let you out-DPS her slams while Snip Snip! grinds, so the duel finally flips your way."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online: Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP magic and true-damage center out-grind her huge HP-and-tentacle sustain, and your anti-heal cuts the lifesteal she gets from slamming you."},{"when":"Late","text":"The tankier she builds the harder your max-HP passive and Q shred her, and she has zero mobility — so close fights on your terms and never get walked onto a fresh tentacle field with her ult up."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive levels 1-3 farming with the tip of Snip Snip! and never stand still for a 16s Test of Spirit (E) that turns you into a Vessel","At 6, fight from inside Hallowed Mist so its armor/MR and untargetability blank her autos and E while your Q out-DPSes her tentacle slams","Buy anti-heal and rush Riftmaker so your %-HP + true-damage Q out-sustains her slam lifesteal in extended fights"],"foe":["Land E (Test of Spirit) to rip your spirit and spawn chasing tentacles, forcing you off the lane before your kit comes online","Close with a 4s Harsh Lesson dash, then ult to ground your escape so every slam lands","Out-stat and out-sustain you levels 1-3 with raw base damage before your W and items exist"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are hers and you have to respect it — Illaoi out-stats you on raw base damage, and a landed Test of Spirit (E, 16s at rank 1) rips your spirit out so tentacles spawn and chase you while you have no W and no items to soak the hits. Spacing alone will not save you: Harsh Lesson is a 4s dash that also resets her auto, so she closes the gap herself and the swing wind-up, not the cast, is your tell. Last-hit with the tip of Snip Snip!, dodge the E, and settle for safe last-hits over poke you cannot afford.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay dicey — you are a melee with no mist uptime against her field, so keep farming and dodging her 16s E while you wait for 6. Everything flips at 6: Needlework gives you a slow, and your full Q-W-E lets you fight from inside Hallowed Mist on top of her, where her autos and Harsh Lesson cannot target you and you out-DPS the slams. The hard rule is Leap of Faith: it GROUNDS you, so Skip 'n Slash is disabled while it is up. Spend your dash before she ults, never after — once she has, you are staying in that tentacle field whether you like it or not.","late":"This is your house. Snip Snip!'s percent-max-HP magic plus its true-damage centre ignore the armour and HP she stacks, so the tankier she builds the harder you shred her — and she has zero escape once you dash onto her. Carry Grievous Wounds to cut the lifesteal she gets off slamming you, fight inside your mist so her autos and Harsh Lesson whiff, and never let her Leap of Faith you on a full tentacle field: the grounding takes your dash away and you cannot leave. Close fights on your terms and her total immobility loses every time.","whys":["Illaoi out-stats you at level 1 and your item-less HP can't survive a Test of Spirit grab plus the tentacles it spawns — farm, don't fight.","She still owns this window: her E pulls your spirit and chases you with tentacles while you have no W up to make yourself untargetable to her.","With Q+E you poke and reset, but she is ahead until your mist is online — commit only after a 16s Test of Spirit whiffs.","You're a melee with no mist uptime versus her tentacle field, so it's a coinflip on who lands cooldowns — keep dodging her E.","At 6 you fight inside Hallowed Mist on top of her: it blanks her autos and Harsh Lesson while Needlework slows and your Q out-DPSes the slams — but Leap of Faith grounds your dash.","Riftmaker plus anti-heal let your %-HP and true-damage Snip Snip! out-sustain the lifesteal she gets from slamming you in any extended duel.","The more HP and armor she stacks the harder your max-HP passive and magic Q shred her, and her zero mobility means she can't escape your dash-in all-in."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"irelia","win":["Skill","Irelia","Skill","Irelia","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Irelia's window — with Q up and minions to surf, Bladesurge dashes onto you and her passive stacks shred faster than your level-1 Snip Snip! can answer, so don't melee-trade before you have W."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus W flips it: drop Hallowed Mist the instant her Flawless Duet stun blades are in flight, R-slow her inside the fog, and snip her down while her Q has nothing to reset to."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online — your %-max-HP Snip Snip! and on-hit out-damage her, and Skip 'n Slash refunds let you stay sticky through her Bladesurge resets in any fight dragged into the mist."},{"when":"Late","text":"Roughly even teamfight scaling, but a fed Irelia Bladesurge-chains through your backline; keep Hallowed Mist on yourself so she can't target you from outside it and snip whoever she dives."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach 6 and bait her 16s Flawless Duet, then drop W as the blades land so the all-in whiffs","Stand inside Hallowed Mist so Irelia must dash in to touch you — Bladesurge resets from outside the cloud can't target you","Stack %-max-HP Snip Snip! and on-hit, healing off the damage to out-sustain her passive-fed reset duel"],"foe":["Get Bladesurge a minion to reset on so she can dash in and stick to you before you have mist","Land Flawless Duet (E) to stun AND ground you, locking out both your W and your dash","Stack Ionian Fervor shred and time Defiant Dance (W) to eat your Q burst, then snowball off an early kill"]},"early":"Both of you are soft at level 1, but Irelia edges the early levels because Bladesurge resets off the minion wave — a 10s cooldown that refunds on every kill — let her dash in, stick, and heal off each reset before you have any mist. Do not melee-trade Snip Snip! when her Q is up and the wave is low. Last-hit at the tip of your cone, tag her with the true-damage centre snip when she walks up, and respect Flawless Duet (E, 16s): it stuns AND grounds, so Skip 'n Slash stays disabled even after the stun ends. Hold your trades until 6.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still hers if you have not hit 6 — Ionian Fervor shred plus a well-timed Defiant Dance (W, 20s) eats your Q burst, so she wins the extended reset duel. The lane flips at 6, and the whole fight is the W timing: drop Hallowed Mist the instant her Flawless Duet blades are out or as she Bladesurges in, so she must stand inside the cloud to hit you. Her E is 16s and your Mist is 22s, so you do not get a fog for every stun — bait it rather than react to it, because the grounding takes your dash too. Then R-slow, snip, and heal it back.","late":"This scales out roughly even — neither of you hard out-scales the other, so it stays a skirmish lane into teamfights. Your %-max-HP Snip Snip! and on-hit punish any bruiser HP she stacks, Grievous Wounds cuts the health Bladesurge refunds her on every reset, and mist nullifies her dive whenever you are the target she has to reach. The danger is a fed Irelia Bladesurge-chaining through your backline: keep Hallowed Mist on yourself, never get caught by a flanking Flawless Duet, and snip whoever she commits onto.","whys":["Both of you are weak level 1 and neither can commit — stack snips on the wave and tag her with the true-damage center when she steps up to farm.","Bladesurge resets off the minion wave here — she dashes in and sticks before you have mist, so don't melee-trade into her passive shred.","You get Q+E to poke-and-reset, but a 20s Defiant Dance still eats your burst and her Ionian Fervor shred answers — a coin-flip skirmish.","Without W yet you're a melee with no untargetability into her reset chain, and her passive shred out-trades you outright.","Needlework plus a full kit lets you W-mist her Flawless Duet so the all-in whiffs, then R-slow and snip her down while her Q has nothing to reset onto.","Riftmaker's %-HP Snip, Skip 'n Slash refunds and Grievous Wounds out-sustain the healing her resets give her — force the fight into your fog and win it.","Neither out-scales the other into teamfights; keep mist on yourself and snip whoever she Bladesurges onto to keep it a fair fight."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"jax","win":["Skill","Jax","Jax","Skill","Skill","Jax","Jax"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Snip Snip!'s percent-max-HP cone with its true-damage center snip is your only poke before you scale, so chip him on the wave — but his autos and base stats win a straight stand-still trade, so never sit in his range to throw it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework is your one clear window: drop Hallowed Mist, bait his Q-leap-and-E into the fog so the Counter Strike stun whiffs while you stay untargetable, slow him with R, and out-sustain the brawl off your ability healing."},{"when":"Jax 1st item","text":"His Counter Strike stun into Trinity/Blade burst is the lane's scariest moment — his Empower auto-reset is the tell, and once the stun lands the follow-up all-in out-stats you even with mist down."},{"when":"Late","text":"Riftmaker brings your %-HP Snip and Thousand Cuts online to shred his stacked durability, but his R defensive stats and Counter Strike dodge still let him choose the fight — only ever commit standing inside your own mist."}],"wants":{"you":["Wait out Jax's E (Counter Strike) — either side-step so the stun whiffs or trade only after it expires, then Skip 'n Slash in and Snip his HP through the dodge window","Hit Level 6 and drag every all-in into Hallowed Mist so his leap-and-stun engage whiffs while you snip and slow him with Needlework","Stack anti-heal and Riftmaker, then grind down his R-stacked durability with %-HP Snip and Thousand Cuts in extended fights inside the fog"],"foe":["Bait your autos into Counter Strike so the stun lands, then Leap Strike in with Empower's reset","Q-leap in and Counter Strike burst when you are caught outside mist range or stepping up to last-hit","Hit his Trinity Force spike and pop R's defensive stats to take over every committed duel on open ground"]},"early":"\"Your Q, Snip Snip!, is the whole early game — the cone deals percent-max-HP magic and the center snip is true damage, so chip him on the wave when you can step up safely. But do not throw it inside his auto range: the moment you commit, Jax pops E, Counter Strike, dodges your autos, stuns you, then Q-leaps and bursts you while you are pinned. Your W (Hallowed Mist) untargetability only matters if you are standing in it, and at level 1-2 you cannot brawl through his base stats anyway — so last-hit, throw the long snip on his approach, and accept you lose the straight stat-check levels 1-3.\"","mid":"\"Levels 4-5 stay rough — you have Hallowed Mist and Skip 'n Slash to reposition, but pre-Riftmaker he can Leap Strike straight back onto you. Counter Strike only dodges basic attacks: Snip Snip! lands through it in full, so keep the cone on him and hold your autos until the counterattack stun has fired. The flip is Level 6 and Needlework: drop W as he commits so his stun and Empower auto get eaten while you stay untargetable to anything outside the fog, slow him with R, and out-heal him off your ability sustain. His E is 17s at rank 1 — that gap is your step-up.\"","late":"\"Once Riftmaker lands, your %-HP Snip and Thousand Cuts shred whatever durability his R and items pile on, and a clean mist fight is winnable. The problem is he picks the moment: Counter Strike still dodges your autos and his R grants huge defensive stats on demand, so an even-items Jax out-duels you on open ground. Only ever commit with Hallowed Mist down under your feet and the fight dragged into the fog — never get caught split-pushing in the open where he can Q-leap onto you with no mist to stand in.\"","whys":["His E (Counter Strike) isn't up to start, so you can Snip his HP on the wave — but his base stats and autos match your level-1 stat-check, so it's a wash.","Counter Strike dodges autos, never Snip Snip! — snip through it, hold your autos, and walk out before the counterattack stun fires.","He has his full Q-W-E engage and you have no Riftmaker yet — he out-stats every all-in and your Skip 'n Slash dash can't escape his gap-close.","This is his pre-spike window: he soaks your whole trade on Counter Strike and Q-leaps back in while you have nothing but mist to hide behind.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it — bait his Q-leap-and-E into the fog so the stun whiffs, slow him with R, and out-sustain off your ability healing.","His Trinity Force stun-and-burst spike outpaces your first item — a single landed Counter Strike on your volley is a lost trade.","Even with Riftmaker shredding his HP, his Counter Strike dodge and R defensive stats let him pick the duel on open ground — only fight inside mist."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"jayce","win":["Jayce","Jayce","Jayce","Jayce","Gwen","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Jayce's window. His cannon-form Shock Blast fired through the Acceleration Gate out-ranges everything you have before Hallowed Mist, so don't trade back, just farm at max range and eat the chip."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework comes online and you finally have Hallowed Mist. Drop W on yourself so his poke whiffs while you're untargetable, then E-dash in, snip him, and chain R to slow his escape."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker or Nashor's: if you force one extended fight inside mist, %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus your ability healing out-sustain anything he has, since Jayce builds no lifesteal."},{"when":"Late","text":"Knife's edge. Touch him inside mist and Snip Snip!'s true-damage center snip plus your all-in deletes a squishy Jayce, but a fed Jayce just pokes from gate range and never lets you close."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive levels 1-3 last-hitting at the tip of your range, out of a 16s Shock Blast's empowered poke, until you have Hallowed Mist","Hit 6, then drop W to go untargetable through his poke and E-dash onto him so his hammer-form Thundering Blow knockback has nothing to peel","Scale to Riftmaker/Nashor's where %-max-HP Snip Snip! and your ability sustain win the extended duel a no-lifesteal Jayce cannot kite forever"],"foe":["Poke you down with Shock Blast through the Acceleration Gate before you ever reach E-dash or mist range","Swap with Mercury Cannon into a 20s Thundering Blow to knock you away as you E in, then gate-speed out","Keep the lane long and roam on his gate mobility, denying you the committed melee fight where your mist and sustain win"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are his. You have no Hallowed Mist yet, no untargetability, and only a short-range Snip Snip! cone, so his cannon-form Shock Blast fired through the Acceleration Gate pokes you off the wave for free. Do not try to trade back, his poke out-ranges you and he just gate-speeds away from any step-up. Last-hit at the very tip of your range, accept the chip, and stay healthy, his poke alone can't kill you if you don't walk into a hammer-form Thundering Blow all-in.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still rough, you're a melee with no mist eating ranged poke pre-spike. But level 6 flips it. With Needlework up and Hallowed Mist available, drop W on top of yourself to become untargetable to his poke, then E-dash in with the on-hit range bonus and snip him while your healing tops you back up. Chain R so he cannot gate away, and hitting him with E refunds most of the dash. Watch the Mercury Cannon swap, not the hammer cast — it is a 6s auto reset and it is your only warning that a 20s Thundering Blow knockback is coming, so bait it before you commit.","late":"It stays a knife's edge. The instant you touch him inside your mist, Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP damage and its true-damage center snip plus your all-in delete him, he's squishy and builds no lifesteal to out-trade your sustain. The problem is a fed Jayce never lets you touch him. His Shock Blast window shrinks from 16s at rank 1 to 6s at max, so the gap you are hunting closes as the game runs — use mist to cross the poke early, let your team eat the harass, and land the one E-dash combo before that window is gone.","whys":["No Hallowed Mist yet, so his Shock Blast through the Acceleration Gate pokes you for free and your Snip Snip! cone can't answer from melee range.","Still soft with one ability, his cannon-stance poke out-ranges you and he gate-speeds back from any step-up you try.","You can contest with Q and E, but his 16s Shock Blast still out-ranges you and gate mobility resets the spacing before you arrive.","Worst window for you, a melee with no untargetability against his Shock Blast poke and still no item online.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist lets you go untargetable to his poke, E-dash in, and chain R's slow, this level-6 window is your fight.","Riftmaker/Nashor's: %-max-HP Snip Snip! and your ability sustain win any extended duel, but he can still poke-and-gate to keep the lane even.","Your mist all-in with the true-damage center snip one-shots a squishy Jayce on contact, but a fed Jayce just pokes from gate range and never commits."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"karma","win":["Karma","Karma","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Karma has Mantra from level 1, her Focused Resolve tether roots you on a flat 12s, and her raw Q outranges your whole kit — with no Hallowed Mist yet to go untargetable, this is her biggest free-poke window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"With Needlework, your full Q-W-E online, and Hallowed Mist ranked, E onto her and drop W so her targeted Focused Resolve cannot pick you, then out-sustain the Q war through A Thousand Cuts — the lane flips even-to-yours here."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online: %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus on-hit shred chew through her squishy bar once you close, and your ability healing eats her Q chip in a drawn-out trade."},{"when":"Late","text":"Karma's empowered RE shield-bomb and Mantra poke let her shield allies and disengage in skirmishes, so she scales as a teamfight enchanter — you only win the side-lane 1v1, where you catch her E shield on cooldown."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 6 with Hallowed Mist ranked and drop W so her targeted Focused Resolve tether cannot pick you at all","E onto her with the bonus on-hit range to land Snip Snip! and heal back her chip through Thousand Cuts before she can E away","Scale to Riftmaker — your %-max-HP Q and on-hit shred melt her low HP bar the moment you finally close the gap"],"foe":["Land max-range Q poke every wave and back off before you can E-in to trade","Land the Focused Resolve tether for a 12s root, Mantra it to heal and extend, and chunk you while you are stuck","Use a 10s Inspire shield and its move speed to disengage your all-in and reset the poke war from range"]},"early":"Karma owns the first few levels — Inner Flame outranges everything you have, she has Mantra from level 1, and her Focused Resolve tether roots you on a flat 12s, so eat the minimum poke and farm with the tip of your Q rather than walking up. Do not E-trade at 1-3; her Q chips you faster than A Thousand Cuts heals it back, and she just Inspire-shields and walks away. Last-hit at max range and respect that a landed Focused Resolve root can set up a jungle gank you cannot dash out of.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still a poke-soak — you are a melee with no untargetability and her Q keeps you honest — but at 6 the lane evens out. With Needlework and Hallowed Mist ranked, E in and drop W: she cannot target you from outside the fog, which hard-answers her Focused Resolve tether. The fog is untargetability, not vision — a Mantra-Q cataclysm under your feet still lands. Sidestep the tether or body-block it; once you are on her she has only Inspire's move speed.","late":"Once Riftmaker is online your %-max-HP Snip plus on-hit shred deletes her low HP bar the moment you close, and A Thousand Cuts healing eats her chip in extended duels. The catch is her uptime: Inspire is only 10s at rank 1, so 'catch her shield down' is a narrow window, and Gathering Fire means every ability she lands pulls her 40s Mantra forward. Carry Grievous Wounds — a Mantra-W heals her mid-tether. Force the all-in through your Mist in the side lane: she scales as a teamfight enchanter, you scale as a 1v1 duelist.","whys":["Karma's Q outranges your entire kit and her 12s Focused Resolve tether roots you — she pokes for free and you cannot trade back yet.","Still no Hallowed Mist to go untargetable and her Q chip out-paces your passive heal — farm, do not fight, and dodge the tether.","You finally have Q+E to threaten a reset, but her E shield and the move speed it grants let her disengage before you commit — it evens out.","You're a melee soaking poke before your W is ranked, but anti-heal and on-hit mean one clean E-in trade keeps it level.","Needlework plus a ranked Hallowed Mist flips it — inside the fog her targeted tether cannot pick you, so snip her down with no escape for her.","Riftmaker's %-max-HP Snip and on-hit shred melt her squishy bar once you close, and your ability healing wins the sustain war.","She out-disengages you late — a 10s Inspire is nearly always up and Gathering Fire pulls her Mantra forward, so catching her shield down is a coin-flip."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"kassadin","win":["Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Kassadin","Kassadin"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Kassadin has no waveclear and no pre-6 mobility, so perma-shove with Snip Snip! and E in to snip him off every last hit — your %-HP Q chunks him and the center snip's true damage ignores his passive magic reduction."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Riftwalk (R) is a 5s blink at rank 1 that lets him hop out of your E-W-Q the instant you commit — fight inside Hallowed Mist and bait the blink rather than forcing a clean fan of Needlework."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Riftmaker/Nashor's two-item spike still out-duels a one-item Kassadin if you catch him with R down or before his Tear/RoA stacks finish — but his blink makes every all-in a coinflip now."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Tear plus two AP items drop Riftwalk to 2s and turn it into a spammable blink-Force-Pulse burst — he shields on Null Sphere, blinks before your passive grinds him, and out-ranges your pin."}],"wants":{"you":["Perma-shove with Snip Snip! to deny his CS and zone him off the wave while he's escape-less and meleeable pre-6","All-in with E gap-close into Hallowed Mist before level 6 — his only out is walking, and the center-snip true damage cuts his magic reduction","End the lane on plates and a CS lead before his Tear/Rod of Ages stacks and second AP item come online"],"foe":["Survive to 6, stack Rod of Ages and Tear charges, and farm safely under tower without giving you a kill","Use a 5s Riftwalk to blink out of your E-W-Q all-in and bleed your Hallowed Mist timer before re-engaging on his terms","Reach 2+ items where a 2s Riftwalk into Force Pulse burst deletes you faster than your %-HP autos can grind him down"]},"early":"Kassadin is one of the weakest early champs in the game and you punish that hard — he has no waveclear and no mobility until Riftwalk at 6, so shove with Snip Snip! and E in to snip him every time he walks up for a last hit. Your %-max-HP Q out-trades him and the centre snip's true damage cuts through his passive magic reduction, while Skip 'n Slash refunds on hit so you poke and reposition for free. His one answer is Nether Blade, a 7s auto reset that also refunds his mana, so read the swing wind-up. Deny CS, take a plate, stack the lead.","mid":"At 6 the lane changes character: Riftwalk is a 5s blink at rank 1 that lets him hop out the instant you commit E-W-Q, so the clean all-ins you landed at 1-5 stop connecting for free. Your answer is to fight inside Hallowed Mist and bait the blink — make him burn R, then catch the Needlework slow while it is down and his mana is gone. You still edge the straight duel through your two-item spike if you catch him with R down or before his Tear and Rod of Ages finish, so keep forcing trades and shoving for plates. This is your last window to convert the early lead.","late":"This is where you lose — Kassadin is a hard scaler, and once he has Tear plus two AP items Riftwalk drops to 2s and goes near-spammable: he blinks in, shields himself on Null Sphere, dumps Force Pulse, and bursts you before your passive autos can grind him down. You cannot pin him; Hallowed Mist's untargetability stops mattering once he simply blinks the moment your damage starts, and the front of your Q gets softened by his magic reduction. Your only path is the lead you built before 6 — if the lane was even at first item, accept you will be kited, give him no solo kills, and splitpush while your team peels him.","whys":["Kassadin has zero waveclear and no mobility pre-6 — perma-shove with Snip Snip! and chunk him off every last hit; all he can do is soak it.","You gain E to gap-close and reset on hit; he still has no dash until 6, so every step he takes for CS gets punished with a snip.","Your Q out-trades him and the center snip's true damage ignores the magic reduction his passive grants against your kit.","Still no Riftwalk until 6, so he stays escape-less — keep shoving and punish every last hit, but respect his 7s Nether Blade reset.","Once he hits 6 with R up he can blink out of every all-in, so your clean early combos stop landing and the lane flips to even.","His Tear/Rod of Ages stacks and second AP item start to out-tempo your two-item spike, and the blink makes any pin a coinflip.","He out-scales you outright: Tear plus two AP items let his blink-Q-Force-Pulse combo burst you, and you can't pin a champion who blinks on demand."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"kayle","win":["Gwen","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Kayle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Kayle is a melee, no-escape stub with terrible waveclear here — walk up and land the Snip Snip! cone to chunk her before she has any tools to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Skip 'n Slash in, drop Hallowed Mist on yourself, and all-in: she can pop Divine Judgment, but at rank 1 that is a 160-second cooldown and it expires in seconds — Needlework's slow keeps her in the mist to finish."},{"when":"1st item (Riftmaker/Nashor's)","text":"Your %-max-HP Q plus the untargetable mist out-duel a Kayle whose Nashor's-form power isn't online yet — this is your last clean kill window before she scales."},{"when":"Lvl 11 + 2 items","text":"Kayle's level-11 ranged autos and AoE waveclear out-range Hallowed Mist and let her kite your dash forever — past this point the lane flips to her permanently."}],"wants":{"you":["Bully her meleed early game (Lvl 1-3) with the Snip Snip! cone before her ranged form and Q upgrades arrive","Hit your Lvl 6 + Riftmaker spike and force the all-in inside Hallowed Mist while she is still a weak duelist","Crash plates and snowball a lead so her level-11/16 scaling never gets to matter"],"foe":["Farm safely under tower and dodge the Snip Snip! cone until she reaches Lvl 11 ranged form","Pop Divine Judgment (160s at rank 1) to blank your all-in and reset the trade","Reach 2 items and her ranged upgrades, where she out-ranges your mist and kites you down before you reach her"]},"early":"\"This is the rare lane where Kayle, normally a meleed early-game punching bag, is exactly the victim you want — and you are the bully. At Level 1 you are both soft, but she is a short-range stub with no dash, no escape, and miserable waveclear, so step up and land the Snip Snip! cone to chunk her. By Level 3 with Q + Skip 'n Slash you can poke-and-reset on her every time she steps up to last-hit, and Thousand Cuts heals the return poke back. Do not let her free-farm to safety: every CS she misses is a level-11 spike she hits late.\"","mid":"\"This is your window and you have to use it. At Level 6, Skip 'n Slash in, drop Hallowed Mist on top of yourself so she cannot target you from outside it, and snip her with %-max-HP magic plus the center-snip true damage. Fan Needlework to slow her so she cannot walk out of the cloud. She will pop Divine Judgment for the invulnerability — bait it or simply keep snipping, because it expires and leaves her exposed. Once Riftmaker or Nashor's lands you out-duel her in any extended fight, so force plates and a kill lead here; the clock is entirely against you.\"","late":"\"Be honest with yourself: late game belongs to her. Once Kayle hits her Level 11 ranged form and the Level 16 wave of upgrades, she out-ranges Hallowed Mist entirely — she pokes you down before you ever close to mist range, kites your Skip 'n Slash dash, and Divine Judgment blanks your all-in. Your %-HP kit shreds tanks, but she is not a tank; she is a hypercarry who out-scales even you. Your only answer is to have already won: snowball lane, take her tower, and end before her two-item spike — and never duel her solo once that timer runs out.\"","whys":["You are both weak at Level 1, but who wins the first trade comes down to dodging — land the Snip Snip! cone clean and it's yours, whiff it and her autos punish you back.","She has no dash, no escape, and weak waveclear pre-6; step up and snip her on every last-hit while she has nothing to answer with.","Q + Skip 'n Slash lets you poke-and-reset, and Thousand Cuts heals the return poke; watch her auto wind-up — Starfire Spellblade (E, 8s) is an auto reset.","At Lvl 6 the all-in is yours: mist makes you untargetable, %-HP Q plus true damage shreds her, and Needlework's slow pins her even through the end of Divine Judgment.","Around the first item the lane is a coin-flip — your Riftmaker/Nashor's duel power is real, but if she farmed safe to Lvl 11 her ranged form is arriving and the window is closing.","Two-item ranged-form Kayle out-ranges your Hallowed Mist and kites your dash — once she scales past you, extended fights belong to her.","She is a hypercarry who out-scales even your tank-shredding kit; her Level 16 upgrades and Divine Judgment mean you cannot duel her late — hand her to your team."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"kennen","win":["Kennen","Skill","Skill","Kennen","Gwen","Gwen","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Kennen sits beyond your reach and chips with Q (Thundering Shuriken), stacking Mark of the Storm with autos before you have W mist or E to answer — last-hit at the tip and eat the poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus your full kit flips it: E-dash in, drop Hallowed Mist as his stun lands so he loses untargeted follow-up, and Snip Snip him while he's stuck in melee with no kite."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online — E-gap onto a squishy Kennen with Grievous up and percent-max-HP Snip plus Thousand Cuts on-hits melt him before Lightning Rush kites out."},{"when":"Late","text":"Slicing Maelstrom (R) is a flat 120s at every rank; its AoE stun plus passive move speed resets spacing in 5v5s, so he refuses the 1v1 you are built to win and reclaims the lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive to 6, then E-dash into Hallowed Mist range and Snip Snip him while his energy bar forces him to stand and fight instead of kiting","Bait his R stun or Lightning Rush (E), drop W as it lands, then E-gap and all-in with Grievous Wounds up before his ult comes back","Hold E to close his Q poke gap, never to chase — one whiffed dash and he Lightning-Rushes free and resumes chipping you with Thundering Shuriken"],"foe":["Poke you down with Q (Thundering Shuriken) from max range and stack Mark of the Storm before you ever reach the mist","Land Q into auto-empowered W (Electrical Surge) to detonate three Mark stacks for the stun, then chain R (Slicing Maelstrom) to burst you out","Kite with energy sustain and passive move speed, refusing every melee trade until his ult resets the spacing"]},"early":"Kennen owns these levels and it is damage control, not trading. Thundering Shuriken (Q, 7s at rank 1) outranges everything you have, and his autos stack Mark of the Storm toward a stun while you have no mist and no dash at 1 — you are a melee eating poke on every creep. Do not throw the Snip Snip! cone at a kiter who will never sit in it; last-hit at the tip and accept the chip. Your out is that A Thousand Cuts plus your ability healing means his energy poke cannot out-DPS your sustain if you bank levels, so farm to 6 and refuse to int into a three-stack stun.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — a pre-mist melee getting kited, and a clean Thundering Shuriken into Electrical Surge (W, 13s) detonates three Marks and chunks you out of lane. At 6 it flips: E-dash in, drop Hallowed Mist exactly as his stun or Lightning Rush (E, 10s) lands so you go untargetable through the follow-up, and Snip Snip him while he is stuck in melee. Bait Slicing Maelstrom — with a flat 120-second ult and his dash down he has no disengage, and %-max-HP Q plus Thousand Cuts on-hits grind out the fight he cannot kite away from.","late":"Your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike is real — with Grievous up you E-gap onto a squishy Kennen and burst him with %-HP Snip plus the true-damage center before Lightning Rush (E, 10s) kites out, so close on that mid-game window. Late he reclaims it: Slicing Maelstrom is an AoE stun on a passive-move-speed kite kit, so in a 5v5 he peels you, resets the spacing, and denies the 1v1 you are built to win. Force the all-in while his R's flat 120 seconds and his E are down, before teamfights make his range matter more than your dueling.","whys":["No mist, no E — Kennen sits at range and pokes you with Thundering Shuriken (Q, 7s at rank 1) while his autos stack Mark of the Storm, and you walk up for every last-hit.","He keeps Thundering Shuriken and auto-empowered Electrical Surge (W, 13s) up and keeps kiting; you still have no untargetability and cannot punish his spacing, so chip and Mark stacks build.","With Q and E online you can poke-and-reset and threaten a trade if he steps up, but his ranged Thundering Shuriken still trades even — it is a coin flip on who commits first.","Pre-6 you are a mist-less melee against a kiter: Thundering Shuriken into Electrical Surge lands his third Mark, and that stun is the worst window you face.","Needlework plus your full kit lets you E in, drop Hallowed Mist as his stun lands so you go untargetable through the follow-up, and Snip Snip him down in melee he cannot escape.","Your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike wins the extended duel, but Lightning Rush (E, 10s) carries him out — it is even unless you land a clean E-gap with Grievous up.","Slicing Maelstrom (R, a flat 120s) is an AoE stun on a passive-move-speed kite kit — he peels you off and resets the spacing once the game goes 5v5."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"kled","win":["Skill","Kled","Gwen","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Kled"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Mounted Kled out-stats you early: Bear Trap on a Rope (Q, 11s) pulls you in and Violent Tendencies (W, 13s) shreds you over four fast attacks before you have mist or an E reset — just last-hit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it: bait his Bear Trap or Chaaaaaaaarge!!! engage, drop W untargetable as he commits so the on-hits whiff, then snip him off Skaarl into his frail dismounted form."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's is your peak: %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus your heal-on-damage out-sustains a dismounted Kled, whose courage must rebuild before he can remount and re-engage."},{"when":"Late","text":"Kled out-scales at 2+ items: Skaarl's HP regenerates between fights and Bear Trap + Violent Tendencies + Chaaaaaaaarge!!! flanks let him re-engage repeatedly, so force the all-in before he's fully online."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Bear Trap on a Rope, then E in and drop Hallowed Mist as his Violent Tendencies on-hits land so the trade whiffs from inside the fog","Snip Snip! him once he is dismounted — his Q becomes Pocket Pistol, a knockback, so he can no longer yank you in","Hit Level 6 and your first item, then force extended duels his front-loaded mounted kit can't sustain"],"foe":["Land Bear Trap on a Rope to drag you out of mist range and burst you with mounted on-hits before your E resets","Win the level 1-3 mounted skirmish while you're soft with no W mist and no E mobility","Survive your mid-game spike and out-scale you on Skaarl HP regen and Violent Tendencies into 2+ items"]},"early":"Kled owns the first levels — mounted, his Bear Trap on a Rope pulls you in and his Violent Tendencies on-hits out-stat a Gwen who has no Hallowed Mist and no E dash to escape yet. Do not contest the early skirmish: last-hit at the tip of Snip Snip! and eat a little poke, because his mounted all-in is far scarier than yours right now. The one thing to track is Bear Trap on a Rope — if it's on cooldown he can't pull you, and that's the only window you even think about trading in.","mid":"This is where it flips. With Q-W-E online you stop running and start punishing: bait his engage — the Bear Trap pull, Jousting (E, 13s), or his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! ult — and drop Hallowed Mist exactly as he commits so his on-hits whiff while you stay untargetable from outside the fog and keep snipping. The dismount is your gold mine: once you snip his courage out and he is knocked off Skaarl his Q becomes Pocket Pistol, a knockback that cannot yank you, and Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP and true-damage center shred his foot form while your heal-on-damage tops you back up. At 6, Needlework's slow keeps him in the brawl you now win.","late":"Your mid game is the window — close it. Kled is a hard scaler: as he stacks items Skaarl's HP regenerates back between fights and Violent Tendencies plus his remount aggression let him re-engage on top of you over and over, and his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! ult gives him a flank your mist can't fully cover. Take plates and snowball off your first-item duel; if the game drags to two-plus items, group with your mist for teamfights and stop dueling him in a side lane where he can pull you in and burst you down before your E resets.","whys":["Mounted Kled's Bear Trap on a Rope pull and Violent Tendencies on-hits out-stat a level-1 Gwen with no Hallowed Mist and no E reset — just last-hit.","You pick up a real ability rank but are still soft with no mist; farm unless Bear Trap on a Rope is on its 11-second cooldown.","Q-and-E lets you poke-and-reset, and once you snip Kled off Skaarl his frail dismounted form melts to your %-max-HP and true-damage Snip Snip!.","You out-trade a Kled who has burned Bear Trap — bait the 11s pull, E in behind it and snip him off Skaarl.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist beats his all-in: drop W untargetable as his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! or mounted dash commits and the on-hits whiff while you keep snipping.","Riftmaker/Nashor's is your peak — %-max-HP Snip and heal-on-damage win the extended duel his front-loaded mounted kit can't.","Kled out-scales: Skaarl HP regen and Violent Tendencies ramp at 2+ items and Chaaaaaaaarge!!! flanks your mist — close the game before this."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"ksante","win":["Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Q+E online: chunk his big HP bar with %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus the true-damage center (ignores his armour), then E-reset out inside Path Maker's 14-second cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist: when he charges Path Maker or commits his Q knock-up, drop mist and go untargetable so his engage whiffs, then R-slow and chase as Thousand Cuts heals you off his HP."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's is your peak — %-max-HP Snip Snip scales with every armor stack he buys, and your mist's bonus armor/MR outlasts Path Maker's brief damage-reduction window in extended plate trades."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"K'Sante's window: All Out knocks you out of Hallowed Mist and strips his own resists for a fast, isolated 1v1 where his scaled fighter form out-duels your AP."}],"wants":{"you":["Drag every fight into Hallowed Mist so his Q knock-up and All Out reposition whiff while you snip him untargetable","Stack %-max-HP Snip Snip plus the center true-damage snip to melt his giant HP bar straight through his armor","Use E's attack speed and cooldown refund to poke-reset while Path Maker is down, then bank plates before he stacks tank items"],"foe":["Land the second Ntofo Strikes stack to pull you in, or eat your trade behind Path Maker, then commit once your mist is down","Use All Out to knock you clean out of Hallowed Mist, isolating you for the resist-shredded 1v1","Survive your mid-game and scale into 2+ items where his tank-fighter form out-duels your AP"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are even-ish: you are a clunky melee with a cone Q and no mist, while Ntofo Strikes pokes on a flat 3.5s and Path Maker's damage reduction lets him eat your trades — farm with the tip of Snip Snip! and dodge the pull. At 3 with Q+E you start winning: %-max-HP snips chunk his fat HP bar, the center snip is true damage that ignores his armour, and E refunds its cooldown on hit so you poke and reset out before Path Maker's 14 seconds are back. Do not walk into the second Ntofo stack, and do not dump a trade while he is mid-Path Maker charge.","mid":"This is your lane. From 4-6 your percent-HP Q shreds him harder the more HP and armour he stacks, and Thousand Cuts heals it back off his big body. At 6 it flips fully: when he charges Path Maker or lands the Ntofo pull to commit, drop Hallowed Mist and go untargetable so the all-in whiffs, then R-slow and snip him down while E repositions you inside the fog. Bait Path Maker, mist his engage, shove for plates — he cannot burst you through the mist or out-sustain your healing.","late":"Late flips to him and you have to respect it. At 2+ items All Out strips his own armour and MR but turns him into a fast fighter who knocks you clean OUT of Hallowed Mist and isolates you — the one thing mist cannot answer. Note that while he is All Out, Path Maker no longer stuns, so his CC is the R knockback itself. Your %-HP Q still hurts, but his scaled duelist form wins that resist-shredded 1v1. Close the lane in the mid game, group with your shred, and never get caught alone inside All Out range.","whys":["Ntofo Strikes pokes on a flat 3.5s and Path Maker's damage reduction lets him trade back, but you have no mist yet — farm with Q's tip and dodge his pull.","You are still soft pre-W and he eats any trade behind Path Maker; take CS and wait for the Q+E spike rather than fight into his pull.","Q+E online: %-max-HP snips plus the true-damage center melt his HP through his armour, and E resets you out inside Path Maker's 14s.","You out-trade him here — every point of HP and armour he stacks feeds your percent-HP Q while Thousand Cuts heals off his big body.","At 6 you mist his Ntofo pull or Path Maker charge to go untargetable, then R-slow and snip him as he spends his commit on fog.","Riftmaker/Nashor's is your peak — %-HP Snip Snip! ignores his stacked armour and the mist's bonus resists outlast Path Maker's short damage-reduction window.","At 2+ items All Out strips his own resists, knocks you clean out of mist, and his scaled fighter form out-duels your AP."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"lillia","win":["Lillia","Skill","Skill","Lillia","Gwen","Gwen","Lillia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Pure farm phase. Lillia just Q-pokes the wave and chips you with her passive DOT and move speed; neither of you has a kill threat, so last-hit at the tip of Snip Snip! and don't waste E chasing her Swirlseed."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your sore spot: no Hallowed Mist yet, and Blooming Blows (Q, 6s) deals TRUE damage on its outer edge — MR will not save you on the rim. Hold even and wait for 6."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus W flips it: bait or sidestep her R, drop Hallowed Mist when she commits so her sleep/Q burst whiffs, then snip her down while untargetable from outside the cloud."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's is your peak: E's on-hit range and attack speed glue you through her move speed, and %max-HP Q plus your heal-on-damage out-sustains her passive DOT in any extended fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Use E's dash and bonus on-hit range to close her passive/Q move-speed gap, then land a champion hit to refund the cooldown and stay glued through her kite","Drop Hallowed Mist exactly as she commits her R sleep or W slam so the burst whiffs while you keep snipping from untargetable range","Land Snip Snip!'s %max-HP and true-damage center on her squishy HP bar before her DOT chip and stacked move speed force you off"],"foe":["Q-poke the wave and chip you with passive DOT and on-hit move speed before you ever reach mist range","Land the 150-second Lilting Lullaby to set up a DOT-stacked burst, or to disengage the moment you E in","Stack passive move speed and scale so late-game fights happen on her terms, never in a clean 1v1 inside your mist"]},"early":"Lillia plays this like every kiter you hate: she won't stand still for your Q cone, she just Q-pokes the wave from range and chips you with her passive DOT while her on-hit move speed keeps her a step ahead. Don't chase her around the wave burning E; last-hit at the tip of Snip Snip! and accept some chip. The saving grace early is she's squishy and has no real all-in until her R at 6, so a clean E-in when she steps up to Q the wave lets your %max-HP Q and true-damage center punish her before she peels away.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your sore spot: you're a melee with no Hallowed Mist yet against a champ whose whole kit is Q poke, a passive DOT, and move speed, so she pokes you out and you can't pin her. Hold for 6. Once Needlework and Hallowed Mist are up, the lane flips. Bait or sidestep her R sleep, drop the mist as she commits so the burst whiffs while you stay untargetable from outside the cloud, then chunk her with Q. Your heal-on-damage eats her DOT, and the on-hit range and attack speed from E keep you glued to her once you commit.","late":"This is where Lillia reclaims it. She's also a scaler, and her tools are pure mobility: passive and Q/E move speed plus R sleep mean she chooses when fights start and can always peel off your E. You can still win a clean 1v1 inside mist, but she rarely gives you one; she kites in teamfights and uses her AoE R to sleep your whole side before a collapse. Press your first-item spike hard and try to end before her move-speed scaling makes you unable to catch her.","whys":["You're both harmless level 1, but she's the one with passive move speed to disengage and a ranged Q to chip you, so deny what last-hits you can and don't facecheck her Swirlseed.","Neither of you has a real all-in yet; she just pokes the wave with Q and outruns you on passive move speed, so farm at Q tip and save E for a punish, not a chase.","Q+E online and you can punish a step-up, but with no mist yet she just walks away on stacked move speed — hold even and take the CS you are given.","Levels 4-5 are her window: you have no untargetability yet, so she kites your melee with stacked move speed and piles on passive DOT before you ever reach mist range.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it: drop mist as Lilting Lullaby (150s) or her Q lands so the burst whiffs, then snip her from untargetable.","Riftmaker/Nashor's is your peak: %max-HP Q, heal-on-damage, and E's on-hit range out-duel her passive DOT in any fight you can force.","She out-scales the chase: passive and Q/E move speed plus an AoE R sleep let her dictate when every late fight starts, so close the game before that."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"lucian","win":["Lucian","Lucian","Skill","Lucian","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Lucian's Lightslinger double-shot and Piercing Light laser chunk you every time you step up to last-hit, and you have no W untargetability or E reset to trade back — his strongest window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist: bait Relentless Pursuit, go untargetable as he commits autos, then slow-chase him through its 16-second cooldown."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online: your E refunds on champ hit so you stick, and Thousand Cuts on-hits plus Q burst delete his tiny HP bar once you're inside mist."},{"when":"Late","text":"Itemized Lucian still bursts you down if he kites free — never get caught flashless without W up, and fight near a wall so his E dash has nowhere to peel away."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 6 and your first AP item so W untargetability and E stickiness let you finally catch a squishy Lucian","Bait his E dash, then drop Hallowed Mist as he commits so his double-shot and autos whiff on an untargetable you","Build anti-heal and all-in with E gap-close plus R's slow before he can dash back to safety and kite"],"foe":["Poke you with Piercing Light and Lightslinger double-shots before you can reach mist range","Hold Relentless Pursuit (16s at rank 1) and dash out the instant you E in, kiting your melee range","Avoid your all-in, farm safe behind minions, and out-DPS you from range once both teams group"]},"early":"Lucian owns levels 1-3 outright — his Lightslinger passive double-shots and Piercing Light laser chip you every time you step up to CS, and you have no W untargetability or E reset yet to trade back. Don't walk into his auto range to last-hit; soak the wave with your back to the bounce and farm safe. The one comfort is he can't actually all-in and kill you here without an ult — it's chip, not a kill threat, so eat the poke and get to your spike.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay his while you wait on W, but 6 flips it: bait Relentless Pursuit — 16 seconds at rank 1 — then drop Hallowed Mist the instant he commits double-shot or autos so they whiff on an untargetable you, and answer with R's slow plus passive healing. He is a squishy with no escape once that dash is spent, so E in inside the fog with anti-heal up and your on-hits and Q burst end him. Make him spend the dash defensively first, then go.","late":"This is your half of the lane — your scaling and first AP item beat his, and once you reach him your E sticks (it refunds on champ hit) while on-hits and burst chew through his tiny HP bar faster than he can kite. But respect that an itemized Lucian still deletes you in seconds if he gets free space: never get caught flashless without W up, and always fight near a wall so your E gap-close lands and his dash has nowhere to peel away. Close the gap inside the mist and he simply can't out-trade you.","whys":["Lucian's Lightslinger double-shot and Piercing Light laser punish your last-hits while you have no W or E to answer.","He still out-stats you at range — his double-shot and Piercing Light chip you faster than your slow cone Q can trade back.","With Q poke and an E reset you can trade, but Piercing Light (9s) and a 16-second dash he is still holding keep it a coinflip.","Pre-W and pre-item you're a melee eating his poke with no untargetability — his best relative window to chip you out.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist lets you bait Relentless Pursuit, go untargetable as he commits, then slow-chase a dashless Lucian for 16s.","Riftmaker/Nashor's plus your refunding E, on-hits, and Q burst end a squishy Lucian the moment you close inside mist.","You out-scale a no-escape ADC — untargetability and stick beat his kite as long as you fight near walls with W up."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"malphite","win":["Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Gwen","Skill","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"With Q and E both up, you can Snip Snip! his armor-stacked body for %-max-HP magic plus a true-damage center snip, then E in for the auto and refund the dash off the hit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework gives you ranged poke and the takedown-reset chase, and Hallowed Mist means his 130-second R engage brings no teammates in with him."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker or Nashor's Tooth makes extended duels free — every armor item he buys does nothing against your magic Q and only feeds your passive healing off his huge HP bar."},{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Seismic Shard is a flat 8s and Granite Shield absorbs 10% of his max HP, so his poke is real — but your centre snip is true damage, so trade in the gap after his Q."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold Hallowed Mist for his 130-second R engage — he lands inside it and can still hit you, but his four teammates outside cannot","Spam Snip Snip! into his stacked armor — the cast is %-max-HP magic and the center snip is true damage, so Plated Steelcaps and his W armor barely register","Reach your first AP item, where passive healing off his massive HP pool turns every extended trade in your favor"],"foe":["Land Seismic Shard to slow you and steal your move speed before you can E in or reach mist range","Hold R for a flank or for the moment your Hallowed Mist is down, since he loses the straight 1v1","Stack armor and use R to roam and start objectives — his value is teamfight engage, not beating you in lane"]},"early":"Malphite's Seismic Shard poke and his W armor-and-auto-amp are the entire early threat — at levels 1-2 you have no mist, only one rank of Q, and no E mobility, so he can chip you with a move-speed-stealing slow and a beefed-up auto for free. Don't walk up to trade autos into his W. Once you hit 3 and have Q and E together, the lane flips: Snip Snip! is %-max-HP magic damage that his armor stacking does nothing against, and the center snip's true damage ignores Plated Steelcaps entirely. Last-hit with the Q tip, then E in for the auto and refund the dash when his Q is on cooldown.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a touch soft if you have not hit 6 — Seismic Shard is a flat 8s and he can still slow-and-disengage — so farm and trade in short E-reset bursts rather than committing. At 6 the lane is yours: Unstoppable Force is a 130-second location dash, so sidestep it or drop Hallowed Mist as it lands. He arrives inside the mist and can still hit you, but his four teammates outside it cannot, and he has no follow-up once R is spent. Every point of armour he stacks only feeds your magic Q and your healing.","late":"You shred him harder the more he itemises — every armour item is wasted against your %-max-HP magic Q, and your passive heals more off his huge HP bar, so straight 1v1s are free. The catch is Unstoppable Force: a 1000-range dash to a location on a 130-second cooldown, so it is a flank and a roam tool even though he loses your duel. Push your wave, deny the roam, and do not facecheck a missing Malphite near drag — his engage does not need to beat you to swing a fight.","whys":["Seismic Shard (Q, a flat 8s) chips you, but the centre of Snip Snip! is true damage — Granite Shield and armour both read this trade wrong, so you edge it.","He pokes with the move-speed-stealing slow, yet has nothing to punish with until Thunderclap and Ground Slam are both up — step in on the 8s gap.","Q and E online: Snip Snip! is %-max-HP magic and the center snip is true damage, so his armor stacking and Steelcaps do nothing to your trades.","Without 6 you can't punish his R or fully kite the slow — keep to short E-reset trades and don't overcommit before your mist exists.","Needlework's poke plus Hallowed Mist mean his 130-second R engage buys him nothing: his team cannot target you in the fog and he has zero follow-up.","Riftmaker or Nashor's Tooth makes extended duels free — your magic Q ignores his resistances and you heal off his massive HP bar.","You win every 1v1, but Unstoppable Force is a 1000-range location dash that still flanks your team and starts objectives — deny his roam so his armour never matters."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"maokai","win":["Maokai","Maokai","Skill","Maokai","Skill","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Maokai chips you with Sapling Toss (E) and Sap Magic sustain while your six-snip cone Q wastes most of its damage on the wave — his window, soak it and last-hit at the tip."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"With Hallowed Mist and Needlework up, sit in the fog before he commits: Twisted Advance needs a target, so from outside he cannot cast the 14-second root at all — this is where the lane equalizes."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker online: your %-max-HP Snip and true-damage center start shredding his stacked HP faster than Sap Magic can heal it — your one clear edge in the lane."},{"when":"Anytime","text":"A landed Twisted Advance (W, 14s) chains into Bramble Smash knockback plus a sapling pop — that is his only real kill sequence all game, so be standing in your mist before he ever casts it."}],"wants":{"you":["Stand INSIDE Hallowed Mist before he casts — Twisted Advance is a targeted dash, so from outside the fog he cannot pick you at all and the 14s root is wasted","Stack Thousand Cuts and Snip Snip! on his huge tank HP bar — %-max-HP magic plus the true-damage center out-damages every point of Sap Magic sustain","Reach Riftmaker and force extended duels where Needlework ramps and your ability healing eats his sapling chip faster than he regenerates"],"foe":["Land Twisted Advance to drag you out of mist range, then Bramble Smash knockback and pop a sapling before you can E-reset away","Out-sustain your early cone Q with Sap Magic and shove you off CS at levels 1-3 while you have no mist","Stall the game past your Riftmaker window and use his point-and-click root for ganks, objectives, and roam pressure"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are genuinely Maokai's. Sapling Toss (E) and Sap Magic sustain let him win the poke war while your six-snip cone Q wastes most of its damage on the wave and you have no Hallowed Mist yet to safely step up. Do not try to prove anything here — last-hit at the tip of Q, never walk into Twisted Advance (W) range with your E on cooldown, and accept the chip. His root into Bramble Smash knockback is the only thing that kills you this early; respect it completely.","mid":"Levels 4-6 even out as you come online. Once you have Hallowed Mist, stand in it before he commits: Twisted Advance is a targeted dash, so from outside the fog he cannot pick you and the 14-second root never happens. Do not throw damage at the cast either — he is untargetable for the whole dash. At 6, Needlework ramps the longer the brawl goes and your healing chews his big HP bar, so extended fights are fine. Just never get rooted outside the mist with E down; that one sequence still flips the trade to him.","late":"Your one real edge arrives with Riftmaker, where %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus the true-damage center cuts through his stacked armor and HP faster than Sap Magic can heal it. But Maokai never falls off — he stays a tanky root-bot teamfighter with permanent objective and gank pressure off Twisted Advance, so this lane stays even, not won. Push your item-spike windows in the side lane, force the duel when his W is down, and don't expect to hard-shove a tank who builds exactly the HP your Q wants — just out-value him across the game.","whys":["His Sapling Toss and Sap Magic sustain out-poke you while your cone Q whiffs on the wave and you have no mist to step up safely.","You get E for the attack-speed snip window, but he still out-sustains the trade with Sap Magic and contests CS — neither of you owns it yet.","Snip Snip! and your E reset let you contest, but Twisted Advance (W, 14s) and sapling chip keep the lane genuinely even.","Pre-mist you have nothing to deny his saplings, and a landed Twisted Advance into Bramble Smash knockback punishes any overstep.","Hallowed Mist plus Needlework lets you bait his root into the fog and out-sustain the brawl — the fight is a coinflip on his W landing.","Riftmaker turns your %-max-HP Snip and true-damage center loose on his huge HP bar faster than Sap Magic heals it — your one clear window.","He scales as a tanky root-bot who never falls off, so even fully online you out-value him rather than out-stat him."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"mel","win":["Mel","Skill","Gwen","Mel","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q+E online: Skip 'n Slash in, land the true-damage center of Snip Snip, and E refunds off the champ hit so you can dash back out before her Q poke trades back."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Pre-W, pre-item dead zone — no untargetability yet, so her ranged Q chips you on every walk-up. Farm at max Q-cone range, hold E, and don't commit a half-HP all-in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework + Mist online: dash in, drop Hallowed Mist so she can't target you from range, and chunk her with %-max-HP snips while your passive heals the poke back."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker spike: a prolonged duel inside your Mist shreds a no-dash mage — kill her while Rebuttal (W) is on its 38-second cooldown, before her zone control scales."}],"wants":{"you":["E in onto Mel and land Snip Snip's true-damage center before she repositions out of your cone","Stand in Hallowed Mist so she can't target you with Q poke while you out-trade in melee","Hold autos, Q and especially Needlework through Rebuttal, then unload across its 38-second cooldown"],"foe":["Poke you down with ranged Q on every walk-up while you have no Mist and no dash to close","Pop Rebuttal (W) as you commit so your Needlework projectile reflects back onto you","Stack Overwhelm, execute you low, then reach you anywhere with Golden Eclipse"]},"early":"Mel's ranged Q out-ranges everything you have at level 1 (no Mist, no E), so don't trade — last-hit at the tip of your Snip Snip cone and accept a little chip. Once you hit Q+E at 2-3 you get a real window: Skip 'n Slash in, land the true-damage center of the cone, and E refunds off the champ hit so you reset back out before she kites. Her poke can't out-damage the heal your abilities give you once you connect in melee, and she has no dash to escape your E gap-close.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your soft spot — no Hallowed Mist untargetability and pre-first-item, so Radiant Volley (Q, 10s) whittles you while you farm; respect it and do not force. At 6 it flips: dash in and drop Mist so she cannot target you from outside it, then keep snipping in the melee her kit hates. Rebuttal is about timing, not Mist — it blocks damage AND reflects projectiles, so never dump autos, Q or a Needlework into it. Hold, let it expire, and you have 38 seconds at rank 1 to work with.","late":"You own the straight 1v1 all game — a squishy mage with no dash, and you out-sustain her poke, so one clean E-in under Mist kills her once Riftmaker lands. Two things earn respect. Rebuttal reflects projectiles, so a Needlework thrown into it comes back at you. And Searing Brilliance stacks Overwhelm on everything she touches, which Golden Eclipse then cashes in from anywhere on the map — walking away low and marked is not the same as being safe.","whys":["No Mist, no E, and her Q out-ranges you at level 1 — it's pure poke, so last-hit at cone range and bank the wave instead of trading.","Radiant Volley (Q, 10s) still out-ranges you and you have no Mist — last-hit at cone range and bank the wave instead of trading.","Q+E gives you a real gap-close: dash in, land the true-damage center, and the E refund resets you out before Radiant Volley punishes back.","Her window — pre-Mist and pre-item, Radiant Volley chips you on every walk-up and you cannot close safely, so farm and do not force.","At 6 you dash in and drop Mist so she cannot target you from range, then grind her down in the melee her kit cannot escape.","Riftmaker turns extended Mist duels lethal — a no-dash mage melts in fog she cannot poke through, if you wait out Rebuttal.","You win the 1v1 all game; only Rebuttal (W, 38s at rank 1) earns respect — never throw Needlework into it, since it reflects projectiles."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"mordekaiser","win":["Skill","Mordekaiser","Gwen","Mordekaiser","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Even start before tools come online, but his Q's second hit only deals bonus damage when no other enemy is near you, so do not stand alone in a side bush for last hits and feed his isolation Q."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Realm of Death drags you both into a 1v1 box, but your Needlework (R) slow plus the armor/MR from Hallowed Mist (W) lets you kite-snip his max-HP through his Indestructible shield and out-sustain the stat steal."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online: Snip Snip! shreds his stacked HP with %-max-HP magic plus the true-damage center snip, and Skip 'n Slash (E) resets keep you on him for plates and out of his E pull."},{"when":"His R window","text":"Realm of Death (140s at rank 1) is his only real win condition — dodge the 16-second E pull first, then drop fresh mist inside the realm and make sure Grievous is on him before he cashes Indestructible."}],"wants":{"you":["Use Hallowed Mist (W) to body-block his E pull and deny the Q isolation, snipping his max-HP from inside the fog while he stands outside it","Have Grievous Wounds on him BEFORE he consumes Indestructible — the shield is built from damage he deals and takes, and he can turn all of it into a heal","Chain Skip 'n Slash (E) resets to dodge the E pull, stick through his slow, and shove for plates before he reaches 2 items"],"foe":["Land his E pull to yank you out of Hallowed Mist and into Q isolation range for the bonus slam","Let you feed Indestructible (W, 12s) with your own damage, then consume the shield as a heal","Save Realm of Death (R) for when your W is down, dragging you into a 1v1 box to steal your stats and burst you"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are his, not yours. You have no mist and no E dash yet, so his E-pull into an isolated Q slam backed by Indestructible out-stats your clunky cone Q in a straight trade. Do not stand alone in side brush or sit at melee range for a CS — that is exactly the no-enemies-nearby isolation his Q bonus wants. Farm with the tip of Snip Snip! at max range, respect the pull, and accept a little chip; his W heal means you cannot win the level-1 poke war anyway. Reach 6 and your %-HP shredding plus mist flip the lane.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still rough — a melee with no untargetability against shield-backed trades — so farm and side-step Death's Grasp (16s at rank 1) instead of forcing. Everything flips at 6: Needlework slows him out of walk-up range, Hallowed Mist gives you armour and MR and hides you from a Morde standing outside it, and Thousand Cuts heals you back. In Realm of Death, hold W and drop fresh mist as the box forms. One warning: Indestructible is built from damage he deals AND takes, so a blind grind funds it — land Grievous before he consumes it. Keep snipping his max-HP through the stat steal — your %-HP grind out-trades a Morde who has to spend his whole kit just to kill you.","late":"This is your lane to own from first item on. Riftmaker/Nashor's turns Snip Snip! into a max-HP-and-shield shredder — the more HP he stacks and the bigger his Indestructible, the harder your %-HP magic and true-damage center snip cut through, and Thousand Cuts heals you for chunks of his giant bar. Skip 'n Slash resets let you stick through his slow and reposition out of the E pull on demand. His one win condition is landing a clean Realm of Death while your W is down, so track your mist cooldown, never get isolated off your wave, and pop W as the realm forms. Snowball before he hits 2+ items and the lane is yours.","whys":["Neither of you has a real tool at level 1, but his Q only gets its bonus when you are alone — even start, just deny the side-bush isolation pick.","Death's Grasp (E, 16s at rank 1) into an isolated Obliterate plus the Indestructible shield out-stats your toolless level 2 — farm at range.","With Q and E online you can poke and reset out of his pull, and your %-HP snips start punishing his HP faster than his shield refreshes.","Pre-6 you are a melee with no mist against his shielded trades, and every hit you land feeds Indestructible — dodge the 16-second pull and farm.","Needlework slows him out of walk-up range and Hallowed Mist's armour/MR carries you through Realm of Death — with Grievous on before he cashes the shield.","Riftmaker/Nashor's makes Snip Snip! shred his stacked HP and shield with %-max-HP plus true damage while Thousand Cuts heals it all back.","At 2+ items the more HP and shield he builds the harder your %-HP Q cuts him — he has no scaling answer, so you own the late duel."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"nasus","win":["Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Nasus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q+E online: Skip 'n Slash dashes in, refunds on champ-hit, and Snip Snip! shoves so you can deny his Siphoning Strike last-hits and choke his stack count before he scales."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework + Hallowed Mist: drop W when he Withers you, slow him with R, and snip untargetable while his crippled, stack-less all-in whiffs."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's plus anti-heal: your Q's %-max-HP magic and the true-damage centre snip melt his fat HP bar faster than Soul Eater lifesteal refills it."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"A free-farmed Nasus reclaims the lane — his stacked Siphoning Strike one-shots and his R health/sustain out-drains your passive, so close the game before he gets there."}],"wants":{"you":["Deny his Siphoning Strike stacks by shoving with Q+E and zoning him off the cannon wave","Bait his W Wither, then drop Hallowed Mist as the cripple lands so the all-in whiffs while you snip untargetable","Rush anti-heal and a %-HP first item so your Q shreds his HP bar before his stacks come online"],"foe":["Free-farm Siphoning Strike stacks unbothered until one Q one-shots cannons and squishies","Land Wither (15s at rank 1) to gut your attack speed and kite, then walk you down","Drag the game past 2 items where his stacked Q and R sustain out-scale your healing"]},"early":"At Level 1 you're both soft with no combo, so just trade last-hits. But the moment your Q+E come online at 2-3, your job is to make his stacks expensive: Snip Snip! shoves the wave and Skip 'n Slash darts you in (refunding its cooldown on a champ-hit) to deny his Siphoning Strike farm — every cannon you steal is a stack he never gets. Don't facetank his auto into a fresh Q, but you out-poke him cleanly here with no all-in for him to punish you pre-6.","mid":"This is where you take over. His only real threat is Wither shutting off your attack speed, so bait it: let him commit, drop Hallowed Mist as the cripple lands, and you are untargetable while he flails — then you have fifteen seconds at rank 1 before it returns. At 6, Needlework slows him and your passive heals off the damage you deal. Fury of the Sands hands him bonus armour and MR, and the centre of Snip Snip! is true damage, so fight him THROUGH his ult rather than waiting it out. The fatter he builds, the harder you snip.","late":"Here is the honest part: a free-farmed Nasus out-scales even you. Fully stacked, Siphoning Strike one-shots through a dropped mist, and inside Fury of the Sands its cooldown drops further while his Health and Soul Eater sustain out-drain your healing — the 2+ item window is his. Everything before that was your lane. You should have a CS and plate lead from shoving him off the wave, so trade it into objectives and end. If the game drifts to 30 minutes even, his stacked Q wins the 1v1.","whys":["You're both weak at level 1 with no combo — trade last-hits and start angling to zone him off his Siphoning Strike stacks.","Your Q+E come online and shove — every cannon you deny is a stack he never gets, and he has no all-in to punish the push.","With Q to poke and E to dash-reset in, you out-trade a stack-less Nasus who can only farm and Wither.","You're melee with no untargetability until W, but he still can't all-in you — keep denying stacks and farming safely.","Hallowed Mist eats his Wither all-in: drop W as the cripple lands, stay untargetable, and Needlework slows his retreat.","Riftmaker plus anti-heal lets your %-max-HP Q and the true-damage centre shred him faster than Soul Eater refills — your hardest all-in window.","A fully-stacked Nasus out-scales you: Siphoning Strike one-shots and Fury of the Sands (120s) out-drains your healing — close before this."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"nautilus","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Nautilus","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Nautilus's Dredge Line hook plus his Staggering Blow auto-root can chain you before you have W mist up to break line of sight — this is his cleanest catch window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework online: bait his hook or Depth Charge, drop W so the follow-up Riptide whiffs, then grind his tank HP with %-max Snip Snip while your passive heals the trade."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker turns your %-max-HP Q and Thousand Cuts on-hit into real sustained DPS that out-trades anything Nautilus can stack."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Pre-6 his hook into Riptide and the Staggering Blow root out-stat you in a flat brawl — his strongest window, and Dredge Line is only 14s."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait the Dredge Line hook, then drop Hallowed Mist so you go untargetable from outside it and his Riptide follow-up whiffs","Snip Snip his tank HP with %-max-HP magic and the true-damage center snip while Thousand Cuts heals you off it","Reach Riftmaker, where your %-HP Q and on-hit passive grind down anything Nautilus stacks faster than he can sustain"],"foe":["Land the Dredge Line skillshot and lock you with the Staggering Blow root before you can break vision with mist","Pin you with Depth Charge knockup out of mist range so his jungler collapses for the kill","Stack health and trade evenly through your early kit, denying you a clean lead before your items"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are a coinflip and his Dredge Line hook decides it — get caught and the Staggering Blow auto-root locks you, Riptide chunks you, and your W mist isn't up yet to break his line of sight. Don't walk into hook range to last-hit when Q is up; farm at max Snip Snip cone range and respect that one hook chains his full combo. The flip side: his trade does damage but has no kill pressure if you dodge the hook, so just refuse the catch and farm even.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his window — he has Dredge Line into Riptide and the auto-root before your kit fully comes online, so respect that brawl and farm rather than force it. At 6 the lane swings to you: drop Hallowed Mist the instant his hook or Depth Charge lands so the Riptide follow-up whiffs and you're untargetable from outside the cloud, then Snip Snip his health bar with %-max-HP magic and the true-damage center snip. He can't burst through your Thousand Cuts healing, so a baited all-in into your mist favors you hard.","late":"This stays even because your strengths and his cancel out. Your %-max-HP Q and Thousand Cuts anti-tank profile shred everything Nautilus builds — the fatter his HP bar, the harder you hit and the more you heal. But his CC never falls off: one Dredge Line, which he can also hook off a wall to reposition, or one targeted Depth Charge pins you out of mist and lets his team delete you. Itemise to survive the catch, group with W up, and you out-DPS his whole frontline.","whys":["You're both weak at level 1, but his Dredge Line hook plus the Staggering Blow auto-root can chain you with no W mist to break vision yet — last-hit at max range.","Still a coinflip — no kill button yet, so sidestep the 14-second hook and farm even.","Snip Snip! lets you poke and Skip 'n Slash resets it, but his 14-second hook into Riptide trades evenly back — nobody owns this stage outright.","Pre-6 and before your kit's online you're a melee with no untargetability into his hook plus Riptide and auto-root — this is his strongest window.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it: drop W on his hook or Depth Charge and Snip Snip grinds his tank HP while Thousand Cuts healing eats his damage.","Your first AP item makes the %-max-HP Q and on-hit passive out-trade anything Nautilus stacks — force the all-in here.","Your anti-tank DPS shreds his health, but Dredge Line and a targeted Depth Charge never fall off and can pin you out of mist — it nets even."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"neeko","win":["Neeko","Skill","Skill","Neeko","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Neeko owns level 1 — her Q (Blooming Burst) bounces AoE damage onto you while you have no W mist to duck behind. Last-hit at max range and accept the chip."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Her biggest pre-6 window: no mist for you, Blooming Burst (9s) blooms twice off the wave, and a Tangle-Barbs through a minion roots you for longer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hallowed Mist plus Needlework flips the lane — sidestep her Pop Blossom radius with E, then mist and snip her squishy body while R slows her escape."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online: E-dash onto her, drop W on her root, and %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus your true-damage center snip melt her low base HP in one extended trade."}],"wants":{"you":["Sidestep her E (Tangle-Barbs) root so she can't pin you, then E-dash in and drop W mist on top of her","Reach level 6 and your first item, where %-max-HP Q plus mist lets you out-duel her squishy body in an extended fight","Dodge the Pop Blossom radius by dashing out, then punish the long R cooldown with a mist-and-Needlework all-in"],"foe":["Fire Tangle-Barbs through a minion so it lands bigger, faster and longer, then stack Blooming Burst poke","Channel Pop Blossom from a clone or unseen angle to stun and burst you out of position","Use her W (Shapesplitter) clone and disguise to roam and set up picks rather than fight your scaling 1v1"]},"early":"Neeko owns level 1 — her Q (Blooming Burst) bounces AoE damage onto you for free while you have no mist to duck into and a slow-to-land cone Q of your own. Don't walk up to last-hit into her E (Tangle-Barbs) root; if she pins you, she stacks Q damage and you can't trade back. Farm with the tips of Snip Snip! and accept some poke — your Thousand Cuts healing eats most of it once you start landing autos on her. By level 3 you have Q+E to dash in and reset, but she just roots-and-kites with her clone, so pick your spots and don't burn E chasing a Shapesplitter decoy.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are her window: no mist yet means her Q poke and E root chip you down with nothing to hide behind, and this is when her roam or a jungle gank punishes you hardest. Then level 6 flips it — Hallowed Mist plus Needlework turns you into the duelist. Her Pop Blossom is centered on her own body, so mist alone won't save you if she lands on top of you — dash out of the radius with E first, then drop W and snip her squishy body down while R slows her escape. She has no sustain to answer your Thousand Cuts healing in an extended fight.","late":"You out-scale her in a straight 1v1 all day — her low base HP folds to %-max-HP Snip Snip! and the true-damage center, while your mist blanks burst thrown from outside it. But Neeko is a pick-mage, not a duelist: she will Shapesplitter-disguise as a teammate, flank, and Pop Blossom your backline. Worse, while she is disguised the Pop Blossom preparation is HIDDEN, so the wind-up you would normally see is not there. Group with vision, mist the engage, and make her spend a 120-second R into your team where you can E on top of her.","whys":["Neeko's Q (Blooming Burst) bounces AoE poke onto you for free while you have no W mist to hide behind and only a slow cone Q — concede the level and last-hit at range.","You pick up E and a second Q rank but you're still a soft melee against her poke-and-root — farm rather than fight; your Thousand Cuts passive sustains the chip.","Q+E lets you dash and reset, but Tangle-Barbs (12s) grows larger and roots longer through a minion, so the trade washes out.","Still no mist, so Blooming Burst (9s) and a 12-second Tangle-Barbs own you — her best roam and gank window before your six.","Needlework plus a full Q-W-E kit lets you dodge Pop Blossom, mist her follow-up, slow her with R, and grind her squishy body down — you own the duel from here.","Riftmaker/Nashor's online: E-dash in, mist her CC, and %-max-HP Snip plus your true-damage center snip delete her low base HP in one extended trade.","You win the straight duel forever, but she is a pick-mage: disguised, her Pop Blossom wind-up is hidden, so she flanks instead of fighting and the lane nets even."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"olaf","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Olaf owns the early levels — his Undertow (Q) axe slows you, and picking it up refunds the cooldown and speeds him up, so he weaves autos and walks you down before you have Mist or E to peel off."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R Needlework plus the Q-W-E rotation flips the duel — drop Hallowed Mist on his all-in so he can't full-commit, slow him with needles, and snip the percent-max-HP off his bruiser bar."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Nashor's into Riftmaker is your real spike — the attack speed feeds your percent-HP Snip Snip! and your ability healing out-grinds his lifesteal in extended fights inside Mist."},{"when":"R window","text":"Ragnarok (R, 100s) is the danger button — it makes him immune to disables for as long as he keeps attacking, so Needlework's slow does nothing. His true damage is Reckless Swing (E, 11s), not his autos."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his all-in into Hallowed Mist so he eats the resist wall and can't pick his axe back up off you while you keep snipping","Reach Level 6 and Nashor's where the Needlework slow plus percent-HP Snip Snip! and ability healing out-grind his bruiser HP","Use Skip 'n Slash to dodge his thrown axe and reset E off each hit so he never gets the pickup move-speed to stick on you"],"foe":["Land Undertow (Q) slows and grab the axe back to walk you down levels 1-3 before you have Mist or E mobility","Pop Ragnarok mid-trade so its disable immunity ignores your slows, then land Reckless Swing's true damage through Mist's resists","Stack lifesteal and auto-weave to out-sustain your snips in a straight stand-and-fight before you spike"]},"early":"Olaf owns the first three levels — his Undertow (Q) slows you and, if he picks the axe back up, the cooldown resets and he gets move speed to weave more autos and walk you down before you have Hallowed Mist or E mobility. Do NOT stand and trade autos here; your six-snip cone Q can't out-DPS his early all-in and he sustains through any chip with lifesteal. Side-step his thrown axe so he never gets the pickup speed boost, and last-hit at range — denying him that axe is the whole lane, and without it his pressure stalls.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — a melee with no untargetability against slow-and-chase — so farm safely and wait for 6. At 6 the lane flips: Needlework's slow plus your full Q-W-E rotation lets you drop Hallowed Mist as he commits, deny the axe pickup so Undertow sits its full nine seconds, and snip the percent-max-HP off his bruiser bar while your abilities heal you back. The trap is Ragnarok — for 100 seconds at rank 1 he can be immune to disables while he keeps attacking, so your slows do nothing. Bait it or fight while it is down.","late":"Your Nashor's-into-Riftmaker spike turns extended fights your way — percent-HP Snip Snip! plus ability healing grinds his bar down harder the more HP he builds, and Mist's resists blunt his physical autos, which are NOT true damage. Two things to respect. Ragnarok strips your slows with disable immunity for as long as he keeps swinging, and Reckless Swing (E, 11s) is real true damage that ignores those resists. Worse, Berserker Rage gives him attack speed and lifesteal off MISSING health, so a half-dead Olaf is the dangerous one. Fight when R is down, kite around his 9-second axe, and the lane stays the coinflip it is.","whys":["Olaf out-trades you levels 1-3 — his Undertow slow plus the axe-pickup speed and his lifesteal walk you down before you have Mist or E to escape.","Still his edge but softening — you have E now; side-step his axe to deny the pickup and farm rather than trade autos you'll lose.","You get Q+E to poke-and-reset, but his axe-pickup sustain and lifesteal keep the all-in even — don't over-commit before Mist.","Your worst window if Mist isn't up — a melee with no untargetability against his slow-and-chase, so concede and farm to 6.","Needlework plus full Q-W-E flips it — drop Mist on his all-in, deny the axe pickup, slow him with needles, and snip the percent-HP off his bruiser bar.","Nashor's into Riftmaker lands — your percent-HP Snip and ability healing out-grind his lifesteal in extended duels inside Mist.","Genuinely even — your percent-HP shred and healing scale, but Ragnarok's disable immunity blanks your slows and Reckless Swing's true damage ignores Mist's resists, so whoever lands their window wins."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"ornn","win":["Ornn","Ornn","Ornn","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Ornn's lane is strongest here: Bellows Breath (W, 12s) applies Brittle, and Searing Charge (E, 14s) knocks up only when he hits TERRAIN — usually his own Q pillar."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it — you sit untargetable in the fog, slow him with R, and start grinding his HP bar with Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP and true-damage center snip while your passive heals every cut."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online — your Q center snip ignores his stacked armor (true damage), and every point of HP/armor he forges just feeds your passive damage and ability healing."},{"when":"Late","text":"Ornn's R into the magma pillar is a double knock-up — that's his one win condition vs you, so dodge the rolling wave or it pins you out of Mist for his team to collapse."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his Q pillar or E charge, then drop Hallowed Mist as the knock-up lands so you go untargetable and his Brittle detonation finds nothing","Reach 6 and grind his max-HP bar with Snip Snip!'s %-HP plus the true-damage center snip while your passive and ability healing top you off","Use Skip 'n Slash's cooldown refund off his squishy plates/minions to reset spacing and dodge his next pillar"],"foe":["Use Bellows Breath (W, 12s) to apply Brittle, then charge into his own Q pillar so Searing Charge gets the terrain knock-up","Drop a Q magma pillar to wall off your Mist angle and give Searing Charge its terrain","Stack armor and self-forged items to scale and save R's double knock-up to catch you out of Mist in a teamfight"]},"early":"Ornn out-stats you levels 1-3, so respect the combo: Bellows Breath (W, 12s) applies Brittle, and Searing Charge (E, 14s) only knocks up if he collides with TERRAIN — which is why he drops a Q magma pillar first. Deny him that geometry: do not CS beside a fresh pillar or a wall, and his charge is just damage. Farm with the tip of Snip Snip! and accept you are the weaker stat-check until your kit is online; this is the one window he genuinely beats you.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay close — you're a melee with no untargetability yet, so trade short and bait his Q/E knock-up into where your Hallowed Mist will drop so the Brittle detonation whiffs. At 6 the lane flips hard: Needlework plus Mist means you can sit untargetable in the fog, slow him with R, and grind his massive HP bar with the %-max-HP and true-damage center of Snip Snip! while your passive heals every cut. He has no sustain to answer that, so once you hit 6 you own the extended duel.","late":"This is a tank-shred matchup built for you — the more armor and self-forged HP Ornn stacks, the harder your %-max-HP Q hits and the more your passive and ability healing leech off his bar, so the straight 1v1 only widens. The one thing to fear is his R: the magma-pillar double knock-up can pin you out of Mist and let his team collapse on you, so never get caught flat-footed near a fight. Win the side lane, shove his plates, and reduce him to nothing but that teamfight CC.","whys":["Ornn is a strong level-1 tank with better base stats — last-hit safe, don't trade into his Bellows Breath and Brittle before you have any defensive button.","Bellows Breath (W, 12s) makes you Brittle and his Searing Charge only knocks up off TERRAIN — his own Q pillar is that wall, so stay clear of it.","You get Q+E to poke and reset, but his base stats and Brittle still stat-check the even trades — step up while Searing Charge sits its 14s.","A coin-flip skirmish window: short trades and baiting his Q pillar into your Mist drop keep it even while you wait for 6.","At 6 Needlework plus Hallowed Mist lets you sit untargetable, slow him, and snip his huge HP bar with %-HP and true damage while your passive heals you.","Riftmaker/Nashor's online means your Q center snip's true damage ignores his armor and his self-built tankiness only feeds your healing.","He scales into nothing about your duel — every HP/armor item he forges makes your %-max-HP passive hit harder, so the longer the 1v1, the more you win it."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"pantheon","win":["Pantheon","Pantheon","Pantheon","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Shield Vault (W, 13s) is a targeted stun into a Mortal Will empowered Comet Spear -- his kill window. Aegis Assault (E, 22s) also blanks damage from the front, so do not try to win the trade-back; farm at Snip range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it: when his W stun lands and he steps in, drop W so he's standing outside your mist and goes untargetable to him, then R-slow and snip while your ability healing out-sustains his Q chip."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker or Nashor's is your takeover -- %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus E's on-hit range and CD refund let you out-DPS and out-heal any extended duel his mana-hungry, fading Q poke can't close."},{"when":"Late","text":"Pantheon is a husk past two items; only his global R ult and roams matter, so shove him in, take his tower with your 1v1 scaling, and use his weak side-lane to pressure the map."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive levels 1-3 at the tip of Snip Snip! and refuse trades — an empowered Mortal Will spear off a Shield Vault stun wins any short exchange","Hit 6 and use Hallowed Mist to go untargetable when his W stun lands, so the empowered Q follow-up whiffs and you R-snip him back","Spike on Riftmaker/Nashor's and force extended duels where %-max-HP Snip and ability healing grind out his fading Q poke"],"foe":["Land the Shield Vault stun (W, 13s) and chain a Mortal Will empowered Comet Spear straight into it","All-in at levels 1-3 before you have mist or E mobility to escape his W-into-Q burst","Snowball the early lead or use his global R to roam, since he falls off hard once your items come online"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to Pantheon: Shield Vault (W, 13s) is a targeted stun, Mortal Will empowers the Comet Spear that follows, and Aegis Assault (E, 22s) makes him invulnerable to damage from the FRONT while he channels. Do not trade back -- farm with the tip of Snip Snip! at max range and eat a little poke rather than feeding the all-in. With no Hallowed Mist and no E reset yet, a W-stun into spear has nothing to bail you out of. Soak XP and wait for 6.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a holding pattern: Comet Spear (11s) is still live but his mana bleeds and your ability healing quietly eats the chip. At 6 everything flips. When he Shield Vaults in for the empowered spear, drop Hallowed Mist so HE is standing outside it -- you go untargetable and the follow-up hits nothing. Then R to slow, Skip 'n Slash in, and snip him. If he sets Aegis Assault, walk around it: the invulnerability only covers his front, and it is 22 seconds at rank 1.","late":"Once you finish Riftmaker or Nashor's it's over for him in a straight fight: Pantheon is a husk past two items while your %-max-HP Snip Snip! and untargetable mist win every extended duel his mana-hungry, fading Q poke can't close. The only threats left on him are his global R ult and roams, so don't let him fish for plays elsewhere -- shove him in, take his tower with your 1v1 scaling, and look to end before his team-fight chip stops mattering entirely.","whys":["Mortal Will empowers his next spell every few casts, and Shield Vault (W, 13s) is a targeted stun into that spear — you have only a cone Q to answer with.","He's still the lane bully and you're a melee with no mist or E mobility -- his W-into-Q all-in beats anything you can do back at level 2-3.","You have Q poke and E resets, but Aegis Assault (E, 22s) makes him invulnerable from the FRONT — get behind him or the trade goes nowhere.","Comet Spear (Q, 11s) poke fades as his mana bleeds and your sustain eats the chip, but you are pre-mist — a coinflip window, so do not overstay.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist arrives — bait Shield Vault, drop mist so he is outside it and you go untargetable, then R-slow and out-sustain his burst.","Riftmaker/Nashor's lets your %-max-HP Snip and E on-hit range win extended duels his mana-hungry Q poke can no longer sustain.","Pantheon hard-falls-off into items while you scale -- your 1v1 and %-HP shred own the map; only his global R still matters."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"poppy","win":["Poppy","Poppy","Poppy","Poppy","Gwen","Poppy","Poppy"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Steadfast Presence stops your E dash and GROUNDS you, so there is no recast, and Hammer Shock's delayed slow zone wins the short trade — she owns these levels."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your one flip: drop W as her E or R commits so it whiffs, R-slow her, and grind her with %-max-HP Snip Snip whose center snip is true damage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online is your only window to win an extended duel inside Hallowed Mist before her tank items make her trades unloseable."},{"when":"Late","text":"Tank Poppy's E Heroic Charge wall-stun and R Keeper's Verdict knock you off your mist every fight — her biggest window as she out-tanks your sustained DPS."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her E Heroic Charge into empty space, then drop W and chunk her with %-max-HP Snip Snip true damage","Reach Level 6 so Hallowed Mist + Needlework slow let you out-sustain her short trades","Force the duel on your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike before her armor items snowball the lane"],"foe":["Land E Heroic Charge to pin you to a wall for the stun and a free Q-auto burst window","Hold Steadfast Presence (20s) to stop your E dash, ground you, and slow you out of range","Save R Keeper's Verdict to knock you clean out of your own Hallowed Mist mid-fight"]},"early":"Poppy owns the early outright — Steadfast Presence stops your E dash the instant you reposition and GROUNDS you afterwards, so you cannot recast it, and Hammer Shock's slow zone plus her buckler shield win the short trade while you have no Hallowed Mist. Do not walk up to throw a cone Q she can answer with Heroic Charge into the wall behind you. Last-hit at max Q range and wait for the level where untargetability exists. The upside: A Thousand Cuts still chips her percent-max-HP any time she greeds.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay hers — you are a melee whose only gap-close gets stopped, grounded and then wall-stunned, so farm and respect Heroic Charge (14s) near terrain. At 6 it tilts: drop Hallowed Mist as her E or R commits so the follow-up whiffs, slow her with Needlework, and let your healing out-grind her while the true-damage centre ignores her armour. Bait Steadfast Presence first — at rank 1 it is 20 seconds, and that is your whole window.","late":"This goes back to Poppy late and you have to accept it — she builds tank, so her W denies your E engage, her E Heroic Charge pins you off your mist, and Keeper's Verdict knocks you out of a fight you were winning. Your %-max-HP Q hurts her more the more armor she stacks, but she only has to land one E to delete your positioning. Win or even the lane on your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike and take side-lane priority — never duel her against a wall, and never E into her W.","whys":["Steadfast Presence stops your E dash AND grounds you, and Hammer Shock's slow zone wins the trade while you have no mist.","She still out-stats a mist-less Gwen and can Heroic Charge you into the wall behind for a stun — last-hit, not trade.","Her buckler shield and Hammer Shock out-sustain your cone poke; without untargetability you cannot punish her.","Levels 4-5 you're a melee whose only dash gets wall-stunned — farm and respect terrain, don't commit.","At 6 Hallowed Mist whiffs her E/R, Needlework slows, and true-damage Snip Snip lets you out-grind her trades.","Riftmaker/Nashor's online is your one window to win the extended duel inside mist before her tank items scale.","Tank Poppy out-tanks your DPS and her E/R peel you off your mist — your %-HP Q hurts but one E undoes your position."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"quinn","win":["Quinn","Quinn","Quinn","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Quinn's window: Harrier-marked autos plus Blinding Assault (Q, 11s) out-poke you before you have mist or the E range to touch her, and Vault (12s) slows you and lands her back at max range. Just farm."},{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Skip 'n Slash gives you a dash with bonus on-hit range and attack speed — your first way to reach her — but it refunds nothing if she vaults out, so don't burn it into open air."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips the lane: E in, drop W so you're untargetable/armored as her vault and poke land on the fog, then R-slow her kite and trade her down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's with anti-heal: %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus Thousand Cuts healing turn any landed all-in on a no-armor Quinn into a kill."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach level 6, E in to close range, and drop W mist so her vault knockback and poke land on the fog while the armor/MR and untargetability blank her damage","All-in a squishy Quinn with %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus anti-heal once you have your first item — she builds no armor and has no sustain to answer Thousand Cuts","Farm safe through levels 1-3 poke, then snowball mid and close the game before her roams and late kiting take over"],"foe":["Proc Harrier and poke you on every step-up, blind you with Blinding Assault (11s), then kite back on passive move speed","Poke you to half before 6 and roam bot/mid since she shoves fast and outruns your dash","Stay at max range outside your W and never let you land an E gap-close into the all-in"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to Quinn. Harrier marks you for a heavy nimble auto, Blinding Assault (Q, 11s) hinders your vision, and Vault slows you, briefly interrupts your cone and drops her back at max attack range — so every walk-up ends with her kiting off on passive move speed. With no mist and not enough E range yet, last-hit at the tip of Snip Snip! and do not chase a Vault you cannot catch. Her poke is real, but it cannot kill you if you farm safe.","mid":"This is where you take over. The moment you hit W, Hallowed Mist answers her whole kit: E in with Skip 'n Slash, drop the fog, and her vault and poke land on you while you're untargetable from outside it and sitting on bonus armor and MR. At 6, Needlework slows her kite so she can't peel away, and Thousand Cuts healing eats through her poke. Bait the vault, then commit on top of her — she's a squishy with no armor once you've closed the gap.","late":"You own the scaling and the straight 1v1 from your first item on. With Riftmaker/Nashor's and anti-heal, %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus Thousand Cuts healing delete a Quinn who builds no defensive stats — one E into mist on top of her is a kill. Her outs are roaming and split-pushing with Behind Enemy Lines, which is a channelled fast-travel rather than a true global, so it can be caught. Close the game before she turns the map into her playground.","whys":["Quinn out-ranges you early: Harrier-marked autos and Blinding Assault (Q, 11s) chip you while she kites on passive move speed, and you have no mist or E range to answer.","She still owns level 2 — her vault poke and Harrier procs beat your slow cone Q, and your one early ability can't reliably close the gap she keeps opening.","With Q and E you can poke and reset, but Vault (12s) slows you, interrupts your cone and lands her back at max range — neither of you cleanly wins.","You hit W: drop Hallowed Mist so her vault and poke land while you're untargetable from outside it, sitting on armor and MR she has no way to answer.","Needlework slows her kite while mist blanks her damage and Thousand Cuts out-sustains her poke — you own every committed fight now.","Riftmaker plus anti-heal is your peak: %-max-HP Snip Snip! shreds a no-armor Quinn and your healing erases her DPS the instant you land an E into mist.","You out-scale her hard — a sidelane Quinn loses to your %-HP shred and self-heal, so only her roams and the R fast-travel threaten you."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"renekton","win":["Renekton","Renekton","Renekton","Renekton","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"At 50+ Fury his W stuns for 1.5s instead of 0.75s and Cull the Meek (7s) heals the trade back — with no Hallowed Mist yet, eat the chip and last-hit at the tip of Snip Snip!."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist online: bait his Slice-and-Dice W all-in, drop W as the stun lands so his empowered follow-up hits nothing while you're untargetable, then R-slow and snip him down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker into Nashor's Tooth is the real flip — %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus your ability healing out-grind the extended duel his short fury window can't close."},{"when":"Late","text":"Renekton's fury combo stays on a clock while your %-max-HP autos and Thousand Cuts shred any duel — only a scaling teammate of his, not Renekton himself, contests you here."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive levels 1-5 last-hitting at the tip of Snip Snip! — never trade into a full fury bar or his empowered W stun","Reach Level 6 and bait his Slice-and-Dice all-in into Hallowed Mist so the empowered W-combo whiffs while you're untargetable","Hit Riftmaker/Nashor's where %-max-HP Snip Snip! and your ability healing out-grind his item-starved fury kit"],"foe":["Open with a full fury bar and point-click W stun into Slice and Dice before you have any mist","Win every level 1-3 short trade and heal it back with Cull the Meek while denying your CS","Snowball the early lead and roam or force objectives before your first AP item comes online"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are his lane. Renekton targets you with Ruthless Predator — 0.75s normally, a full 1.5s at 50+ Fury — follows with Slice and Dice, and heals the trade back with Cull the Meek, and you have no Hallowed Mist to make any of it whiff. Do not contest the fury-empowered all-in; last-hit at the tip of Snip Snip! and soak the chip, because your %-HP damage and healing scale while his window is a clock. One warning: Reign of Anger generates MORE Fury the lower he gets, so chipping him without killing him refills the bar you were draining.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your worst window — a melee with no untargetability against a targeted stun — so farm and wait for 6. Once Needlework and your full kit are online the lane flips: when he burns fury to W-stun in, drop Hallowed Mist as the stun lands so the empowered follow-up hits nothing, then R to slow his retreat and grind him with %-HP Snip Snip!. Both his W and his Slice and Dice are 16 seconds at rank 1, so once the fury dumps and the dash is spent he cannot re-engage — just keep Grievous on him so Cull the Meek cannot refund it.","late":"This is where Renekton stops being a threat — he scales into items terribly while %-max-HP Snip Snip! and Riftmaker sustain turn every extended duel into a grind he cannot win. You shred him through Hallowed Mist and he has no answer once the fury combo is down, and Skip 'n Slash refunds let you reset the duel faster than he can re-fury. Keep anti-heal up, because Cull the Meek is a flat 7 seconds. The only thing that takes this lane from you late is a true scaler on his TEAM out-pacing you — against Renekton himself, close it out and do not let his early game turn into a lead he cannot replicate.","whys":["A full-fury Ruthless Predator stuns for 1.5s instead of 0.75s, and a level-1 Gwen has no Hallowed Mist and no Skip 'n Slash to answer it.","He out-stats you hard at 1-2 and Cull the Meek (7s) heals back any chip you land while your Snip Snip! cone is still clunky.","Even with Q poke and an E reset, his targeted stun and fury combo own the level-3 trade before you can drop mist.","Your worst window — a melee with no untargetability against a fury-empowered all-in you cannot make whiff.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist online: bait the W all-in into mist so the empowered follow-up whiffs while you are untargetable, then R-slow and snip him through its 16 seconds.","Riftmaker into Nashor's flips the extended duel — %-max-HP Snip Snip! and ability healing beat his item-starved fury window.","Renekton falls off a cliff into items while %-HP Snip Snip! and Thousand Cuts shred him — the lane is yours unless his team out-scales you."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"riven","win":["Riven","Riven","Riven","Riven","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Broken Wings plus a point-blank Ki Burst stun out-stat your slow cone Q before you have mist or E — her best window, so soft-farm and refuse the raw trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus your full Q-W-E flips it: hold W and drop Hallowed Mist as her Q3 knockup lands so her combo whiffs while you Snip her HP and heal off the ability damage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's is your spike — %-max-HP Snip plus your passive on-hit and ability healing win the extended duel her front-loaded burst can't sustain."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your worst window if you haven't hit W yet — a melee with no untargetability eating her dash-in Ki Burst all-in before your spike."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 6, hold W, and bait her Ki Burst stun so dropping Hallowed Mist makes her empowered Q3 and R whiff","Hit Riftmaker/Nashor's and grind her in extended duels her short front-loaded combo can't out-sustain","Snip her with %-max-HP Q and heal off the ability damage while she has no disengage from the mist once committed"],"foe":["Win levels 1-3 with Broken Wings dashes plus a Ki Burst stun before you have mist or E mobility","Land the full Ki Burst into Q3 knockup combo with R to burst you down inside her front-loaded window","Use her three Q dashes and the Valor shield-dash to sidestep your cone and eat your poke"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are hers. Riven's Broken Wings dashes plus a point-blank Ki Burst stun out-stat your slow cone Q before you have mist or E mobility, so don't step up to throw a Q she can just dash around. Last-hit at max Snip range, accept a little chip, and deny her the stat-check trade. The good news: her burst is front-loaded, so if you survive lane her short combo window can't out-grind what you become.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your worst window if you have not hit W — a melee with no untargetability against her dash-in all-in. At 6 it flips: hold W and drop Hallowed Mist the instant Ki Burst lands, so the Q3 knockback and R burst whiff while you stand untargetable and snip. Do not poke into Valor either — it blocks the damage outright. Bait the real Ki Burst, and remember Broken Wings is a flat 13 seconds for all three casts.","late":"Your Riftmaker/Nashor's spike is where you take over — %-max-HP Snip plus passive on-hit and ability healing win the long duel her front-loaded combo cannot grind through. Once all three Broken Wings casts are spent she has thirteen seconds with no disengage from your mist, and that is your commit. It stays close because a fed Riven still one-combos you out of position, so watch the auto after each cast — Runic Blade puts her damage there.","whys":["Broken Wings dashes and a Ki Burst stun out-stat your clunky cone Q at level 1 — no mist, no E, just farm.","She gets her second Q dash and trade pattern online before you have a real tool — soft-farm, don't trade raw.","With Q+E you can finally Snip-and-reset and contest, but her dash-stun burst still trades evenly through your pre-mist kit.","Pre-W you are a melee with no untargetability eating her dash-in Ki Burst (11s) all-in — her cleanest dive window.","Needlework plus full Q-W-E lets you mist her combo and out-sustain her front-loaded burst — you own the duel from here.","Riftmaker/Nashor's: %-max-HP Snip plus passive on-hit and ability healing win the extended fight her short combo can't out-grind.","A fed Riven still one-combos you out of position, but in a clean extended duel your %-HP Snip and sustain hold even."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"rumble","win":["Gwen","Skill","Rumble","Rumble","Gwen","Rumble","Rumble"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Flamespitter (Q, 10s) is free heat-fuelled DPS, and his two Electro Harpoons slow you AND stack a Magic Resist cut so the cone lands far harder."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hallowed Mist (W) plus Needlework (R) is your window: stand in your fog so his single-target damage can't reach you, slow him with R, and E in to trade — but step OUT of his Equalizer burn, the mist doesn't block ground AOE."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker online: your %-max-HP Snip Snip! (Q) and ability healing out-grind his Flamespitter sustain, and Skip 'n Slash refunds let you reset trades repeatedly."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your center-snip true damage and anti-heal shred him in an isolated duel — but his Equalizer still zones teamfight chokes regardless of your mist, so only commit when you've dragged him to a side lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive to Level 6 so Hallowed Mist (W) plus Needlework (R) give you a fog window to trade from","Stack into Riftmaker so %-max-HP Snip Snip! and ability healing out-grind his Flamespitter sustain","Close while he is Overheating at 100% heat — he cannot cast a single spell for those seconds"],"foe":["Pump Flamespitter (Q) heat and chunk you with Overheat-empowered autos while you're stuck in melee","Land both Electro Harpoons to shred your Magic Resist and slow you, then channel a full Flamespitter","Drop the Equalizer (R) on the wave to zone you off CS and force you to eat burn or give up farm"]},"early":"Rumble owns levels 1-3. Flamespitter (Q, 10s) is a wall of heat-fuelled magic damage that melts your melee form, and you have no Hallowed Mist and no Skip 'n Slash reset to escape the cone. Worse, he carries TWO Electro Harpoons and each one cuts your Magic Resist as well as slowing you, so an E-E into a full channel is the real combo — not the cone on its own. Last-hit at the edge of his Q range, accept the chip, and never eat both harpoons and a full Flamespitter in the same window. If he steps up with heat banked he chunks you with Overheat-empowered autos and shoves you off the wave — give up the CS, not the health bar.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your flip. Once you have Needlework (R) plus Hallowed Mist (W), drop your fog before you commit: anything outside the cloud cannot target you, so his poke goes dead while you slow him with R and E in for the attack speed and on-hit range. The trap: Equalizer is ground AoE that burns you inside the mist, so place your fog to the SIDE of the burn. The key read is his heat bar — at 100% he Overheats and cannot cast ANY spell for a few seconds, so that is when you close, even though his autos hit harder. Engage on the empty bar, not on the cone, and keep Skip 'n Slash for the reset rather than the escape.","late":"This is where you reclaim it. Riftmaker plus your %-max-HP Snip Snip! and ability healing finally out-sustain his Flamespitter DPS, and the center snip's true damage cuts through whatever MR he builds while your anti-heal kills his lifesteal. In an isolated 1v1 you win — fog to the side of his Equalizer so you stay untargetable, slow-chase with Needlework, and snip him out. The honest caveat: his Equalizer is a teamfight zoning tool that burns a whole choke whether you're in mist or not, so don't fight him standing in the carpet with your team behind you — drag him to a side lane and duel him where only the fog matters.","whys":["No fog and no Skip 'n Slash reset yet, and his Flamespitter (Q) out-DPSes your melee form every second you're in the cone.","Two Electro Harpoons stack a MAGIC RESIST cut on you before the cone even lands, and you cannot walk out of the slow.","Still a fog-less melee versus sustained Flamespitter poke — this is your worst window before Hallowed Mist (W) comes online.","Hallowed Mist plus Needlework flips it: stand untargetable in fog, slow him with R, and trade from inside — just dodge the Equalizer burn.","His heat-cycle Flamespitter still races your Riftmaker spike, and one Equalizer can deny your wave and your timing.","Even window — your Riftmaker duel spike trades blows with his, decided by whether you catch him post-overheat.","%-max-HP Snip Snip! plus anti-heal out-grinds his Flamespitter in any isolated 1v1 away from his Equalizer choke."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"ryze","win":["Ryze","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Ryze"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Ryze pokes with Overload (Q) lines and roots you with Rune Prison (W) — but only once Spell Flux (E) is on you, and you have no Mist and no E dash yet to answer it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist lets you eat his W root, go untargetable on top of yourself, and slow-chase him out of position — your first real kill window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker or Nashor's turns Snip Snip! lethal: drop W as he roots, dash in with Skip 'n Slash, and your %-max-HP Q plus on-hit healing grind him down before he can flux-reset enough Q poke."},{"when":"Late","text":"Past two items Ryze becomes a raid boss — Spell Flux-empowered Q resets fire on near-zero cooldown and burst you from range before you ever reach Mist; do not duel him then."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 6 and drop Hallowed Mist the instant his Rune Prison root lands so his follow-up Q spam fires into your fog while you stay untargetable","All-in with Skip 'n Slash plus Snip Snip! and Needlework on your first-item spike, before his Q stacks turn him into a raid boss","Shove the wave and take plates with your %-max-HP Q while he is still squishy — he out-scales you if it reaches 25+ minutes"],"foe":["Land Rune Prison's point-and-click root, then chain Overload poke and Spell Flux resets to chunk you before you can close the gap","Survive your Level 6 all-in with his root and range, then farm safely to two items where he takes over","Stack Overload damage and items, then kite and burst you from range while Realm Warp roams pressure the map"]},"early":"Ryze owns these levels — his Overload (Q) line outranges everything you have at 1000 units, and Rune Prison (W) roots you the moment Spell Flux (E) is on you, so every step up to last-hit risks a rooted Q combo. You have no Mist and no Skip 'n Slash dash yet, so soak XP at max range, take the poke, and never walk up while his E is off cooldown. The one comfort: his early Q poke can't out-pace your passive healing once you start trading back, and he has no real kill pressure until he lands E-into-W with jungle help or near his tower.","mid":"Six is where this flips. Now you can bait his Rune Prison root, drop Hallowed Mist on top of yourself the instant it lands, and his follow-up Overload spam fires into your fog while you stay untargetable and keep snipping. Dash in with Skip 'n Slash for the attack speed and on-hit range, Snip Snip! his squishy bar with your true-damage center snip, and Needlework slows him so he can't kite back to safety. From your first item — Riftmaker or Nashor's — your %-max-HP Q plus on-hit healing burst him faster than he can flux-reset enough Q poke to answer. Force every trade inside your Mist here.","late":"This is Ryze's game, not yours. Past two items his Spell Flux-empowered Overload resets fire on near-zero cooldown and let him burst you from a screen away before you ever reach Mist range, and his Realm Warp roams pressure the whole map. You out-scale tanks, not a hard-scaling control mage who simply never lets melee touch him. Win this lane on your 6-and-first-item spike, take his tower, and group — if it drags to 25+ minutes he is the raid boss and you are the one getting rooted and one-combo'd from range.","whys":["Ryze outranges you with Overload (Q) at 1000 units and Rune Prison (W) roots once Spell Flux tags you — with no Mist and no Skip 'n Slash dash you cannot answer, so he chunks you for free.","He still pokes with Overload but his W root is on cooldown between casts; you can farm without eating a guaranteed all-in, so the lane evens out into your Level 6 spike.","At 3 Hallowed Mist arrives — Rune Prison and Spell Flux are both targeted at 615, so from outside the fog he cannot cast either and his combo has no opener.","Rune Prison is down 9-11 seconds after each cast; step up in that gap, dash in, snip the true-damage centre, and let passive healing out-sustain his poke.","Needlework's three casts ramp and slow him out of kiting range, and Realm Warp is no combat ultimate — six is your kill window, so Mist his W and commit.","Your first-item all-in beats him before his Overload stacks scale — close the lane and take plates with your %-max-HP Q while he is still fragile.","Ryze out-scales you hard: past two items his Spell Flux-empowered Q resets and range burst you before you reach Mist, so refuse the late duel and end early."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"sejuani","win":["Skill","Sejuani","Sejuani","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Sejuani's window: her W (Winter's Wrath) percent-HP swipe applies Frost, and once you're fully stacked her E (Permafrost) detonates it for a stun — she out-stats your soft Q-only kit and can step up to chunk you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it — drop W the instant her Permafrost (E) stun lands so the follow-up whiffs, then snip her down while untargetable inside the fog."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online: your percent-max-HP Snip Snip! plus the true-damage center snip melt her stacked HP and armor while Thousand Cuts heals you off every cut."},{"when":"Late","text":"Sejuani's R (Glacial Prison) AOE stun is her biggest threat — it pins you out of Hallowed Mist position for her team to collapse, so never facecheck where she can land it."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her E (Permafrost) stun into Hallowed Mist so the detonation's follow-up whiffs while you keep snipping untargetable","Reach Riftmaker and grind her HP/armor bar with percent-max-HP Q plus the true-damage center snip","Use E (Skip 'n Slash) to dash a champ and refund its cooldown, repositioning to land snips without eating free Frost-stacked autos"],"foe":["Stack Frost with W and autos, then detonate with E (Permafrost) to stun you out of mist range for a trade","Use Winter's Wrath (W) percent-HP and her tanky early stats to out-trade your soft levels 1-4","Hit her R (Glacial Prison) AOE stun in a skirmish to lock you down where her team can burst you"]},"early":"Sejuani out-stats you levels 1-4 — she's tankier, and her W (Winter's Wrath) does percent-HP while applying Frost stacks. Once you're fully stacked, her E (Permafrost) detonates them for a stun, so don't sit in range trading autos while you try to land a clunky cone Q at level 1. Respect the W swipe; if she steps up with E ready she can stun-trade and win it. Farm with the tip of Q, soak a little poke, and don't burn your level-3 Q+E chasing — you have no mist yet, and her Permafrost stun cancels your Skip 'n Slash dash mid-air.","mid":"Level 6 is where the lane flips your way. Now you can bait her engage: hold Hallowed Mist and drop it the instant her Permafrost (E) stun lands so the follow-up autos whiff while you keep snipping inside the fog, untargetable to her from outside. Needlework slows her so she can't peel away, and Thousand Cuts heals you off every cut. She's an HP-and-armor target, which is exactly what your magic percent-max-HP Q with its true-damage center snip is built to shred — out-sustain the duel and you take it.","late":"Once Riftmaker is online you are the better duelist all game — the more she builds tank, the harder your Snip Snip! percent-HP and true damage chew through her, and your healing eats her flat tank DPS. The one thing that beats you is her R (Glacial Prison), the AOE stun: in a teamfight it pins you out of Hallowed Mist range and lets her team collapse on you. So fight on your terms, keep mist up for the engage, and never facecheck into a Glacial Prison you can't see coming.","whys":["Sejuani is a weak level-1 too, but so are you — no mist yet, just a cone Q; deny her W last-hits and set up the lane rather than fight into her tankier stats.","She gets Winter's Wrath plus a Frost-stack stun off her E (Permafrost) before your kit comes online, so she out-stats your soft level-2 and can step up to chunk you.","This is your worst window — melee with no untargetability against her percent-HP W and Permafrost stun, and pre-spike, so she owns the trade if you over-step.","You finally have Q+E to poke-and-reset, but her tankier stats and stun still keep the trade even — contest CS, don't commit a full all-in yet.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it — Permafrost is targeted at 560 and cannot reach you inside the fog, and her Frost Armor only ignores slows out of combat.","Riftmaker online means your percent-max-HP Snip plus true-damage center snip shred her HP-and-armor bar faster than she can trade back, and your healing scales off it.","You out-duel her 1v1 forever, but her R (Glacial Prison) AOE stun pins you out of mist in fights — it's a team-fight skill check, not a lane loss."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"sett","win":["Sett","Sett","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Sett owns the early grit — Pit Grit's alternating punches and a charged Haymaker (W) out-trade your six-snip cone Q, so farm at the tip of Q and never feed his Grit bar."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it: bait Facebreaker (E) or The Show Stopper (R) — R is targeted at 400, so from outside the mist he cannot even open the combo."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online — your %-max-HP Q plus mist sustain win the long duel, and Sett's front-loaded W smash needs the fight to stay short."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"The more HP and grit Sett stacks, the harder your Thousand Cuts and %-max-HP Q shred him; his one W smash can't out-burst your per-auto healing."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach 6, bait his E grab or R, then drop Hallowed Mist and step into it so he can't target the stored-W smash that follows the CC","Stretch the duel with Skip 'n Slash CD refunds — your auto-DPS and mist healing beat his front-loaded W burst","Scale to Riftmaker and melt his stacked HP bar with Thousand Cuts %-max-HP autos plus the true-damage center snip"],"foe":["Land his stored-W true-damage smash while you're soft pre-6 with no mist or E reset, and out-grit short trades","Catch you opposite an ally with Facebreaker (E) so the pull stuns not slows, then Knuckle Down into the all-in","Use R to suppress you and guarantee the W smash lands before you can drop mist or reset with Skip 'n Slash"]},"early":"Sett owns these levels and you must respect it — his passive double-punch and a fully charged W (true-damage smash) out-stat your weak level-1 cone Q, and you have no mist and no Skip 'n Slash reset yet to bail. Don't walk into auto range to throw a Snip Snip! when his W bar is glowing — he eats the trade behind the charge and smashes you. Farm with the tip of Q, soak only chip grit, and back off the moment his W meter fills off your face.","mid":"By levels 4-5 you trade more evenly with Q poke and Skip 'n Slash resets, but don't all-in yet — if you maxed Q you're still pre-mist, and his E grab into double-punch out-bursts you. The lane flips at 6: with Needlework and Hallowed Mist you bait his E grab or R, then step into your fog so he can't target the stored-W smash that's supposed to follow the CC, and snip him while he's locked out of you. His all-in is front-loaded; yours wins the longer you stretch it with E cooldown refunds.","late":"This is all yours. The more grit and HP Sett stacks, the harder your Thousand Cuts %-max-HP autos and Snip Snip! shred him, and your per-auto and ability healing off his huge bar out-sustains his single W smash. With Riftmaker and beyond, mist his all-in, slow him with Needlework, and grind — he has no kite and no scaling answer to a fed Gwen. Just bring anti-heal for his grit and don't get caught flat-footed by a fresh E grab around objectives before your mist is up.","whys":["Sett's level-1 passive double-punch and a charged W true-damage smash out-stat your six-snip cone Q, and you have no mist or Skip 'n Slash to escape yet.","He out-grits short trades and lands his W smash before you own a real reset — keep farming, never fight a full W bar.","You get Q poke and Skip 'n Slash refunds to contest, but his E grab into double-punch still trades it roughly even — a skill lane now.","Facebreaker (E) only stuns enemies on opposite sides of him — stand alone on one side and it is a slow, so never let a minion put you in the middle.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it — bait his E grab or R, step into your fog so he can't target the stored-W smash follow-up, then snip him.","Riftmaker/Nashor's online: your %-max-HP Q and mist healing win the long duel his front-loaded W needs to keep short.","You shred his stacked HP and grit harder every item with Thousand Cuts and out-sustain his single smash — he has no kite or scaling answer to a fed Gwen."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"shen","win":["Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Even — Shen's W (Spirit's Refuge) zone blanks your Thousand Cuts on-hit magic and his passive shield-bash sustain trades fine, so farm with the Q tip and stack snips instead of forcing it."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Q+E online — Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP magic and true-damage center snip bypass his armor, and Skip 'n Slash refunds most its cooldown on a champion hit, so you poke-and-reset whenever his E taunt is down."},{"when":"Lvl 6 + 1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's takeover — drop Hallowed Mist as his E taunt-dash lands so his Q-empowered auto whiffs into the fog while you snip his HP bar and heal off the damage."},{"when":"Late","text":"The duel is never the danger — it's Stand United (his global R) shielding and teleporting to a dying ally. Track his ult timer and ping it up so your team doesn't get bailed out of a won fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Snip his stacked HP bar — Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP magic and true center snip ignore his armor-heavy build entirely","Drop Hallowed Mist the instant his E taunt-dash connects so his W-zoned, Q-empowered auto follow-up whiffs while you keep snipping and healing","Use Skip 'n Slash's on-hit cooldown refund to poke-and-reset off his taunt timer, then all-in and shove plates before he answers"],"foe":["Land E taunt to lock you out of repositioning and stick his Q-empowered auto plus W-zoned autos on you","Stand in W (Spirit's Refuge) to block your Thousand Cuts on-hit while his passive shield trades against your ability healing","Concede the 1v1 and use Stand United's global R to win 4v5 skirmishes across the map"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are genuinely even — Shen's W (Spirit's Refuge) blanks your Thousand Cuts on-hit magic for anyone standing in the zone, and his passive shield-bash gives him enough sustain to trade against your ability healing, so don't force a fight you can't win yet. Farm with the tip of Q and stack snips on the wave. The moment you hit 3 with Q+E, the lane tilts: Snip Snip! deals percent-max-HP magic with a true-damage center snip, so his armor means nothing, and Skip 'n Slash refunds most of its cooldown on a champion hit. Respect the E taunt — never get caught mid-snip — but otherwise start chipping his big HP bar.","mid":"This is where you take over. Your Q out-damages anything his kit can sustain because magic and true damage ignore his armor entirely, and Skip 'n Slash lets you poke-and-reset whenever his E taunt is on cooldown. The one thing that beats you is eating his taunt outside your mist — so bait it. When he E-dashes in, drop Hallowed Mist on yourself as the taunt lands: his W-zoned, Q-empowered auto follow-up whiffs into the fog while you keep snipping and healing off the damage you deal. At 6 with Needlework you can slow him on the way out and out-grind any committed trade he starts.","late":"You win the straight 1v1 all game — the more armor and HP Shen stacks, the harder your %-max-HP Q and Riftmaker hit and the more you heal off each snip, and he has no way to out-sustain that. The real problem is never the duel: it's Stand United (his global R) shielding and teleporting to a dying ally across the map. So close the lane hard, shove for plates and turret, and always track his ult — ping it the instant it's up so your team doesn't get bailed out of a won fight. Beat him on the map, not just in lane.","whys":["Shen's W (Spirit's Refuge) blocks your Thousand Cuts on-hit and his shield-bash sustain matches your ability healing — you have no mist value yet, so farm and stack Q snips.","You gain Skip 'n Slash but you're still squishy and your W isn't worth committing; his W keeps zoning your on-hits, so farm rather than fight.","Q+E online: Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP magic and true center snip ignore his armor, and Skip 'n Slash refunds on a champion hit so you out-poke off his taunt cooldown.","You out-trade him as long as you dodge the E taunt — bait it out, then snip his HP bar with magic and true damage his armor can't reduce.","Needlework slows him on the way out and Hallowed Mist makes his committed E-taunt all-in whiff while you heal off every snip you land.","Riftmaker/Nashor's plus mist win extended duels — drop W as his taunt connects, grind his huge HP bar, then shove plates while he recovers.","The more armor and HP he builds the harder your %-max-HP Q hits and the more you heal — you own the 1v1, just track Stand United so it can't bail an ally."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"singed","win":["Singed","Singed","Singed","Singed","Gwen","Singed","Singed"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Singed proxies your wave and walks at you on passive move speed, Flinging you into his poison trail and leaving before your cone Q snips connect — you have no W mist or E dash yet to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your one window: Needlework's slow plus Skip 'n Slash's attack speed lets you actually stick on him long enough for Snip Snip! to bite his huge HP bar with %-max-HP and true damage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Singed's Rylai's turns his poison trail into a slow leash and Liandry's burns your HP as you chase — even your E dash and on-hit range can't close the gap he keeps opening."},{"when":"Late","text":"Move speed plus drain-tank sustain mean he out-paces and out-heals your %-HP grind in any extended fight — the one 'tank' your kit can't crack because he never commits."}],"wants":{"you":["Use Needlework's slow plus Skip 'n Slash's attack speed at 6 to pin him long enough for Snip Snip! to grind his max HP","Rush anti-heal (Sundered Sky / Oblivion line) so your %-HP chip actually out-paces his drain-tank passive sustain","Drop Hallowed Mist on yourself to go untargetable through his Fling and poison ticks, then trade from inside it"],"foe":["Fling you into his poison trail and walk off on raw move speed before your cone Q snips chain","Proxy the wave behind your tower to deny your farm and dodge any all-in near your mist","Build Rylai's plus Liandry's so his slow leash and burning poison run you down once you leave the mist"]},"early":"Singed is the worst kind of 'tank' for me — I want to grind a big HP bar with Snip Snip!, but he never stands still to let me. He proxies my wave behind tower and walks at me on passive move speed, Flings me into his poison trail, and is gone before my cone Q snips even connect. I have no W mist for safety and no E dash to chase until levels 2-3, so early I just lose CS and eat poison ticks. Don't follow him into his trail — that kite is exactly what he wants. Hold the tip of Q for last-hits, drop mist on myself if he Flings me, and accept I'm behind through the first few levels.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay rough: I'm a melee eating poison ticks while his drain-tank passive heals it all back and his move speed keeps him a step ahead. Level 6 is my one real window — Needlework's slow plus Skip 'n Slash's attack speed lets me actually stick on him long enough for Snip Snip! to bite his huge HP bar with %-max-HP and true damage. Bait his Fling first: if I'm sitting in my own Hallowed Mist I'm untargetable to him from outside it, so his repositioning does nothing while I trade. If I can't land E onto him, don't force it — whiffing the dash just hands him a free Fling and a free chase.","late":"This is where Singed buries me. Once he has Rylai's and Liandry's, his poison trail becomes a slow leash that burns my HP every step — my E dash can't open the gap he keeps stretching, and my mist is stationary so it can't escape a foe who simply walks beside it. His move speed plus drain-tank sustain out-heal my %-HP grind in any extended fight, and I never get the committed all-in my kit punishes. Anti-heal helps me trade, but realistically I give up the 1v1, group up, and let my team's CC pin a man who's almost impossible to catch alone.","whys":["Singed proxies your wave and runs you down on passive move speed — you have no W mist or E dash yet to answer his Fling-into-poison.","He keeps full poison-trail uptime while you're still a clunky cone Q with no untargetability — he kites you every step and Flings before your snips chain.","Even once you have Q plus E, he Flings you into the trail and walks off, and his drain-tank passive heals back the chip Snip Snip! lands.","You're a melee eating poison ticks, and his sustain out-heals any %-HP damage your kit deals before you can stack it.","At 6, Needlework's slow plus Skip 'n Slash's attack speed finally lets you stick and grind his huge HP bar with %-max-HP and true damage — your one window.","His Rylai's slow leash and Liandry's burn out-pace your single-item duel — your E can't close the gap and your stationary mist can't chase.","Move speed plus drain-tank sustain beat your %-HP grind in any extended chase — an uncatchable drain-tank is exactly what your kit can't crack."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"sion","win":["Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Respect his charged Q — a fully held knockup is his only real kill setup pre-6, so never sit still in melee range while he winds it up; a tap-cast Q barely hurts."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Q+E online: shred a chunk of his max HP with Snip Snip!, then E-reset out before his long-range E poke and MR-shred can set up the return trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist makes you untargetable to him mid-engage — drop W as his Q charge releases so the knockup whiffs while you keep snipping his bar down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker or Nashor's Tooth turns your %-HP Q into a tank-melter; the more armor and HP Sion stacks, the harder your magic damage and true-damage center snip bite."}],"wants":{"you":["Snip his huge HP bar with Snip Snip! — the center snip's true damage and %-max-HP magic ignore all the armor he builds","Bait a fully charged Decimating Smash into Hallowed Mist so the swing whiffs and you punish the 6-10s gap","Use E's attack speed and bonus on-hit range to weave around his long-range E poke and reset trades repeatedly off the cooldown refund"],"foe":["Land a fully charged Q knockup to pin you and let his jungler collapse for the all-in","Chip you with Roar of the Slayer's 800-range armour shred before you reach mist range, then shove and roam","Survive lane, build full tank, and convert into a W-shield frontline whose knockup engage your single-target damage can't peel alone"]},"early":"Sion can only really hurt you with a fully charged Decimating Smash (Q), so never stand still in melee while he winds it up — sidestep the slow charge and a tap-cast is harmless. Roar of the Slayer (E) pokes from 800 and shreds your armour, not your MR, so it cannot out-damage what A Thousand Cuts restores once you trade back in melee. At level 1 you are both soft, so just farm; by level 3 your Q+E snips a chunk of his big bar and resets out before his E returns.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a wash — he can shove and chip with E from range while you wait for your spike, so don't force a fight without W up. At 6 the lane tilts hard your way: Hallowed Mist makes you untargetable to him while he stands outside it, so bait his charged Q, drop the fog as the knockup releases, and it whiffs while you keep snipping. His max HP is your ammo — Snip Snip!'s true-damage center and %-max-HP magic shred a tank far faster than his E can chip you down.","late":"You win the straight 1v1 all game — every point of armor and HP Sion stacks just feeds your %-max-HP Q and true-damage snip, and his single-target threat is one telegraphed knockup you can mist or sidestep. The only thing that flips is teamfights: his charged Q and W-shield AOE make him a strong engage frontline, so don't let him land a five-man knockup on your carries. Snowball your lane lead, take his plates and tower, and translate it before he becomes a body your team has to peel around.","whys":["You are both weak level-1s — he has only a slow charged Q knockup and you have a clunky cone Q, so just deny his last-hits and dodge the windup.","Your level-2 tool plus passive %-max-HP on-hit damage starts chipping his big bar faster than his E poke chips yours.","Q+E lets you snip his max HP with the true-damage center, then E-reset out before his long-range E poke returns.","Roar of the Slayer shreds armour, not MR, so his 800-range chip is physical — farm through it and wait for 6 rather than forcing.","Needlework and Hallowed Mist flip the lane: mist his charged Q so the knockup whiffs while you keep snipping his HP down.","Riftmaker or Nashor's makes your %-HP magic and true snip melt the armor and HP he builds — your hardest tank-shredding window.","He out-scales nothing about your 1v1 — every tank item feeds your %-max-HP Q; only respect his teamfight knockup, not the duel."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"swain","win":["Swain","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Swain's only real window — his Death's Hand (Q) bolts and Vision of Empire (W) bomb chip you before you have Mist, and a landed Nevermove (E) root locks you for a free Q+autoattack trade you can't escape."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hallowed Mist plus Needlework online: drop W as he casts Demonic Ascension so you snip him untargetable from inside the cloud while his R drain heals off minions and the wave, not off you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's spike: your percent-max-HP Snip Snip! shreds his HP-stacking drain-tank build and Gwen's anti-heal cuts the sustain his W and R lean on."},{"when":"Late","text":"Extended fights are yours — the longer you brawl in Mist the more your Q true-damage center and Thousand Cuts on-hit heal stack against a drain-mage whose only out-trade was early poke."}],"wants":{"you":["Sidestep Nevermove (E) on its RETURN trip — the outgoing wave does not root, so keep moving the moment it passes you","Reach 6 and your first item, then all-in inside Hallowed Mist where he can't target you and your %-HP Q out-trades his drain","Build anti-heal early (Oblivion Orb) to gut the lifesteal Demonic Ascension and his W rely on"],"foe":["Land Nevermove (E) when you're cornered on minions so the root chains into his W bomb and Death's Hand burst","Poke you down levels 1-3 with Death's Hand (Q) and Vision of Empire (W) before you have Mist or E to close","Force an open extended brawl where Demonic Ascension's AOE drain out-sustains you if you're caught outside your cloud"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to Swain — his Death's Hand (Q) bolts and Vision of Empire (W) bomb out-range your clunky cone Q, and a single landed Nevermove (E) root chains into a trade you have no Mist or E dash to escape yet. Do not walk up to last-hit with minions stacked behind you; that is exactly where his slow-traveling E lands clean. Farm with the tip of Snip Snip! and its true-damage center when it's safe, eat a little poke, and rush an Oblivion Orb component — your Thousand Cuts healing and %-HP scaling mean his chip never converts into a kill.","mid":"This is where it flips. At 6, drop Hallowed Mist the instant he commits Demonic Ascension — its drain is an AOE around him, so he heals off the wave while you snip him untargetable from inside the cloud. Bait the E: once Nevermove is on cooldown, dash in with Skip 'n Slash, snip his HP, and your anti-heal turns his W and R lifesteal into nothing. Your Riftmaker spike lets you win every extended trade he tries to drag out.","late":"You own the late 1v1 outright as long as you respect one button — Nevermove. Swain stacks HP and Demonic Embrace to fuel his drain, which is the worst possible build into your percent-max-HP plus true-damage Q: the bigger his bar, the harder you snip and the more Thousand Cuts heals you. Fight in your Mist, anti-heal his R, and never facecheck brush where a hidden E can pin you. Skirmish him down before he can ever land the one root that lets him reset the trade on his terms.","whys":["Pre-Mist and pre-6, his Death's Hand and Vision of Empire out-range your cone Q, and a landed Nevermove is a free trade you have no dash to answer.","You get a real tool (E or Q max) but stay soft — farm the wave and don't step into Nevermove range to throw a snip he can punish.","Q plus Skip 'n Slash lets you poke-and-reset, but his W+Q burst still out-trades you at range until you have Mist, so contest only when his E is down.","His poke loses value as your Thousand Cuts sustain and anti-heal come online — trade when Nevermove is on cooldown and bank the lane.","Hallowed Mist nullifies Demonic Ascension — the form lasts only while he drains a champion, so untargetable inside the fog you make his ultimate expire.","Riftmaker plus anti-heal: your %-HP Snip shreds his HP-stacking drain-tank build and guts the lifesteal his W and R rely on.","Extended Mist brawls compound your Q true damage and Thousand Cuts healing against a drain-mage whose AOE you simply stand outside of."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"sylas","win":["Skill","Sylas","Skill","Sylas","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Sylas can Abscond-Abduct (E) onto you and Chain Lash (Q) poke before you have Hallowed Mist to hide in, and Kingslayer (W) heals the trade back — his cleanest window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it: drop mist on his Abduct so he lands in the cloud and you go untargetable, slow him with R, and out-sustain him with passive healing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker online — your %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus mist wins the extended AP duel his burst-and-Kingslayer pattern cannot rush."},{"when":"Lvl 6+","text":"His R Hijacks your Needlework — bait it onto a teammate or never ult first in a fight you do not need to."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 6 and drop Hallowed Mist as his Abduct (E) connects so you go untargetable and his Q-W follow-up whiffs","Bait his R before you cast Needlework so he cannot Hijack your ult mid-fight","Scale to Riftmaker where %-HP Snip Snip! out-grinds his Kingslayer burst in a long duel"],"foe":["Land Abscond-Abduct (E) into Chain Lash (Q) to poke you before your mist is up","Save R to Hijack your Needlework and turn the AP duel in his favor","Use Kingslayer (W) heal to win short trades and recover his poke back early"]},"early":"Sylas is a real AP lane bully before you spike — his Abscond (E) closes 400 and the recast chains him back onto you, his Chain Lash (Q) pokes from 775, and Kingslayer (W) heals the trade back, while you have no Hallowed Mist yet. Do not walk up to throw a cone Q he can answer with the recast and a W heal-trade. Farm with the tip of Snip Snip!, soak a little poke, and respect that his W heals off champions — your sustain only out-grinds his once you own your full kit and Grievous Wounds.","mid":"Level 6 is your flip. When he commits Abscond (E) and recasts onto you, drop Hallowed Mist as he arrives so he is standing inside the cloud and you go untargetable while you keep snipping, then slow him with Needlework so the dash cannot kite back out. The one trap: Hijack is only 30 seconds at rank 3, so never open with your ult in a fight you can win without it — bait the R, then commit.","late":"This stays a coinflip AP duel, and your edge is the extended fight. His Q poke plus Kingslayer (W) is burst-and-sustain, but your Riftmaker plus %-max-HP Snip Snip! grinds him down over a longer trade he cannot rush, and mist eats his all-in. Just never ult into him first in a teamfight — a Hijacked Needlework chaining off your own takedowns is how this even lane swings against you.","whys":["Both of you are soft level 1, but he has Abscond (E) mobility and Chain Lash (Q) poke while you have only a clunky cone Q and no mist.","Sylas owns this: his Abscond-Abduct (E) into Chain Lash (Q) pokes you freely before you have Hallowed Mist to hide in.","You get Q-plus-E to poke-and-reset, but his Kingslayer (W) heal trades evenly with your sustain pre-spike.","He edges 4-5: still no mist if you maxed Q, so his E-Q poke into Kingslayer heal out-stats you in a straight trade.","Needlework plus mist flips it — Abscond and Kingslayer are both 400 range, so from outside the fog neither reaches you while you keep snipping.","Riftmaker plus %-max-HP Snip Snip! wins the extended duel his burst-and-Kingslayer pattern cannot rush, and mist nullifies his all-in.","Two even AP scalers trade blows late, but his Hijacked Needlework off your ult is the swing that keeps it a coinflip."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"tahmkench","win":["Skill","Tahm Kench","Skill","Tahm Kench","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"His Tongue Lash stacks An Acquired Taste, and the third stack stuns; if he marks you and walks up, that stun unlocks Devour (R) and bursts you before you have a second point in Snip Snip! or any mist to hide behind."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus a maxed Q-W flips the lane: drop Hallowed Mist as he lashes in so his devour whiffs on an untargetable you, then R-slow him so he can't tongue away while your percent-HP snips grind his grey-health bar."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker or Nashor's Tooth is your real spike: extended duels inside Hallowed Mist let percent-max-HP Snip Snip! plus its true-damage center snip out-shred the giant HP bar he keeps stacking faster than grey-health refills it."},{"when":"Late","text":"His grey-health passive heals between trades and his W can negate your committed snip damage in one button, so if you can't close a duel inside one mist window he just devours, walks it off, and roams away with R."}],"wants":{"you":["Drag fights into Hallowed Mist and grind his max-HP bar with percent-HP Snip Snip! plus the true-damage center snip, since the more HP he stacks the harder your passive and Q hit","Rush anti-heal (Tabis are useless, build Morellonomicon/Oblivion Orb line) so his grey-health passive can't undo the chunk your snips deal","Hit Level 6 and your first item, where R-slow plus mist untargetability let you commit a full duel he can't tongue out of and can't out-sustain"],"foe":["Land Tongue Lash, stack his passive to three, and stun-into-W-devour you levels 2-3 before you have mist or a second Q point","Use Devour (R) to swallow your committed snip burst, or Abyssal Dive to disengage, then let Thick Skin regen reset the trade","Roam with R to make plays bot or jungle and turn his utility-tank scaling into a team lead while the lane itself stays even"]},"early":"Tahm's Tongue Lash is the whole early game: each Q (or auto) stacks his passive marker, and the third stack stuns, so the danger is letting him mark you up and walk in for stun-into-W-devour while you're still mist-less and on one point of Snip Snip! pre-2. Last-hit with the tip of your Q cone and accept some chip; your percent-HP snips already chunk his big bar and your passive heals off the damage, but his grey-health regen wins it back, so don't expect to win a raw poke war yet. The one rule levels 2-3: never sit in lash range at a full stack count, because that stun is his only kill window before you outscale.","mid":"Level 6 is your flip. Needlework's slow plus a maxed Q-W means you can drop Hallowed Mist exactly as he Tongue-Lashes in, go untargetable while the stun and his follow-up whiff, then R-slow him so he can't tongue away while you snip the giant bar down. Your passive heals off every snip that lands on him, so the more HP he stacks the more you out-sustain the trade. Keep anti-heal up: Thick Skin's stored-damage shield, off a 3-second cooldown, is the only thing keeping these trades even instead of yours, and Devour (R) is the one button that still cancels your burst.","late":"This stays a grind, not a stomp. Your percent-max-HP snips and true-damage center snip are exactly what punish a Tahm who stacks HP, and a clean mist duel shreds him, but Thick Skin regenerates grey health between every trade and Devour (R) can swallow you in one cast, so if you can't close one mist window cleanly he just resets. Burst him inside a single Hallowed Mist with anti-heal up; if he dives away or roams with R, don't chase a drain-tank across the map, take the tower and the tempo and let your scaling do the rest.","whys":["Both of you are weak at Level 1 - your cone Q is clunky to land cleanly and his Q is single-stack poke, so just last-hit and set the wave.","His Tongue Lash stacks to a third-stack stun into W-devour, and you have no mist yet to dodge the burst - concede the level.","Q poke and your percent-HP snips chunk his bar, but his grey-health regen heals it back while neither of you can commit, so it's a wash.","You're a mist-less melee with no untargetability yet and his grey-health out-sustains your chip - levels 2-3 are his only real kill window.","Needlework plus mist untargetability plus E reset finally beats his sustain - drop W as he lashes in, R-slow him, and snip the giant bar down.","Riftmaker or Nashor's turns one mist duel into a kill - percent-max-HP snips out-shred his HP-stacking faster than grey-health refills it.","He never truly falls off - Thick Skin resets grey health between trades, Devour swallows your burst, and his R roams, so a missed mist window slides the lane back to even-or-his."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"teemo","win":["Teemo","Skill","Skill","Teemo","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Teemo's Blinding Dart shuts off your Thousand Cuts on-hit autos and his Toxic Shot poison chips you while you have no Mist and no Skip 'n Slash yet — last-hit at max range and eat it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it: E in, drop W on top, and the R-slow runs down a Teemo whose blind and move-speed kite can't peel a target standing in the untargetable cloud."},{"when":"1st item","text":"On Riftmaker/Nashor's, Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP plus its true-damage center snip and your ability healing out-grind his Toxic Shot chip in any trade that lasts past one blind."},{"when":"Late","text":"His shrooms wall every objective choke and he splitpushes a side — the 1v1 stays yours, but he turns into a vision/map problem, so cash the lead before ~25 min."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait the Blinding Dart, then Skip 'n Slash in and drop Hallowed Mist before his next auto so his kite whiffs into the cloud","Hit 6 and force the all-in — Needlework's slow plus W untargetability run down a Teemo with no dash and no escape","Close the lane on your Riftmaker spike, before his shroom map-control and splitpush start mattering"],"foe":["Land Blinding Dart on your empowered autos every trade and kite back on Toxic Shot's passive move speed","Stack E poison and farm at range so you never close the gap to your Mist all-in","Place shrooms on chokes, scale, and turn the game into a splitpush and vision war"]},"early":"Teemo owns the first two levels and I just swallow it — his Blinding Dart turns off my Thousand Cuts on-hit autos and his Toxic Shot poison chips me while I have no Hallowed Mist and no Skip 'n Slash to close. I do NOT walk up to throw a Snip Snip! he can blind through and kite away from; I last-hit at the back of the wave and accept the poison. The saving grace is his DPS can't out-pace my eventual ability healing and he has zero escape the second I do reach him, so I farm toward 6 rather than trade.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are my worst stretch — still a short-range threat eating poison, so I don't force anything and just keep my Mist and E up. Then 6 changes the lane: I Skip 'n Slash onto him, drop Hallowed Mist on top of us so his autos go untargetable, and Needlework-slow him so his blind and move-speed kite can't peel. Bait the blind first — if I dash in while Blinding Dart is up I've burned the window; commit when it's on cooldown and let my ability healing out-grind his Toxic Shot ticks.","late":"Straight up I win the 1v1 all game — once I'm on Riftmaker, Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP plus its true-damage center snip and my heal-on-ability-damage eat his poison chip in any extended duel, and he has no dash to break the Mist. The problem is Teemo stops being a laner and becomes a map issue: shrooms wall off every objective choke and he splitpushes a side. So I snowball this lane and end before ~25 minutes, and I never facecheck unwarded brush near Dragon or Baron.","whys":["Teemo blinds my empowered autos with Blinding Dart and pokes with Toxic Shot while I have no Mist or Skip 'n Slash to close — I just farm and eat it.","Even ground: his blind-poke still out-trades a mistless me, but I out-sustain it and he has no escape, so neither side commits.","I get Snip Snip! plus Skip 'n Slash to poke-and-reset, but he can blind the dash auto and kite the move speed back — it stays a coinflip skirmish.","Levels 4-5 are my worst window — still short-range against his blind and poison with no all-in threat yet, so this stretch is his.","At 6 Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it: I make the all-in untargetable, R-slow a champion with no dash, and heal through his DPS.","Riftmaker online means Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP and true damage plus my ability healing beat his Toxic Shot chip in any extended duel.","I still win the 1v1, but his shrooms and splitpush turn it into a map problem — respect mushroom walls and end early."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"trundle","win":["Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Gwen","Skill","Trundle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Trundle's Chomp (Q) saps AD you barely use and resets his auto, while King's Tribute heals him off dying minions and Frozen Domain (W) boosts it — concede CS, don't auto-war."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist is your one clean window — drop W on his Pillar so he can't target you, snip his fat HP bar with %-max-HP Q, and chain R if he Flashes out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker plus Nashor's lets your %-HP Q and true-damage center snip finally out-grind his base healing — force the all-in inside mist before his Subjugate comes back up."},{"when":"Late","text":"His R Subjugate rips a chunk of your armor and MR and heals him off it, refunding the HP your snips chip away — a fed Trundle reclaims any extended fight, so kill him before two items."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 6 and fight only inside Hallowed Mist so his Pillar engage commits into fog he can't target through while you keep snipping","Rush anti-heal (Sorcerer's then Oblivion Orb) so your %-HP Snip Snip sticks through his Chomp lifesteal and Subjugate drain","Spike on Riftmaker and all-in before he stacks enough armor/MR for Subjugate to steal a meaningful amount"],"foe":["Farm on Frozen Domain so King's Tribute heals amplified off every dying minion, winning the level 1-5 attrition Gwen can't sustain","Stand in his W zone for the move/attack speed and Pillar (E) you into a wall to stick the fight","Save Subjugate for the long fight to strip your resists, heal off them, and out-sustain everything your snips chip off"]},"early":"Drop the \"Gwen beats tanks\" instinct here — Trundle is a drain-tank, not a static one. His sustain is King's Tribute, healing off every unit that dies near him and amplified while he stands on Frozen Domain (W); Chomp (Q) resets his auto every 3.5s and the AD it saps costs an AP Gwen almost nothing. With no mist and no burst, don't contest the level 1-3 stat-check. Last-hit at max Q range and never dash at a Trundle holding Pillar of Ice (E).","mid":"Level 6 is your window and you have to take it. With Needlework, a full Q-W-E rotation, and anti-heal started, drop Hallowed Mist on top of his Pillar so his engage commits into a fog he can't target you through, then snip his huge HP bar — your %-max-HP magic Q and the true-damage center snip ignore the armor he stacks. Slow him with R if he Flashes out. This is the one stage where your healing-on-damage outpaces his Chomp sustain; everywhere else he edges you.","late":"Here's the honest part: late, his R Subjugate strips a chunk of your armor and MR and heals him off it, directly refunding the HP your snips grind away — the same drain that lets him hard-counter bruisers answers Gwen's kit better than a normal tank's. Your Riftmaker spike is real, so the cleanest path is to force the all-in inside mist around first item and snowball, because a two-item Trundle reclaims the extended duel. Never get baited into a long fight on his terms with Subjugate up.","whys":["No mist, no burst, and King's Tribute heals him off every dying minion — you lose the level 1 stat-check.","His W zone gives him the move and attack speed to stay glued and trade for free; Gwen has one ability and no reset yet.","Q-E poke is online, but Pillar of Ice walls Skip 'n Slash outright and the attrition still starts at a deficit.","This is Gwen's worst window pre-mist — a melee with no untargetability against a drain-tank who out-sustains her chip.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it: mist his Pillar engage, then %-HP Q and true-damage center snip shred his HP bar faster than he heals.","Riftmaker plus anti-heal lets your %-HP Q out-grind his Chomp drain — but only if you commit inside mist before Subjugate is up.","His R Subjugate steals your resists and heals off them, refunding your snips — a two-item Trundle out-sustains any extended duel."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"tryndamere","win":["Tryndamere","Tryndamere","Tryndamere","Tryndamere","Gwen","Skill","Tryndamere"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Tryndamere's crit autos and Bloodlust healing out-stat your slow six-snip cone before you have Mist or Skip 'n Slash, so you have no answer to his early spin-trades."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist finally gives you a window: drop the fog so he spins on an untargetable target, slow him with R, and out-sustain his Bloodlust with your ability healing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Nashor's/Riftmaker narrows the gap, but only after you've slotted Executioner's so your percent-HP Q out-grinds Bloodlust — even then his crit kiting still edges the open lane."},{"when":"Tryndamere R","text":"Undying Rage survives your full Q-R-auto burst at 1 HP for 5 seconds, then he crits you down the moment your Mist and Needlework are spent."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive to 6, then bait his E-engage into Hallowed Mist so his spin whiffs on an untargetable target while you keep chipping with Q and R","Rush Executioner's so your percent-max-HP Q and passive out-grind his Bloodlust sustain instead of feeding it","Use Skip 'n Slash to reset spacing and refuse extended spin-fights until Nashor's/Riftmaker is online"],"foe":["Spin-kite your Snip Snip cone and heal the chip straight back with Bloodlust before you can scale","Hold Undying Rage to eat your burst at 1 HP, then crit you out once your Mist and R are on cooldown","Catch you fleeing so Mocking Shout's back-turned slow lands, then Spinning Slash outside Mist range"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are rough — no Mist, no Skip 'n Slash dash yet, just a slow six-snip cone, while his crit autos and Bloodlust heal him through your poke and let him win every spin-trade. Do NOT short-trade him into the wall; his spin shreds you and Bloodlust erases the chip instantly. Last-hit at the tip of Snip Snip, give ground when he E-dashes in, and accept you're behind until you hit 6.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay his — he can W-slow and E onto you before your kit is fully online, so keep farming and don't facecheck his all-in. At 6 the lane flips for one window: drop Hallowed Mist as his E lands so you go untargetable while he spins on nothing, slow him with Needlework, and let your ability healing out-grind Bloodlust. Bait his engage into the fog, never fight him in the open lane.","late":"Late, respect Undying Rage above all — your Q-R-auto burst will NOT kill through the 5-second 1-HP window, and the instant your R and Mist are down he crits you to death. Slot Executioner's early so your percent-HP Q actually out-trades Bloodlust, hug your Mist, and never commit a full combo while his R is up. He out-duels you in the open; you only win standing inside the fog with cooldowns ready.","whys":["No Mist and no Skip 'n Slash yet — his crit autos and Bloodlust heal beat your slow six-snip cone in every level-1 spin-trade.","He has a real crit spin window while you're still a soft melee farming — contesting his trades just feeds Bloodlust.","You can Q-poke and Skip 'n Slash to reset, but his crit DPS plus Bloodlust sustain still out-stat you before your spike.","Mocking Shout slows only enemies with backs turned — face him, and his engage loses its setup.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips this one window — go untargetable in the fog, slow with R, and out-sustain his Bloodlust.","At first item it's genuinely close: your Nashor's/Executioner's spike trades into his crit, so the kill comes down to who lands the engage cleanly.","Undying Rage survives your full burst and his crits finish you once your R and Mist are spent — he reclaims the duel."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"urgot","win":["Urgot","Urgot","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Urgot's W Purge fires his shotgun legs on a short cooldown and out-DPSes your slow cone Q while you have no mist and no E dash yet — eat the shove and farm."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus a ranked Hallowed Mist flips it: when he Disdain-charges in, drop W on yourself so his Purge legs hit an untargetable Gwen and his combo whiffs."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online — your %-max-HP Snip Snip! and true-damage center line shred his tanky HP bar faster than his Purge legs grind through your mist sustain."},{"when":"Lvl 6+","text":"Fear Beyond Death is the kill button all game — never drop below its execute threshold near him, or one R recast deletes you and fears your escape."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive to 6, then bait his Disdain charge into your Hallowed Mist so his Purge legs and R follow-up hit an untargetable Gwen","Spam Snip Snip! to melt his stacked max-HP bar with %-HP magic plus the center true-damage snip, healing off every hit via Thousand Cuts","Rush Riftmaker and an anti-heal item so his sustained Purge DPS can't out-trade your passive healing in a long mist fight"],"foe":["Win levels 1-3 with W Purge legs before Gwen has mist up or her E dash to reset trades","Land Disdain to charge-flip her out of mist range and pin her for a free Purge burst","Drop her below the Fear Beyond Death execute line, then R-recast for the kill and a fear on anyone nearby"]},"early":"Urgot owns the first three levels — his W Purge fires his shotgun legs on a falling cooldown, 12 seconds at rank 1 down to nothing at rank 5, while you have a slow cone Q, no E dash yet, and no Hallowed Mist to hide in. Don't walk up to trade Q for his Purge; it prioritises whoever he last tagged with Corrosive Charge and it triggers Echoing Flames off his legs. Last-hit at max Q range, soak the shove, and respect that Disdain shields him on the charge and can flip you under tower. Your %-HP Q does answer his eventual bulk, but at level 1-2 you simply don't have the kit to fight him.","mid":"Once you hit W and then 6 this becomes a real fight. Bait his Disdain charge — when he commits the flip and turns on Purge, drop Hallowed Mist on yourself so you're untargetable while his shotgun legs hit nothing and his combo stalls. Snip Snip! through the mist grinds his big HP bar with %-max-HP magic plus the true-damage center line, and Thousand Cuts heals you off every chunk. The one thing that kills you here is his R: never let him land a Disdain while you're below the Fear Beyond Death execute threshold, because the execute deletes you and the fear locks down your dash out.","late":"Past your first item this is genuinely even-to-yours — Riftmaker and anti-heal mean your %-HP Snip shreds whatever bulk he stacks faster than his Purge legs grind you, and Hallowed Mist resets the duel every time it comes back up. But Urgot is a sustained-DPS bruiser-tank who never fully falls off: Fear Beyond Death is a kill button in every skirmish, so the lane stays a coinflip around picks. Don't facecheck or commit your E dash when his R is up and you're below the execute line — that's the only way he reclaims a fight you should otherwise out-grind.","whys":["His W Purge legs out-DPS your slow cone Q at level 1 with no mist to answer — farm and concede the shove.","Urgot still out-stats you with Purge up while you have no untargetability and no E dash yet — don't contest trades.","Post-6 you get Q poke and the E reset, but his %-HP Purge trades back even — it's a true coinflip skirmish now.","Pre-mist you're a melee eating his Purge DPS, but your %-HP Q answers his bulk — neither side wins the trade clean.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist lets you bait his Disdain charge into the fog so his Purge and R whiff while you snip and heal.","Riftmaker and anti-heal make your %-max-HP Snip shred his tankiness faster than his Purge legs grind you down.","Both of you scale into bruiser-tanks — your mist resets duels but his Fear Beyond Death execute keeps every skirmish a coinflip."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"vayne","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Vayne","Gwen","Gwen","Vayne"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your worst window — Hallowed Mist isn't online until 6, so Vayne tumbles around your slow Snip Snip cone and the Silver Bolts third hit chips %-max-HP true with nothing to untarget behind."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus full Q-W-E flips it: bait the Condemn, drop Hallowed Mist as she commits so the knockback and bolts whiff while you stay untargetable, then E-in and grind her squishy frame with %-HP Snip."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's is your real spike — E-dash closes past her tumble, Hallowed Mist soaks her kite, and Gwen's heal-on-damage outlasts her DPS before the third bolt lands."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Vayne's window — fully-itemised Silver Bolts true damage shreds your HP regardless of build, Final Hour's invis makes her impossible to pin, and Condemn knocks you off every time you E in."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 6 and drop Hallowed Mist onto her commit so the Condemn follow-up and Silver Bolts whiff while you keep snipping from untargetable","E-dash through the gap she opens with Tumble, anti-heal her lifesteal, and out-sustain the trade with Thousand Cuts heal-on-damage","Snowball your Riftmaker spike, shove for plates and roam before her third item turns the Tumble-kite unbeatable"],"foe":["Stack Silver Bolts to the third hit for the %-max-HP true proc, then Tumble out before your Snip Snip cone connects","Condemn you into a wall to stun-burst, or just use the knockback to peel you off when you E-dash in","Survive to 2+ items where %-true damage and Final Hour's invis-resets out-scale even Gwen's late game"]},"early":"Neither of you wants to fight levels 1-3 — you're a clunky cone Q with no Hallowed Mist yet and she's a squishy hypercarry farming for items, so this is a true even race. Last-hit with the tip of Snip Snip and don't walk into her auto range to throw a Q she can just Tumble out of. Silver Bolts only hurt once she stacks the third hit on you, so deny her free poke and never let her land a free third-proc while you're cornered with no mist to hide in.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your scary window — still no Hallowed Mist, so her Tumble-kite and %-true bolts chip a melee with nowhere to hide. Farm it out and wait for 6. The moment you hit Needlework it flips: bait her Condemn, drop the mist so the knockback and her bolts whiff while you stay untargetable, then E-dash in and grind her squishy frame with %-HP Snip and Thousand Cuts healing. An anti-heal item makes her lifesteal-sustain matter far less in the extended fight.","late":"This is where Vayne reclaims it. Fully-itemised, her Silver Bolts %-true damage shreds your max HP no matter how much you build, Final Hour's invisibility resets the kite faster than you can E-reset onto her, and Condemn knocks you off every time you commit. One Hallowed Mist buys a single good fight, not a sustained chase. Win the lane on your Riftmaker spike, take plates and roam, and let your team body her in the 5v5 — do not try to solo a three-item Vayne in the sidelane.","whys":["You're a weak level-1 cone Q with no mist, but she's an equally fragile carry who just wants to farm — neither side has a reason to commit, so it's a last-hit race.","Still a soft melee with one ability online; she has no incentive to fight either, so trade last-hits and deny her any Silver Bolts stacks.","Q plus E lets you contest, but she can Tumble the cone and reset the kite — it stays a genuine farm-race, not a kill lane.","Your worst window: no Hallowed Mist yet, so her third-hit Silver Bolts %-true and Tumble-kiting chip you with no untargetability to answer.","Needlework plus full Q-W-E flips it — mist her Condemn, stay untargetable through the knockback, and your %-HP Snip out-trades her paper frame.","Riftmaker/Nashor's is your real spike: E-dash past the Tumble, mist soaks the kite, and Thousand Cuts healing eats her DPS before the third bolt procs.","She out-scales hard — full-build Silver Bolts true damage melts your HP and Final Hour's invis resets the Tumble, so play safe and group rather than duel."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"vladimir","win":["Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Pre-pool Vlad has no escape — your Snip Snip! cone chunks him for %-max-HP magic plus its true-damage center snip while his only answer is a slow-charging Tides of Blood you can sidestep. Auto-trade now."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework's slow plus Hallowed Mist's untargetable cloud lets you all-in the instant Sanguine Pool is on its ~28s cooldown — bait the pool, then dump R. Your single hardest clean-kill window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online: your %-max-HP Q and ability-heal out-grind a pre-Rylai Vlad in any extended duel — Skip 'n Slash refunds on-hit so you reset E and stay on him. Force it, take plates."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Full-AP Vlad with Rylai/Liandry's kites you, pools your Needlework, and his ult-amped drain heals through your DPS. He out-scales you outright — your dominance ends, so close the lane before this."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Sanguine Pool with a feint or single Q, then commit Q-E-R all-in while it's on its long cooldown","Drop Hallowed Mist as he steps up so his Tides of Blood poke and ult whiff while you snip from inside the cloud","Snowball levels 6-through-first-item and end the lane before his full-AP Rylai/Liandry's scaling takes over"],"foe":["Sanguine Pool the moment you commit to go untargetable, dodge Needlework, and reset every all-in you start","Charge Tides of Blood where no minion blocks it and stack Transfusion to whittle you before you reach mist trades","Survive to Rylai's and Liandry's, then out-scale you into an unkillable drain-tank AP threat your Q can't punish"]},"early":"Vlad is one of the softest level-1s in the game, and with no Sanguine Pool yet he has no way to dodge you — so you out-trade him outright. Walk up and land your Snip Snip! cone for the %-max-HP chunk plus its true-damage center snip; his only answer is a slow-charging Tides of Blood you can sidestep. Deny his Transfusion (Q) last-hits to choke the sustain that defines his lane, and don't overstay in his minions where his E fully charges. You're soft too before Hallowed Mist, so trade and reset, don't all-in yet.","mid":"This is your takeover window. Once you hit Hallowed Mist, drop it on yourself as he tries to E-poke or step up — he can't target you from outside the cloud while you keep snipping with bonus on-hit range from Skip 'n Slash. At 6, Needlework's slow locks the chase, but he WILL Sanguine Pool the instant you commit, so bait the pool first (a feint or single Q) then dump your real R-E all-in while it's on its ~28s cooldown. A pre-Rylai Vlad simply loses the extended duel to your ability-healing and %-max-HP Q.","late":"Here's the honest part: full-AP Vlad out-scales you. Once he has Rylai's and Liandry's he kites you with the slow, pools your Needlework to dodge it cleanly, and his ult-amplified Tides of Blood plus Transfusion drain heal him through your DPS faster than you can grind him down. Your %-max-HP Q still bites, because Crimson Pact converts every point of his AP into 1.6 bonus health — it is his healing, not his tankiness, that beats you, so anti-heal is mandatory. Win lane hard from 6 to your first item, take towers, and shove the game toward your team before he closes you out.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1 — deny his Transfusion last-hits and set the lane up instead of forcing a trade you can't finish pre-W.","You hit Hallowed Mist and out-stat a pre-pool Vlad — land your Q cone for the %-max-HP chunk before his Tides of Blood can charge.","Your Q poke and Skip 'n Slash reset out-trade his charged E, and he still has no Sanguine Pool to escape with.","You out-grind a pre-Rylai Vlad in any extended duel — your ability-healing eats his drain and his poke can't sustain you off.","Needlework's slow plus the untargetable mist lets you all-in the moment his pool is down — your hardest clean kill window.","Your Riftmaker spike beats his first AP item; %-max-HP Q and mist win the extended duel, so close the lane before he scales.","Full-AP Vlad out-scales you — he kites with Rylai's, pools your R, and drains through your DPS, so hand him to your team."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"volibear","win":["Skill","Skill","Gwen","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q+E online you start chipping him with Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP cone and refund Skip 'n Slash off the champ hit, then back out before his W bite heal is up to trade back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hallowed Mist plus Needlework blanks his all-in: Thundering Smash stuns the first enemy he attacks, so drop the mist as he closes and, untargetable, there is nobody for him to attack. Then R-slow and snip."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker is your peak power spike — extended duels parked in the mist heal you off his fat HP bar via Thousand Cuts while Snip Snip!'s true-damage center snip ignores every tank item he buys."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"His one threat window before your mist: a stacked passive auto into Thundering Smash and a Sky Splitter slow can pin and burst you with no Hallowed Mist to hide in — never sit in Frenzied Maul range."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his Q-dash + E-fling engage, then drop Hallowed Mist so the W bite follow-up whiffs while you stand untargetable and keep snipping","Stack Thousand Cuts autos and Snip Snip!'s true-damage core on his huge HP bar — the more tank he builds the harder your %-max-HP shred hits and the more your abilities heal you","Reach Riftmaker and grind long mist duels where Gwen's per-ability healing out-sustains his W bite heal and turret-shielded brawl"],"foe":["Land Sky Splitter (E) to slow you out of mist range, then chain Thundering Smash's stun before your cooldowns reset","Use W bite's heal and slow to win the short pre-3 trades and out-sustain your poke before you scale","Pop R to disable your turret and dive you with the shield and his tanky stats once he has a couple of health items"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are even and clunky — you have no Hallowed Mist yet and Snip Snip! is a slow short-range cone, while his W bite heals and slows any short trade he forces, so just farm with the tip of Q and stay out of his auto range. Watch his passive: a stacked Volibear auto hits hard and his Q-dash closes distance fast. By level 3, Q+E flips it — poke with the %-max-HP cone, hit Skip 'n Slash for the cooldown refund off the champ hit, and step back before his W heal is back up.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a coinflip until you hit 6 — he can Thundering Smash in and Sky Splitter you into a Frenzied Maul with no Hallowed Mist to save you, so play around that 10-12 second engage cooldown and don't facecheck. At 6 it's yours: Thundering Smash stuns the first enemy he attacks, so drop the mist as he closes and, untargetable, he has nobody to hit. Stand in it, R-slow him, and keep snipping. Your per-ability healing off his big HP bar out-sustains a Frenzied Maul re-cast in any extended fight.","late":"You own the late 1v1 hard — this is exactly what Gwen is built for. Every health item Volibear buys only feeds Thousand Cuts and Snip Snip!'s %-max-HP plus true-damage core, and the longer the fight runs the more your mist plus per-ability healing grind him down. Just respect his R: he can disable your turret and dive in with the shield, so take fights parked in your own mist, never under a contested turret where his all-in CC can pin you outside it.","whys":["No mist yet and his W bite heals and slows the trade — but you're equally clunky at level 1 with just a short cone Q, so neither side commits; farm the tip of Snip Snip!.","He has his Q-dash but you've got Skip 'n Slash to reposition — it's still soft and two-way, so last-hit and dodge his bite range rather than force it.","Q+E lets you poke with the %-max-HP cone and refund Skip 'n Slash off the champ hit, out-trading him before his W bite heal comes back up.","Pre-6 Thundering Smash into a Sky Splitter slow can pin and maul you with no Hallowed Mist to escape, but you can sidestep the engage and punish the whiff — a real skill test either way.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist blanks his all-in: Thundering Smash stuns the first enemy he attacks, and untargetable in the fog there is nobody for him to attack.","Riftmaker turns long mist duels in your favor — your per-ability healing out-sustains his W bite heal and Snip Snip!'s true-damage core shreds his tank items.","Every health item he buys only feeds your %-max-HP autos and Thousand Cuts — you out-duel a tanky Voli all game inside the mist; just dodge his R turret-dive."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"warwick","win":["Warwick","Skill","Skill","Warwick","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Warwick's biggest pre-6 window: Q heals on every drain and W move speed lets him run you down before you have Hallowed Mist or E to break the chase."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Pre-drop Hallowed Mist BEFORE he commits R — Infinite Duress is a directional leap onto the first champion it hits, so sidestep the line from inside the fog and the all-in whiffs."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's plus grievous wounds: your %-max-HP Snip Snip! and anti-heal out-grind his Q drain and low-HP passive in an extended mist fight."},{"when":"Late","text":"Even scaling: %-max-HP autos and your true-damage center snip shred his bruiser stack faster than a tank's, but a landed R from fog you mistimed still picks you."}],"wants":{"you":["Pre-place Hallowed Mist as he steps in so his point-blank R suppress can't land, then snip him while he's stuck outside the fog","Stack grievous wounds early so his passive low-HP healing and Q drain stop out-sustaining your %-HP snips","Use E's attack-speed and on-hit range to chunk his bruiser HP with %-max-HP Snip Snip! in drawn-out trades"],"foe":["Catch you below his passive HP threshold so his enhanced low-HP healing flips the drain fight","Catch you under 50% so Blood Hunt's speed closes the gap and lengthens his R leap","Out-sustain your levels 1-3 pokes with Q drain-heal while you have no mist or E to trade safely"]},"early":"Warwick out-sustains you levels 1-3 — his Q heals on every hit and his passive heals harder the lower a target sits, so a naive poke war just feeds his bar. Don't trade autos for free; farm with the tip of Snip Snip! and last-hit at range. You have no mist, no E mobility and no all-in yet, so your only job is to stay above his passive low-HP threshold where his healing spikes. Respect that his W move speed lets him close faster than most melees before you have any escape.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his window — Q heal plus Blood Hunt move speed runs you down with no Hallowed Mist yet to break it, so hold near tower. Everything flips at 6, but play it right: Infinite Duress is a directional leap that suppresses the first champion it collides with, and its distance scales with his bonus move speed, so staying above 50% health keeps Blood Hunt off you and the leap short. Pre-drop mist before he commits and sidestep the line — then snip him while he whiffs. From there you trade evenly, because your healing-on-damage answers his healing-on-drain.","late":"This stays a true coinflip into the late game. Your %-max-HP Snip Snip! and true-damage center snip chew through his bruiser HP faster than a tank's, and grievous wounds chokes both his Q drain and his passive sustain, so straight duels are yours to win. The danger is never the 1v1 damage — it's his R: he only needs one clean point-blank suppress while your mist is down or you've stepped out of fog to lock you and burst you. Keep mist ready for every committed all-in, hold anti-heal up, and never face-check his W roams.","whys":["Warwick's Q heals on every hit and his passive heals harder as you drop — at level 1 with no mist and no E you simply lose the sustain war.","You pick up a tool but still no mist; he can W-close and Q-heal through your pokes, so it's a wash where you just farm safely.","Q plus E lets you poke-and-reset, but his drain sustain answers your chip — neither side wins the trade cleanly yet.","His worst window for you: Q heal plus W move speed runs you down and you still have no untargetability or dash to break the chase.","Infinite Duress is a directional leap onto the first champion it collides with — sidestep the line and the whole all-in whiffs.","Riftmaker/Nashor's plus grievous wounds let your %-HP snips out-grind his Q drain, and anti-heal chokes his low-HP passive — your item spike.","Your %-HP and true damage shred his bruiser HP and anti-heal chokes his drain, but one clean R out of fog ends you — a coinflip."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"wukong","win":["Wukong","Wukong","Skill","Wukong","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Wukong out-stats you early: his empowered Q (Crushing Blow) shreds your armor on the next auto and his base damage wins the short trade before you have W mist or your E dash. Respect his level-2 E gap-close."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips the all-in: drop W as his R spin (Cyclone) winds up so you go untargetable in the fog, his knockup whiffs, and your passive out-sustains his burst."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online and your %-max-HP Snip Snip! shreds the armor he stacks; E's cooldown refund lets you stick on the real Wukong while mist denies his clone-burst combo."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"You out-scale him outright: the more armor he buys, the harder your magic %-HP Q hits and the more your passive heals — anti-heal plus the true-damage center snip closes the duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive levels 1-4 last-hitting at Q-tip range, then hit 6 and bait his R spin into your Hallowed Mist so the knockup whiffs and you go untargetable in the fog","Reach your first AP item where %-max-HP Snip Snip! ignores his stacked armor and the true-damage center snip out-trades his shred","Use E's attack-speed dash and champ-hit cooldown refund to stick on the REAL Wukong through his clone, chasing him down rather than the decoy"],"foe":["Win levels 1-3 with his empowered Q armor-shred and base damage before your mist and E dash come online","Land R spin (Cyclone) knockup to pin you OUTSIDE Hallowed Mist range so you can't go untargetable","Pop W to drop a clone and turn invisible, baiting your Q/E onto the decoy, then re-engage once his cooldowns reset"]},"early":"Wukong owns the first three levels — his empowered Q (Crushing Blow) shreds your armor and his base autos out-stat you while you have no mist and no E dash to trade back safely. Don't walk up to throw a slow cone Q at him; last-hit at the Q-tip and eat a little chip rather than feeding his level-2 E gap-close. His threat is the all-in burst, not sustained poke, so deny the trade window and farm — every minute you survive tilts the lane toward your scaling.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — you're a short-range melee with no untargetability against his shred-and-dash, so keep farming and stay outside his E commit range. Everything flips at 6: drop Hallowed Mist the instant his R spin winds up so the knockup whiffs and you go untargetable in the fog, slow him with Needlework, and out-heal his burst with your passive. Force the all-in inside your mist, never the open lane — and when he pops W, watch for the clone and chase the real Wukong with your E, not the decoy.","late":"This is where you take over for good. Wukong stacks armor to survive, which is exactly what your magic %-max-HP Snip Snip! and true-damage center snip want — the tankier he builds, the harder your Q lands and the more your passive heals off him. Drop Riftmaker and your mist makes his clone-burst combo whiff while you grind him down; bring anti-heal and his R spin can't out-trade you. He stays item-dependent and you simply out-scale — close every fight standing inside your fog.","whys":["Wukong's empowered Q armor-shred and base autos out-stat your slow cone Q at level 1 — no mist, no E dash, so don't contest the trade.","His level-2 E gap-close lets him punish you while you're still soft with one ability up — farm, don't fight.","By 3 you have Q+E to poke-and-reset, but his shred-and-dash still edges the raw trade — it's close, so play for farm and your 6 spike.","Levels 4-5 are your worst window pre-mist tempo — a short-range melee with no untargetability against his E dash-in and Q shred.","At 6 Hallowed Mist blanks him: Nimbus Strike dashes to a targeted enemy, so from outside the fog he has no opener, and Needlework plus passive healing flip the all-in.","Riftmaker online: %-max-HP Snip Snip! ignores the armor he stacks and mist untargetability blanks his clone-burst combo while E keeps you on the real him.","You out-scale him outright — the more armor he buys the harder your magic %-HP Q hits, and anti-heal plus the true-damage center snip finish him."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"yasuo","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Yasuo","Gwen","Gwen","Yasuo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"His Wind Wall (W) blocks projectiles, so it eats Needlework — but Snip Snip! is a cone, not a projectile, and cuts straight through. Walk up, drop the cone at melee, and chase the true-damage centre snip."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your worst window: still no Hallowed Mist to go untargetable, and a flow-shielded Yasuo stacking E off the wave out-skirmishes you in a straight melee scrap, so concede CS and farm safely to 6."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework and Hallowed Mist both come online at once: bait his Q3 or EQ knockup, drop W the instant it lands so his crit auto and R whiff on an untargetable Gwen, then snip him down inside the fog while your passive heals it back."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Crit Yasuo with Infinity Edge and a zeal item out-duels you, and a single R off your dash-in flips the fight the mist can't fully cover, so take plates on your first-item spike and sidelane rather than 1v1 him."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his Q3 or EQ knockup, then drop W as the CC lands so his crit auto and R hit an untargetable Gwen","Fight on top of Hallowed Mist and grind his bar with %-max-HP Snip Snip plus the heal off every ability you land","Use E's cooldown-refund-on-champion-hit to stay glued to him through his minion dashes and keep resetting the dash"],"foe":["Predrop Wind Wall to eat your Needlework volleys before they ever reach him","Stack flow shield and E off the minion wave to out-skirmish you while your W is on cooldown","Scale to crit items and save R for the moment you dash in, since he needs you airborne to land it"]},"early":"Level 1-3 is genuinely even and it's all about respecting Wind Wall. Never throw an R volley into it — the wall blocks projectiles for four seconds and eats every needle — but Snip Snip! is a cone, not a projectile, so it cuts through. I trade by walking up and dropping the Q cone right on top of him at melee, and I lean on the true-damage center snip to chunk him. I have no mist and no E reset value yet, so I just contest CS and avoid eating a full E-dash into a two-stack Steel Tempest knockup while his flow shield is up.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are my worst window: I still have no Hallowed Mist to go untargetable, and a flow-shielded Yasuo stacking E off the wave genuinely out-skirmishes me in a straight melee scrap, so I farm and wait for 6. The moment Needlework and a full Q-W-E kit come online the lane flips: I bait his Q3 or EQ knockup, drop W as the CC lands so his crit follow-up and R both whiff on an untargetable me, then snip him down inside the fog while my passive heals it back. From 6 I win or trade evenly on most committed all-ins.","late":"This is where the EVEN lane tilts back to him. Crit Yasuo with Infinity Edge and a zeal item out-duels me: his sustained crit DPS, plus a single R the moment I dash in, flips extended fights the mist can't fully cover since R only needs me airborne once. My %-HP Q still hurts if he goes bruiser, but a full-crit build just out-scales me, so I want to cash my first-item spike for plates and tempo, then group or sidelane rather than 1v1 him into his third item.","whys":["No mist and no E reset yet, but Wind Wall is the real story: it blocks Needlework, not the Snip Snip! cone, so trade up close and never feed it an R volley.","Both of us are soft here; I farm with Q snips and dodge his E-dash into Q3 knockup rather than commit, since I have no untargetability to bail me out.","Q+E lets me poke and reset off him, but a flow-shielded Yasuo still trades evenly up close, so I keep it a CS lane and respect his minion-dash gap-close.","My worst window: no Hallowed Mist to go untargetable and his E-stack flow-shield skirmish beats me in raw melee, so I concede CS and wait for Needlework.","Hallowed Mist plus R online flips it: I bait his knockup, go untargetable as his crit and R try to land, and snip him down inside the fog while my passive sustains me.","My Riftmaker or Nashor's spike with %-HP Snip and the mist wins extended duels at 6, so I force the all-in and shove for plates now.","Full-crit Yasuo with Infinity Edge out-scales me, and one R off my dash-in flips the fight, so I close before his third item or let my team peel him."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"yone","win":["Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Yone"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Q+E online — when he Q-dashes in to cleave, snip him with the true-damage center snip and E out before W spins, your %-HP magic shreds his crit build's zero MR."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"When he commits Q3 knockup or R dash-through, drop Hallowed Mist on yourself so his follow-up whiffs into the fog, then R-slow him as he E-recalls to his body."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online — your mist armor/MR plus ability healing out-grinds his W shield in any extended duel he can't disengage from."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yone's biggest threat: at 3+ items he kites with W move speed and R-engages, becoming a slippery crit carry who out-scales you — close the game before then."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his Q3 knockup or R dash into your Hallowed Mist so you go untargetable and his combo whiffs, then snip him out of the animation","Reach level 6 and grind extended fights where your mist resists and ability healing beat his one-shot W shield","Snowball mid before his 3-item crit spike reclaims the scaling crown and his W kiting outruns your E"],"foe":["Land his third-Q knockup to chain R and burst you before your Hallowed Mist drops","Soul Unbound (E) out, trade, then recall to his body to reset a losing exchange and dodge your slow","Avoid your mist all-ins, farm even off W waveclear, and out-scale you into the very late game"]},"early":"Yone is genuinely even with you at levels 1-2, so don't try to prove anything before you have tools — his Q poke and dash out-trade your clunky cone if you facecheck. By level 3 you have Q+E: when he Q-dashes in to cleave, snip him with the true-damage center and E away before his W shield-cleave spins up. Your %-max-HP magic shreds him because he builds crit and lethality with almost no MR, so even short trades favor you once your kit is online.","mid":"This is where you take over. The instant he commits — Q3 knockup or R dash-through — drop Hallowed Mist on yourself so you go untargetable to him standing outside it and his follow-up whiffs, then snip him while he's locked in the animation. At 6 your R needles slow him so his E (Soul Unbound) recall to his body can't cleanly disengage, and your mist resists plus ability healing eat his W shield in any extended brawl. Force every all-in here on his Q-and-R cooldowns; pre-Riftmaker Yone simply can't out-grind your mist.","late":"You own the straight duel through your first two items, but Yone is a true hypercarry — at 3+ items he kites with W move speed, R-engages into your backline, and out-scales even you. Your win condition is to snowball the mid-game so hard his late never matters: take plates, roam, and end before he comes online. If it goes long, respect his R engage and never get caught alone without mist up — that's the one window where his burst-then-cleave actually kills you.","whys":["You're both even at level 1 — he has Q-dash poke but no W shield-cleave yet, so just farm and don't facecheck his snip range.","Still soft for both of you; his Q out-poke edges a Gwen with no mist up, so last-hit and wait for your kit.","Q+E online — you snip him as he Q-dashes in and E out before his W cleave, and your %-HP magic ignores his crit-build MR.","You out-trade a pre-item Yone: bait his Q3 knockup, sidestep or eat it, then punish his cooldowns with snips.","Mist his all-in: drop Hallowed Mist as Q3 or R lands so you go untargetable, then R-slow him through his E recall.","Riftmaker plus ability healing means extended fights are yours — your mist resists out-grind his one-shot W shield.","He out-scales hard: 3-item Yone kites with W and R-engages your team — play safe and let your team peel."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"yorick","win":["Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Level 1 he has no ghoul graves and no W-cage, so contest the first wave and Snip him whenever he walks up to last-hit with Last Rites."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist lets you bait his Dark Procession all-in and out-sustain his Maiden + ghoul swarm once your passive healing comes online."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker or Nashor's Tooth turns your %-max-HP Snip into a duel-winner that out-trades his bruiser HP bar even through the ghoul swarm."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Maiden is permanent and he has 2+ items he ignores the 1v1 and splitpushes — his W-cage plus Maiden zone you off the side wave, so close before then."}],"wants":{"you":["Drop Hallowed Mist the instant his Dark Procession ring lands so the cage traps you next to an untargetable Gwen while you keep Snipping","Snip HIM, not his ghouls — your %-max-HP Q ignores the swarm and shreds his bruiser HP bar directly","Snowball the lane and take towers before his permanent Maiden and splitpush make the 1v1 irrelevant"],"foe":["Land Dark Procession (W) to wall you onto the ghoul army, then Mourning Mist (E) to slow-mark you so every ghoul pounces","Keep Maiden alive and raise ghouls off graves so every trade is him plus four units versus you","Survive to 2+ items and take the lane to the side, where his cage + Maiden win the splitpush you can't"]},"early":"Yorick is a slow starter and so are you, but level 1 he has no ghoul graves and no Dark Procession cage, so you can step up and Snip him whenever he comes to last-hit. From level 2 don't waste your Q on his ghouls — your %-max-HP Snip ignores them and chunks HIS bar, so always aim the center snip through the swarm at Yorick himself. Respect his Mourning Mist (E): it cuts your armour, slows, and marks you so every summon sprints at the mark. And the Dark Procession (W) wall is destructible — if it cages you onto the ghoul pile, break a segment out rather than eating the whole army.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you're still a melee against a juggernaut who can wall you in, so farm and only trade when his ghouls are dead and Maiden is off the field. At 6 the lane flips: drop Hallowed Mist the instant his Dark Procession ring lands so you're untargetable inside the trap while Needlework slows him and your passive heals off his HP, and his ghouls pounce on a mist you've already left. Your %-max-HP Q out-trades his bruiser bar the longer the fight runs, so bait the cage all-in, mist it, and Snip him down.","late":"Your first item (Riftmaker or Nashor's Tooth) is the window where your Snip out-duels him even through the swarm — force every all-in here and take his tower. But be honest about the clock: once Maiden is permanent and he's 2+ items, Yorick stops 1v1ing you and goes side-lane, where his Dark Procession cage plus Maiden zone you off the wave and out-push you. You can't win that splitpush, so snowball the early-to-mid lead into objectives and end before his scaling takes the map.","whys":["You're both weak level 1, but he has no ghouls or Dark Procession cage yet — contest the first wave and Snip him on every last-hit step-up.","By level 2 your Q ignores his ghoul swarm and hits his HP bar directly, so you out-poke a Yorick who can't yet wall you in.","Snip-and-disengage with Skip 'n Slash's E-reset lets you trade before his ghoul economy comes online — aim at him, not the swarm.","Still pre-mist but he's pre-Maiden — the Dark Procession wall is destructible, so break a segment, and punish him when his ghouls are dead.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist flips it: mist his W-cage all-in so the ghouls whiff, slow him with R, and out-sustain via passive healing.","Riftmaker/Nashor's makes your %-max-HP Snip out-duel him even through ghouls — force the all-in and take his plates now.","He out-scales you: permanent Maiden plus 2+ items lets him ignore the 1v1 and splitpush with W-cage zoning, so end before this."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"zac","win":["Zac","Zac","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Zac's earliest window: his Stretching Strikes grab and chunky base stats let him body you before you have Skip 'n Slash, so respect his step-up and don't get pulled."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework plus Hallowed Mist online — drop W on the spot his Slingshot lands so the engage finds nothing to target, then fan needles to slow and snip his huge HP bar down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's: your %-max-HP Snip Snip! plus its true-damage center snip melt his blob HP faster than his passive pickups can refund it."},{"when":"Late","text":"His only threat is landing Slingshot onto your carries in a teamfight — in the straight 1v1 you shred him harder the more tank he stacks."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his Slingshot or grab into Hallowed Mist so you go untargetable from outside the fog while you keep snipping his HP bar","Stack %-max-HP Thousand Cuts autos and Snip Snip! on his blob HP, healing more off every hit the bigger he builds","Buy anti-heal (Oblivion line) so his passive blob pickups can't refund the percent-HP shred you stack on him"],"foe":["Land a long Slingshot engage or Q grab when your Skip 'n Slash is down to chunk you before you reach mist range","Pin you to the wall with Q and Unstable Matter, then chunk your bar while he scoops passive blobs to sustain","Scale into teamfights where his Slingshot flanks your backline instead of soloing you 1v1"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are the only soft spot, and they belong to Zac. His Stretching Strikes grab and chunky base stats let him win a raw step-up before you have Skip 'n Slash for mobility, so don't throw a clunky cone Snip Snip! into his face and eat a grab-and-Unstable-Matter return. Last-hit at the tip of the cone and farm — the moment you hit 3 with Q and a dash to poke-and-reset, you start chipping his HP without giving him anything back, because his passive blob pickups can't out-sustain percent-max-HP magic damage.","mid":"This is where you take over. Every point of armor and HP Zac builds makes your %-max-HP Snip Snip! and Thousand Cuts autos hit harder and heal you more off every strike, so trade into him freely. At 6 the lane flips hard: when he commits Slingshot, drop Hallowed Mist on the landing spot — he can't target you from outside the fog while you keep snipping and slow him with Needlework. Bait the engage, mist, then walk out the back of his own all-in and full-combo his blob.","late":"You out-scale him in the straight 1v1 all game — the tankier he gets, the faster your true center snip and %-max-HP Q delete him, and anti-heal shuts off the blob pickups he leans on. His one real win is the map: a long-range Slingshot flanking your backline in a teamfight. Don't get isolated and slung into his team — group with vision and let your percent-HP shred carry the fight once you're in it.","whys":["Zac's Stretching Strikes grab and bigger base stats out-stat you at 1 before you have Skip 'n Slash mobility.","He still owns the raw trade early — you have no dash reset yet and no untargetability, so farm rather than fight.","With Q and a dash to poke-and-reset you start grinding his HP, and his passive blob pickups can't sustain through percent-max-HP magic damage.","Every bit of armor and HP he builds feeds your %-max-HP Q and heals you more via Thousand Cuts — you out-trade him here.","Needlework plus Hallowed Mist lets you mist his Slingshot all-in, go untargetable, and snip-and-slow him to death.","Riftmaker/Nashor's makes your %-HP Q and true center snip melt his tank HP faster than his blob pickups can refund it.","The tankier he builds the harder you shred him 1v1 — his only edge is a teamfight flank Slingshot, not the solo lane."]},
  {"a":"gwen","b":"ziggs","win":["Ziggs","Ziggs","Skill","Ziggs","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Ziggs pelts you with Bouncing Bomb (Q) from outside your reach while your Q is a clunky short cone — eat the poke, last-hit, and only step up for a CS you can take cleanly inside your W cloud."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Needlework (R) plus your full Q-W-E kit lets you commit: E onto him for the cooldown refund, drop Hallowed Mist (W) so he can't target you from outside it, and grind him with %-max-HP Snip Snip! while your abilities heal you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker/Nashor's online — once you E onto an immobile mage and stand in your Mist, percent-HP Q plus ability healing out-sustains his poke; he has no dash to peel you and Satchel (W) only buys one knockback."},{"when":"Late","text":"Ziggs' Q-W-E-R artillery clears your engage wave and pokes you off plates from max range — if he stacks Mejai's/Liandry's and you can't gap-close, you never touch him; force the all-in while Satchel is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive the Bouncing Bomb (Q) poke, then E-gapclose onto him and fight inside Hallowed Mist (W) so he can't target you while your %-HP Snip Snip! grinds him down","Bait his Satchel Charge (W) and Minefield (E) on cooldown, then close the gap once his only knockback and his slow zone are both spent","Use E's cooldown refund on champion hit to stick to an immobile mage who has no dash — chain autos so Thousand Cuts and your ability healing out-trade his poke"],"foe":["Land Bouncing Bomb (Q) from max range to chip you below all-in threshold and deny you any window to step up for CS","Save Satchel Charge (W) to knock you off the instant you E in, then kite back behind his Minefield (E) slow","Stack Mejai's/Liandry's and siege from artillery range so your melee engage only clears the wave while he pokes you off plates"]},"early":"Ziggs owns levels 1-3 — his Bouncing Bomb (Q) outranges everything you have, and as a melee with a short, clunky cone Q you can't trade back through it. You do have Hallowed Mist (W) from level 1, but standing in a fog cloud doesn't stop a bomb that's already in the air, so it only saves you when you can fully duck behind it for a CS. Don't try to trade; last-hit at max range, accept the chip, and bank on the fact that he burns mana fast spamming Q and has zero way to stop you once you finally get on top of him.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay rough — you're a melee against an artillery mage who pokes you off the wave and has Satchel Charge (W) to knock you back the instant you commit. At 6 the lane swings your way: Needlework (R) plus your full kit means once he wastes Satchel or misfires Minefield (E), you E in for the cooldown refund, plant Hallowed Mist (W) so he can't target you from outside it, and grind him with percent-max-HP Snip Snip! while your abilities heal you. He only has one knockback and no dash, so every spent cooldown is your opening.","late":"This is the knife's edge. Once you hit Riftmaker and have E to gap-close, an immobile mage caught inside your Mist is dead — your %-HP Snip Snip! plus ability healing out-sustains his poke faster than he can peel, and his lone Satchel knockback buys him one escape, not a reset. But if you let him free-stack Mejai's or Liandry's and siege uncontested, his Q-W-E-R wall of artillery clears your engage wave and pokes you off every plate before you reach him. Force the all-in the moment his Satchel is down; if you can't close, the lane slips away.","whys":["Bouncing Bomb (Q) outranges your entire kit and your Q is a short cone — you can only eat poke and farm at max range while he chips you for free.","Still just a melee with no gap-closer leveled — he zones you off the wave with Q bounces and Minefield (E) chip while you have no way to answer the range.","You finally have E to step up and reset on it, but his Satchel knockback and long Q range keep the trade even — neither of you wins clean yet.","Ziggs keeps poking from artillery range and Satchel Charge (W) punishes any over-commit — as a melee with no untargetability against untargeted poke, you stay on the back foot.","Needlework plus your full kit flips it at 6 — punish a spent Satchel by E-ing in, planting Mist so he can't target you, and grinding %-HP Snip Snip!.","Riftmaker online: E onto an immobile mage inside your Mist and percent-HP Snip Snip! plus ability healing eats him — he has no dash to peel and Satchel only buys one knockback.","Late game is positional — you delete him the instant you reach him, but his stacked Liandry's/Mejai's artillery pokes you off plates and clears your engage if you can't close the gap."]}
