window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"gwen","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Zaahen","Skill","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 4-5","text":"Aureate Rush into a Dreaded Return pull, before your item — give ground."},{"when":"Level 6","text":"Hallowed Mist answers Grim Deliverance at 600 — the all-in defuses."},{"when":"First AP item","text":"True damage ignores his healing — trades flip permanently your way."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Mist plus dashes out-duel him — but Determination revives him once."}],"wants":{"you":["Survival through 4-5 without bleeding CS","Mist on his ult commits","First item, then endless trades"],"foe":["A walk-down before your item","Fights forced outside your mist","A finish before your true damage scales"]},"early":"Play the opening as a polite farm-off — levels 1-3 nobody has an edge, so manage your mana and E cooldown and trade only when it is clean. The stretch to genuinely fear is 4-5: he can walk you down before your first AP item exists, so give ground, hug your tower, and lose nothing but pride. Reaching 6 healthy is a won early game here.","mid":"At 6 Hallowed Mist answers his ult commit and the danger deflates. Then first item is the hinge of the whole matchup: Q true damage does not care about his healing, so every extended trade now shreds him. Start snipping — trade on your Q stacks, mist his engage, and chunk him off waves. Expect desperation plays as his window closes, and punish them.","late":"Two items on, you out-duel his all-in flat: mist blanks the commit, your dashes re-space, and true-damage shred melts him along with any tank stats he buys. Take the side lane, force him to answer you, and win either the duel or the map — his single-target kit cannot stop both. In teamfights, saw through the frontline he is supposed to anchor.","whys":["Level 1 is even — both of you are just farming before the kits come online.","Level 2 stays even with no clear kit edge on either side.","Level 3 remains a skill check played around your mana and E cooldown — do not spam yourself dry.","Levels 4-5 are Zaahen's: Aureate Rush into a Dreaded Return pull walks you down before your item — give ground.","Level 6 is even — Hallowed Mist answers Grim Deliverance at 600, blanking the all-in he wants.","First item is Gwen: your true-damage shred out-trades his sustain, because healing does not argue with true damage.","2+ items stays yours — mist and your mobility out-duel his all-in every single time."]});
