window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"gwen","b":"masteryi","win":["Gwen","Gwen","Skill","Master Yi","Master Yi","Master Yi","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 1-2","text":"Ranged snips bully his weak autos — take an early CS lead."},{"when":"Levels 4-6","text":"Highlander (85s) is slow-immune — Needlework cannot kite it. Farm safe."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Mist untargetability plus on-hit scaling flip the duel back to you for good."}],"wants":{"you":["A banked level 1-2 poke lead","Survival through his mid-game windows","Two items — you outscale him"],"foe":["Punished mana-dry windows","Slow-immune Highlander run-downs","A finish before your spike"]},"early":"Take your free chapter first: levels 1-2 your ranged snips beat his weak autos, so chip him at every last-hit and bank CS. From 3 his Alpha Strike trades start out-damaging you, and by 4-5 he clearly wins — your mana runs dry and his DPS does not. Shift into farm-only mode early rather than donating the kill that fuels his snowball.","mid":"Levels 6 through first item are the survival chapter — Highlander is a flat 85s, it makes him immune to slows so Needlework cannot kite him, and every takedown extends it. Farm with Q from max range, hold W strictly for his commit, and get Grievous up before he channels Meditate. Every minion here is a brick in the wall he must climb.","late":"At two items the duel is permanently yours: Hallowed Mist blanks his all-in from outside, and your on-hit shred out-DPSes him in the fight he starts. Do not dump damage into Alpha Strike — he is untargetable for it, and his autos drag that 20-second cooldown down. Bait the engage into mist, saw him down, and mist yourself in teamfights to shred whoever dives.","whys":["Level 1 is Gwen — Snip Snip! poke edges out his weak early autos.","Level 2 stays yours: ranged Q keeps controlling the wave before he can close the distance.","Level 3 evens out — Alpha Strike and his autos start out-damaging your snips, so the free poke ends.","Levels 4-5 are Yi's: Wuju Style puts TRUE damage on his autos, so armour will not save your trades.","Level 6 is his — Highlander is slow-immune, so Needlework cannot kite the run-down.","First item stays Yi: Meditate (W) heals through your chip unless Grievous is already on him.","2+ items is Gwen — Hallowed Mist untargetability blanks his all-in and your on-hit scaling out-duels him late."]});
